window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0001", [{"word":"abandon","ipa_uk":"/əˈbændən/","ipa_us":"/əˈbændən/","definition_zh":"放弃；抛弃；遗弃；沉溺","definition_en":"to give something up completely, leave someone or something behind, or give oneself over to a feeling","core_image":"松开的掌心：把原本握住的控制权放开","scene":"地震过后，开裂的房子里已经不能再住人。 After the earthquake, the residents had to abandon their cracked houses and leave with only first-aid kits and flashlights.","sceneCN":"这里 abandon 是「弃置、离开」（第 3 个义项：离开一个地方）；句意：地震后，居民不得不弃置开裂的房子，只带上急救包和手电筒离开。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"放弃；抛弃；遗弃；离弃"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"放任；放纵（多用于文学语境）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"abandon a plan","zh":"放弃一项计划"},{"phrase":"abandon ship","zh":"弃船（紧急离船）"},{"phrase":"abandon hope","zh":"放弃希望"},{"phrase":"abandon oneself to","zh":"沉溺于；纵情于"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"abandons"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"abandoned"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"abandoned"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"abandoning"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"abandoned","pos":"adj.","zh":"被遗弃的；废弃的"},{"word":"abandonment","pos":"n.","zh":"遗弃；放弃"},{"word":"abandoner","pos":"n.","zh":"遗弃者；放弃者"},{"word":"abandonware","pos":"n.","zh":"弃置软件（已停止维护但仍被使用的软件）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Surrender control: give something up","titleCN":"交出控制权：放弃某事","definition":"to give up control over something, especially because you can no longer keep it","definitionCN":"放弃对某事的控制，尤指已无力维持时","example":"They abandoned the plan after the first failure.","exampleCN":"第一次失败后，他们放弃了这个计划。","why":"The Old French phrase was à bandon, 'at will, at discretion'. To put something at someone else's will is to stop holding it yourself, so the word starts from release of control.","whyCN":"古法语短语是 à bandon，意为“随人处置”。把某物交给别人的意志，就是自己不再握住它，因此这个词的起点是“放开控制权”。"},{"no":"02","title":"Leave a person behind","titleCN":"抛下某人：不再负责","definition":"to leave someone you are responsible for, with no intention of returning","definitionCN":"抛弃自己有责任照顾的人，且不打算回来","example":"He abandoned his family and moved abroad.","exampleCN":"他抛下家人，搬到了国外。","why":"The release is now applied to a duty rather than an object. The person let go is no longer covered by your responsibility, so abandonment becomes desertion.","whyCN":"这里放开的不是物件，而是一份责任。被放开的人不再处于你的责任范围，于是“放弃”变成了“抛弃”。"},{"no":"03","title":"Leave a place: let it stand empty","titleCN":"弃置某地：任其空置","definition":"to leave a place permanently or for a long time, especially because it is unsafe","definitionCN":"永久或长期离开某地，尤因该地不安全","example":"The villagers abandoned their homes before the flood.","exampleCN":"洪水来临前，村民们弃置了家园。","why":"A place is something you hold by occupying it. Once you leave and do not return, the place is released just like an object dropped from the hand.","whyCN":"你通过“占据”来握有一个地方。一旦离开且不再回来，这个地方就像从手中掉落的物件一样被放开。"},{"no":"04","title":"Give up a claim or right","titleCN":"放弃权利要求","definition":"to stop claiming, defending, or pursuing a right or legal case","definitionCN":"停止主张、维护或追究某项权利或案件","example":"She abandoned her claim to the inheritance.","exampleCN":"她放弃了继承权。","why":"A claim is a grip on something you believe belongs to you. Abandoning it is voluntarily opening that grip before the matter is settled.","whyCN":"权利要求是你对自认为属于自己之物的“抓握”。放弃它，就是在事情落定之前主动松开这只手。"},{"no":"05","title":"Abandon oneself to a feeling","titleCN":"沉溺于某种情绪","definition":"in the phrase abandon oneself to, to let a feeling control you completely","definitionCN":"用于 abandon oneself to，表示完全任由某种情绪支配自己","example":"He abandoned himself to grief after the loss.","exampleCN":"失去之后，他沉溺于悲痛之中。","why":"The reflexive form comes from Old French 'to devote oneself'. Control is handed over not to another person but to a feeling, so the self stops being the one who holds.","whyCN":"反身形式来自古法语“把自己奉献出去”。控制权不是交给别人，而是交给一种情绪，于是“自我”不再是握住一切的那一方。"},{"no":"06","title":"Abandon ship: leave a vessel in danger","titleCN":"弃船：危险时离开船只","definition":"to leave a ship that is sinking or in danger, as a fixed emergency order","definitionCN":"在船只下沉或遇险时离船，是固定的紧急用语","example":"The captain ordered the crew to abandon ship.","exampleCN":"船长命令船员弃船。","why":"A ship is the most concrete thing a crew holds. When the vessel itself can no longer be kept, the only possible release is to leave it to the sea.","whyCN":"船是船员握有的最具体的东西。当船本身已无法保全时，唯一能做的放手就是把它交给大海。"},{"no":"07","title":"With abandon: free of restraint","titleCN":"放任：毫无拘束","definition":"in the phrase with abandon, in a free, eager way that shows no restraint or worry about appearances","definitionCN":"用于短语 with abandon，表示毫无拘束、尽情而为，不在意他人眼光","example":"The children ran into the waves with abandon.","exampleCN":"孩子们毫无拘束地跑进海浪里。","why":"The noun keeps the gesture of the verb but turns it inward: control is released not to another person but to one's own impulse, so the release becomes a manner of acting.","whyCN":"名词保留了动词的“松开”动作，却把它转向内部：控制权不是交给别人，而是交给自己的冲动，于是“松开”成了一种行事方式。"},{"no":"08","title":"Industry: seal a well or mine for good","titleCN":"工业：永久封弃矿井","definition":"to stop working a well, mine, or drilling site and close it permanently, usually with a legal record","definitionCN":"停止使用油井、矿井或钻井点并永久封闭，通常留下法律记录","example":"The operator abandoned the well after the pressure fell.","exampleCN":"压力下降后，作业方封弃了这口井。","why":"This is the technical form of leaving a place empty: the site stays underground, but nobody holds it any more, so the departure has to be sealed and recorded.","whyCN":"这是“让某地空置”的技术版本：场地仍在地下，却不再有人持有它，因此离开必须封死并登记。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Abandon is a French phrase that hardened into an English verb. Dates are approximate, and the deepest Germanic root is not fully certain.","cn":"abandon 是一个凝固成英语动词的法语短语。年代为大致估计；最底层的日耳曼词根并不完全确定。"},"items":[{"era":"LATE 14C.","en":"First recorded in late 14c. as a verb meaning 'to give up completely, surrender'. A mid-13c. adverbial use already meant 'under someone's control'.","cn":"动词义“彻底放弃、交出”最早记录于 14 世纪晚期；13 世纪中期的副词用法已表示“处于某人控制之下”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"From Old French abandonner (12c.) 'to surrender, release; give freely, permit', also used reflexively as 'to devote oneself'. The phrase à bandon meant 'at will, at discretion'.","cn":"来自古法语 abandonner（12 世纪），意为“交出、释放；随意给予、允许”，反身用法为“献身于”。短语 à bandon 意为“随意、听凭处置”。"},{"era":"LATIN / FRANKISH","en":"à bandon = à (from Latin ad 'to') + bandon 'power, jurisdiction', from Latin bannum 'proclamation'. Bannum itself was borrowed from Frankish, so this is a Germanic word that travelled through Latin and French.","cn":"à bandon = à（来自拉丁语 ad“向”）+ bandon“权力、管辖”，后者来自拉丁语 bannum“公告”。bannum 本身借自法兰克语，因此这是一个经由拉丁语和法语传播的日耳曼词。"},{"era":"PROTO-GERMANIC","en":"The Germanic source is reconstructed as Proto-Germanic *bannan- 'proclaim, summon, outlaw'. Its link to PIE *bha- 'to speak' is marked 'apparently' in standard references, so the deepest root is source uncertain.","cn":"其日耳曼来源被重构为原始日耳曼语 *bannan-“宣告、传唤、宣布不受法律保护”。它与原始印欧语 *bha-“说”的联系在通行资料中只标为“似乎”，故最深层词源来源不确定。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps the core sense 'leave behind / give up'. The reflexive sense 'devote oneself' survives in abandon oneself to. Ban, banish, bandit and contraband belong to the same 'proclamation / outlaw' complex.","cn":"现代英语保留“丢下／放弃”的核心义；反身义“献身于”保留在 abandon oneself to 中。ban、banish、bandit、contraband 都属于同一个“公告／宣告不受保护”的词义群。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The groups below separate spelling neighbours from words with a close meaning. Sound and form are checked first, then meaning.","cn":"下面两组把“拼写相近”和“意思接近”分开。先看读音与词形，再看词义。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"abundant","ipa":"/əˈbʌndənt/","tag":"spelling","definition":"plentiful; existing in large quantities. It shares the ab- beginning but has a different root (unda, 'wave').","definitionCN":"丰富的；大量的。它同样以 ab- 开头，但词根不同（unda“波浪”）。"},{"word":"abandonment","ipa":"/əˈbændənmənt/","tag":"derived form","definition":"the noun from abandon: the act of leaving or giving up. It is not a separate root word.","definitionCN":"abandon 派生的名词：遗弃或放弃的行为。它不是另一个词根词。"},{"word":"bandit","ipa":"/ˈbændɪt/","tag":"same root","definition":"an outlaw who lives by robbery. It comes from the same bannum 'proclamation / outlaw' complex, not from abandon itself.","definitionCN":"强盗；被宣布不受法律保护而四处劫掠的人。它出自同一个 bannum“公告／剥夺法律保护”词义群，而不是来自 abandon 本身。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"desert","ipa":"/dɪˈzɜːt/","tag":"person","definition":"to leave a person or place without help or support. It stresses the duty broken, while abandon stresses the act of letting go.","definitionCN":"遗弃某人或某地，不给帮助或支持。它强调被违背的责任，而 abandon 强调“放手”这个动作。"},{"word":"forsake","ipa":"/fəˈseɪk/","tag":"literary","definition":"to abandon someone or something you once cared for. It is literary and usually carries moral weight.","definitionCN":"抛弃曾经珍视的人或物。它是文学用语，通常带有道德分量。"},{"word":"relinquish","ipa":"/rɪˈlɪŋkwɪʃ/","tag":"right or control","definition":"to give up a right, position, or possession, often reluctantly. It is more formal and narrower than abandon.","definitionCN":"放弃权利、职位或占有物，常含不舍。它比 abandon 更正式，适用范围也更窄。"},{"word":"ditch","ipa":"/dɪtʃ/","tag":"informal","definition":"to get rid of or leave someone or something abruptly. It is informal and often sounds careless.","definitionCN":"突然甩掉或丢下某人某物。它偏口语，常带有草率、不负责任的意味。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real word parts, real phrases and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实短语和真实同族词，而不是编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"à bandon meant 'at will'. To abandon something is to put it at anyone's will but your own.","cn":"à bandon 意为“随意”。abandon 某物，就是把它交给别人的意志，而不再由自己掌控。"},{"en":"ban, banish, bandit and contraband come from the same 'proclamation / outlaw' complex: a banned thing is driven out, and an abandoned thing is left out.","cn":"ban、banish、bandit、contraband 都出自同一个“公告／剥夺保护”词义群：被 ban 的东西被赶出去，被 abandon 的东西被留在外面。"},{"en":"Abandon ship is a fixed emergency phrase: the ship is left to the sea and the crew leaves it.","cn":"abandon ship 是固定的紧急用语：把船交给大海，船员离开它。"},{"en":"Abandoned is the everyday adjective for empty buildings, deserted villages and neglected children.","cn":"abandoned 是日常形容词，用于空置的建筑、荒废的村庄和被忽视的孩子。"},{"en":"Abandon oneself to grief is the reflexive branch: you hand yourself over to the feeling.","cn":"“abandon oneself to grief”是反身分支：你把自己交给这种情绪。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture an open hand: first it holds a rope, then the fingers loosen and the rope falls. Abandon is the instant after release.","cn":"想象一只张开的手：先握着一根绳，然后手指松开，绳子落下。abandon 就是“松开之后”的那一瞬间。"},{"en":"The same release can be applied to a plan, a person, a place, a claim or a ship — anything you were responsible for holding.","cn":"同一种“松开”可以作用于计划、人、地点、权利要求或船只——任何你曾负责握住的东西。"},{"en":"In the reflexive branch the hand releases itself: control is handed to a feeling, and the self is no longer the one holding.","cn":"在反身分支里，手放开了自己：控制权交给一种情绪，自我不再是握住一切的那一方。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The search team abandoned the wrecked car and walked back to the road.","cn":"搜救队丢下撞毁的车，走回了公路。"},{"en":"Do not abandon your studies just because the first test was hard.","cn":"不要因为第一次测验很难就放弃学业。"},{"en":"The old factory stands abandoned beside the river.","cn":"那座老工厂废弃在河边。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿班蹲”——阿班把行李一放、蹲下不走了 → abandon 放弃、丢下","word":"abandon"},"root":"源自古法语短语 à bandon“随意处置”，核心是“交出控制权、放手不管”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of abandon, all built on one gesture: a hand releases what it was holding — control, a person, a place, a claim, the self, a ship, a well, or in the noun, restraint itself.","cn":"abandon 的八个义项都建立在同一个动作上：手松开原本握住的东西——控制权、人、地点、权利要求、自我、一艘船、一口井，或名词义中的“约束”本身。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a hand opens and lets go of what it was holding.","cn":"核心意象：一只手张开，放开原本握着的东西。"},"chain":["HOLD","RELEASE","NO LONGER RESPONSIBLE","LEAVE BEHIND","LEAVE EMPTY","GIVE ONESELF FREELY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 04","en":"CONTROL AND CLAIM: opening the hand on a plan or on a legal right is the same release of what was held.","cn":"控制与权利：放开一项计划或一项法律权利，都是松开原本握住的东西。"},{"senses":"02 · 03","en":"PEOPLE AND PLACES: a person is held by responsibility and a place by occupation, so leaving ends that hold.","cn":"人与地点：人靠责任被握住，地点靠占据被握住；离开就结束了这种握持。"},{"senses":"05","en":"SELF-SURRENDER: the reflexive form hands control to a feeling instead of to another person.","cn":"自我交付：反身形式把控制权交给情绪，而不是交给另一个人。"},{"senses":"06 · 08","en":"WHAT IS LEFT BEHIND: a ship and a well are both handed over to their fate, one to the sea and one to the ground, and both departures are recorded.","cn":"被留下的东西：船与井都被交给各自的命运，一个交给大海，一个交给地下，两种离开都要登记。"},{"senses":"07","en":"MANNER: the noun turns the same release into a style of acting, with no object actually given up.","cn":"行事方式：名词把同一种“松开”变成一种行为风格，并没有真正交出什么对象。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Abandon is not built from a living English prefix. Its parts are frozen inside the French phrase à bandon; English only adds ordinary suffixes to the finished verb.","cn":"abandon 并不是由活的英语前缀构成的。它的成分凝固在法语短语 à bandon 里；英语只是在成品动词后加普通后缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin bannum 'proclamation' is itself a Germanic borrowing, so there is no separate Latin cognate family to list. The Germanic branch survives in ban, banish, bandit and contraband.","cn":"拉丁语 bannum“公告”本身就是日耳曼借词，因此没有另一支可列的拉丁同族词。日耳曼这一支保留在 ban、banish、bandit、contraband 中。"},"items":[{"word":"abandonment","structure":"abandon + -ment (noun of action or state)","meaning":"the act of abandoning, or the state of being abandoned","meaningCN":"遗弃；放弃；被遗弃的状态（-ment 构成行为或状态名词）","example":"The abandonment of the project cost the company millions.","exampleCN":"放弃这个项目让公司损失了数百万。"},{"word":"abandoned","structure":"abandon + -ed (past participle used as adjective)","meaning":"left empty or neglected","meaningCN":"被遗弃的；废弃的（-ed 构成形容词）","example":"They found an abandoned house in the woods.","exampleCN":"他们在树林里发现了一栋废弃的房子。"},{"word":"abandoner","structure":"abandon + -er (person who does)","meaning":"a person who abandons someone or something","meaningCN":"遗弃者；放弃者（-er 表示做该动作的人）","example":"The abandoner of the dog was never found.","exampleCN":"遗弃那只狗的人一直没有找到。"},{"word":"abandonware","structure":"abandon + ware (goods, software)","meaning":"software that is no longer supported or sold by its owner","meaningCN":"弃置软件（原权利人不再支持或销售的软件）","example":"Old games often become abandonware.","exampleCN":"老游戏常常变成弃置软件。"},{"word":"abandonee","structure":"abandon + -ee (person to whom something is abandoned; maritime law)","meaning":"a person to whom abandoned property, especially a ship or cargo, is transferred","meaningCN":"受遗弃财产让与人；（海商法）接受被弃船货的一方（-ee 表示受事者）","example":"Under the law of salvage, the abandonee may claim the wreck.","exampleCN":"根据海难救助法，受遗弃财产让与人可以主张这艘沉船的所有权。"},{"word":"abandonor","structure":"abandon + -or (person who abandons; maritime law)","meaning":"a person who gives up a ship or cargo at sea","meaningCN":"遗弃人；（海商法）在海上弃船弃货的一方（-or 表示施事者）","example":"The abandonor surrendered the vessel to the insurer.","exampleCN":"遗弃人把这艘船让给了保险人。"},{"word":"abandoning","structure":"abandon + -ing (present participle and gerund)","meaning":"the act of giving something up, or the ongoing action of doing so","meaningCN":"放弃（动名词）；正在放弃（现在分词）","example":"Abandoning the search too early cost them the case.","exampleCN":"过早放弃搜寻让他们输掉了这桩案子。"},{"word":"abandonable","structure":"abandon + -able (able to be)","meaning":"capable of being abandoned","meaningCN":"可放弃的；可遗弃的（-able 表示“可以被……”）","example":"Few assets are truly abandonable under the contract.","exampleCN":"按合同规定，真正可以放弃的资产很少。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"ability","ipa_uk":"/əˈbɪləti/","ipa_us":"/əˈbɪləti/","definition_zh":"能力；才能；才智","definition_en":"the power or skill needed to do something","core_image":"握得住、做得成的力量","scene":"面试时，她把作品集摊在桌上，逐页讲解自己的做法。 At the interview she spread her portfolio across the table to show her ability to finish the design project on time.","sceneCN":"这里 ability 是「能力」（第 1 个义项：做某事的力量）；句意：面试时她摊开作品集，以展示自己按时完成这个设计项目的能力。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"能力；本领"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（常作 abilities）才智；专门技能"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"the ability to do something","zh":"做某事的能力"},{"phrase":"natural ability","zh":"天赋"},{"phrase":"to the best of one's ability","zh":"尽自己最大努力"},{"phrase":"ability to pay","zh":"支付能力"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"abilities"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"able","pos":"adj.","zh":"能够的；有能力的"},{"word":"unable","pos":"adj.","zh":"不能的；不会的"},{"word":"disable","pos":"v.","zh":"使丧失能力；使残废"},{"word":"disability","pos":"n.","zh":"残疾；无能力"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Capacity: the power to do something","titleCN":"能力：做某事的力量","definition":"the fact or power of being able to do something","definitionCN":"能够做某事的事实或力量","example":"She has the ability to solve complex problems.","exampleCN":"她有解决复杂问题的能力。","why":"Latin habilis meant 'handy, easy to manage', from habere 'to hold'. Ability is the quality that makes a task holdable — something you can grasp and carry out.","whyCN":"拉丁语 habilis 意为“顺手的、易于操控的”，来自 habere“握住”。ability 就是让任务变得“握得住”的性质——你能抓住并完成它。"},{"no":"02","title":"Learned skill: ability built by practice","titleCN":"习得技能：练出来的能力","definition":"a skill that has been developed through training or experience","definitionCN":"通过训练或经验发展出来的技能","example":"His language ability improved after a year abroad.","exampleCN":"在国外待了一年后，他的语言能力提高了。","why":"The same hold can be strengthened by repetition. What began as capacity becomes a trained grip, so ability also names acquired skills.","whyCN":"同一种“握持”可以通过重复而增强。起初只是能力，后来变成训练出来的抓握，因此 ability 也指后天习得的技能。"},{"no":"03","title":"Natural talent: ability present from the start","titleCN":"天赋：与生俱来的能力","definition":"a natural power or gift, especially in art, music, or sport","definitionCN":"天生的力量或天赋，尤指艺术、音乐或运动方面","example":"The child showed musical ability at an early age.","exampleCN":"这个孩子很小就显露出音乐天赋。","why":"A hold that is there before training is talent. English uses ability for both, but the 'natural' branch points to the hand that already grips well.","whyCN":"训练之前就已经存在的握力就是天赋。英语用 ability 兼指两者，但“天生”这一支强调的是那只本来就很会抓握的手。"},{"no":"04","title":"Mental power: ability of the mind","titleCN":"才智：心智的力量","definition":"intellectual capacity, especially the power to reason or understand","definitionCN":"智力；尤指推理或理解的能力","example":"The test measures the ability to reason under pressure.","exampleCN":"这项测试衡量的是在压力下推理的能力。","why":"Holding can be mental: the mind reaches for an idea, takes it in and works with it. Ability in this branch is the strength of that mental grip.","whyCN":"“握持”可以是心智层面的：头脑伸向一个想法，接住它并加以处理。这一支的 ability 就是这种心智抓握的力量。"},{"no":"05","title":"Financial means: ability to pay","titleCN":"财力：支付能力","definition":"the money or resources that make it possible to pay for something","definitionCN":"使某事物付得起所需的钱或资源","example":"They bought the house according to their ability to pay.","exampleCN":"他们根据支付能力买下了那栋房子。","why":"Money is an abstract hand: it can reach only as far as the amount allows. Ability to pay is the reach of that hand in the market.","whyCN":"金钱是一只抽象的手：它能伸多远，取决于金额有多少。ability to pay 就是这只手在市场里的伸展范围。"},{"no":"06","title":"-ability: the quality of being doable","titleCN":"-ability：可被做到的性质","definition":"the suffix -ability forms nouns meaning 'the quality of being able to be done or handled in that way'","definitionCN":"后缀 -ability 构成名词，表示“能够被那样做或处理的性质”","example":"Readability is the ability of a text to be read easily.","exampleCN":"readability（可读性）就是文本容易被读懂的性质。","why":"This is ability turned into a productive suffix. The noun no longer names a person's power but the passive possibility of a thing being handled.","whyCN":"这是 ability 变成能产后缀的用法。名词不再指某人的力量，而指某物“可以被处理”的被动可能性。"},{"no":"07","title":"To the best of one's ability: the limit of one's power","titleCN":"尽己所能：能力的边界","definition":"in the phrase to the best of one's ability, as well as one possibly can","definitionCN":"用于“to the best of one's ability”，表示尽自己所能","example":"I will help you to the best of my ability.","exampleCN":"我会尽我所能帮助你。","why":"The phrase draws the outer edge of the hand's reach. Everything inside that circle is what you can do; the best of your ability is the furthest point you can reach.","whyCN":"这个短语画出这只手能够到的外缘。圆圈之内就是你能做的范围；“the best of your ability”就是你能伸到的最远处。"},{"no":"08","title":"Of a machine or material: capacity to perform","titleCN":"机器或材料：完成任务的性能","definition":"the power of a device, system, or material to do a particular job under given conditions","definitionCN":"装置、系统或材料在特定条件下完成某项工作的能力","example":"The test measures the battery's ability to hold a charge in cold weather.","exampleCN":"这项测试测量电池在低温下保持电量的能力。","why":"The hand's reach becomes the reach of a tool: what a device can grasp and carry out is measured with the same word as what a person can.","whyCN":"手的伸展范围成了工具的伸展范围：装置能抓住并完成什么，与人能做什么，用的是同一个词。"},{"no":"09","title":"Law: capacity to act validly","titleCN":"法律：有效行为的能力","definition":"the legal capacity of a person or body to make binding acts, such as signing a contract","definitionCN":"个人或机构作出具约束力行为（如签署合同）的法律资格","example":"A minor does not have the legal ability to sign a binding contract.","exampleCN":"未成年人没有签署具约束力合同的法律资格。","why":"Here the grasp is a recognised power rather than a physical one: the law decides whose hand may hold a right and make it stick.","whyCN":"这里的“握”是被承认的权力而非体力：法律决定谁的手可以握住一项权利并使之生效。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Ability came through French from Latin habilitas, a noun built on habere 'to hold'. The initial h- was lost in French, which is why English has both able and the learned habilitate.","cn":"ability 经由法语来自拉丁语 habilitas，这是建立在 habere“握住”之上的名词。词首的 h- 在法语中脱落，所以英语既有 able，也有学术借词 habilitate。"},"items":[{"era":"LATE 14C.","en":"First recorded in late 14c. meaning 'state or condition of being able; capacity to do or act'.","cn":"最早记录于 14 世纪晚期，意为“能够的状态或条件；做事或行动的能力”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"From Old French ableté 'ability', especially 'ability to inherit', corresponding to able + -ty.","cn":"来自古法语 ableté“能力”，尤指“继承资格”，相当于 able + -ty。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"From Latin habilitas (genitive habilitatem) 'aptitude, ability', a noun from habilis 'easy to manage, handy', itself from habere 'to hold, have'.","cn":"来自拉丁语 habilitas（属格 habilitatem）“资质、能力”，由 habilis“顺手的、易于操控的”构成，而 habilis 又来自 habere“握住、拥有”。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Habere goes back to PIE *ghabh- 'to give or receive'. The same root underlies habit, exhibit and prohibit, all built on the idea of holding.","cn":"habere 可追溯到原始印欧语 *ghabh-“给予或接受”。同一词根也支撑 habit、exhibit、prohibit，它们都建立在“握持”这一概念上。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern spelling settled on ability. The Latin h- reappears in learned borrowings such as habilitate and rehabilitation, which shows the same root without the French loss.","cn":"现代拼写固定为 ability。拉丁语的 h- 在 habilitate、rehabilitation 等学术借词中重新出现，显示同一个词根未经法语脱落时的样子。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Spelling neighbours and near-synonyms are kept in separate groups so that form and meaning are not confused.","cn":"拼写相近词与近义词分开成组，避免把词形和词义混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"able","ipa":"/ˈeɪbl/","tag":"base word","definition":"having the power or skill to do something. It is the adjective behind ability, not a synonym of the noun.","definitionCN":"有力量或技能做某事。它是 ability 背后的形容词，不是这个名词的同义词。"},{"word":"agility","ipa":"/əˈdʒɪləti/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"the ability to move quickly and easily. It shares the -ility ending but comes from a different root.","definitionCN":"敏捷；快速灵活移动的能力。它同样以 -ility 结尾，但词根不同。"},{"word":"humility","ipa":"/hjuːˈmɪləti/","tag":"shared ending","definition":"the quality of not thinking you are better than other people. The ending looks like ability but the word is unrelated.","definitionCN":"谦逊；不认为自己高人一等。词尾看起来像 ability，但这个词与它无关。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"capacity","ipa":"/kəˈpæsəti/","tag":"potential","definition":"the maximum amount something can contain or produce; also the power to do something. It stresses a limit or volume.","definitionCN":"容量；最大可容纳或产出的量；也可指做事的能力。它强调限度或容量。"},{"word":"capability","ipa":"/ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti/","tag":"developed power","definition":"the power or ability to do something, often a developed or measurable one.","definitionCN":"能力；才干，常指已发展出来或可衡量的能力。"},{"word":"competence","ipa":"/ˈkɒmpɪtəns/","tag":"standard of skill","definition":"the ability to do something well enough for a standard or job. It stresses adequacy, not mere possibility.","definitionCN":"胜任力；达到标准或职位要求的足够能力。它强调“够格”，而不只是“有可能”。"},{"word":"skill","ipa":"/skɪl/","tag":"learned","definition":"a particular ability learned through training. It is narrower than ability and usually names one concrete competence.","definitionCN":"技能；通过训练学会的具体能力。它比 ability 窄，通常指一项具体本领。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real word parts and real relatives only: able + -ity, the habere family, and the productive -ability suffix.","cn":"只使用真实构词成分与真实同族词：able + -ity、habere 词族，以及能产的 -ability 后缀。"},"normal":[{"en":"ability = able + -ity: literally 'the state of being able'.","cn":"ability = able + -ity：字面就是“能够的状态”。"},{"en":"Latin habilis meant 'handy, easy to manage'. The same habere 'hold' gives habit (what you hold), exhibit (hold out) and prohibit (hold away).","cn":"拉丁语 habilis 意为“顺手的、易操控的”。同一个 habere“握住”还给出 habit（握有的东西）、exhibit（拿出来）、prohibit（挡住不让）。"},{"en":"inability and disable are the negated branches: in- and dis- remove the 'can do'.","cn":"inability 和 disable 是否定分支：in- 与 dis- 把“能做”拿掉。"},{"en":"To the best of one's ability draws the boundary of what one can hold and do.","cn":"“to the best of one's ability”画出一个人能握住、能做到的边界。"},{"en":"-ability is a live suffix: readability, accessibility and reliability are all formed the same way.","cn":"-ability 是仍在使用的后缀：readability、accessibility、reliability 都是同一方式构成的。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Think of ability as the circle a hand can reach: everything inside it is possible for that person.","cn":"把 ability 想成一只手能够到的圆圈：圈内的一切，对这个人来说都是可能的。"},{"en":"The circle can grow with practice (skill) or be wide from birth (talent).","cn":"这个圆圈可以通过练习变大（技能），也可能生来就宽（天赋）。"},{"en":"Money is a reach too: ability to pay is how far the hand can stretch into the market.","cn":"金钱也是一种伸展：ability to pay 就是这只手在市场里能伸多远。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Nina has the ability to stay calm in an emergency.","cn":"妮娜有能力在紧急情况下保持冷静。"},{"en":"The job requires strong communication abilities.","cn":"这份工作需要很强的沟通能力。"},{"en":"He fixed the radio to the best of his ability.","cn":"他尽自己所能修好了收音机。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿比力体”——阿比的力气很大、身体很强 → ability 能力","word":"ability"},"root":"源自拉丁语 habilis“顺手、易于操控”，再往上 habere 为“握住”，核心是“握得住、做得到”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of ability. They all measure a hand's reach: what a person can hold and carry out, whether by nature, training, mind, money, machine, law or grammar.","cn":"ability 的九个义项都在衡量一只手的伸展范围：一个人能握住并完成什么，无论出自天生、训练、心智、金钱、机器、法律还是语法层面。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a hand that can grip and carry a task.","cn":"核心意象：一只握得住、搬得动任务的手。"},"chain":["HOLD","WHAT CAN BE GRASPED","SKILL OR TALENT","MIND, MONEY, MACHINE","LEGAL CAPACITY","THE SUFFIX"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"THE MEASURE: the first sense is simply the reach of the hand, before any question of where it came from.","cn":"度量本身：第一个义项就是手的伸展范围，尚不问这份力量来自何处。"},{"senses":"02 · 03","en":"TRAINED AND NATIVE: practice builds the grip, or the grip was there from the start.","cn":"练出来的与天生的：练习把握力练出来，或者握力本来就在。"},{"senses":"04 · 05 · 08","en":"THE WIDER REACH: mind, money and machine are all extensions of the same grasp beyond the body.","cn":"更远的伸展：心智、金钱与机器，都是同一握力越过身体之后的延伸。"},{"senses":"09","en":"THE RECOGNISED POWER: law decides whose hand may bind a right and make the act stand.","cn":"被承认的权力：法律决定谁的手可以握住权利，并使行为生效。"},{"senses":"06 · 07","en":"GRAMMAR AND LIMIT: the suffix names what can be done to a thing, and the fixed phrase marks the edge of what one person can do.","cn":"语法与边界：后缀指某物能被怎样处理，固定短语则标出一个人能做到的极限。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Ability is a transparent noun: able + -ity. The suffix -ability is also productive on verbs, forming nouns such as readability and accessibility.","cn":"ability 是一个透明的名词：able + -ity。后缀 -ability 也能加在动词上，构成 readability、accessibility 这类名词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on habere 'to hold': habilis 'handy' gives ability and able, while habilitare 'make able' gives rehabilitate and rehabilitation.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 habere“握住”上：habilis“顺手的”给出 ability 和 able；habilitare“使能够”给出 rehabilitate 和 rehabilitation。"},"items":[{"word":"inability","structure":"in- (not) + ability","meaning":"the state of not being able to do something","meaningCN":"无能力；不能（in- 表示否定）","example":"His inability to swim kept him out of the boat.","exampleCN":"他不会游泳，所以没有上船。"},{"word":"disability","structure":"dis- (not, apart) + ability","meaning":"a condition that limits a person's physical or mental ability","meaningCN":"残疾；使身体或心智能力受限的状况（dis- 表示否定、分离）","example":"The building is designed for people with a disability.","exampleCN":"这栋建筑是为残障人士设计的。"},{"word":"enable","structure":"en- (make, put into) + able","meaning":"to make someone able to do something","meaningCN":"使能够；使成为可能（en- 表示“使……”）","example":"This app enables users to track their spending.","exampleCN":"这个应用让用户能够追踪自己的支出。"},{"word":"able-bodied","structure":"able + body + -ed","meaning":"physically healthy and strong, not disabled","meaningCN":"体格健全的（able + body + -ed）","example":"All able-bodied adults were asked to help.","exampleCN":"所有体格健全的成年人都被要求来帮忙。"},{"word":"disable","structure":"dis- (not) + able","meaning":"to make unable to act or work","meaningCN":"使失去能力；使伤残（dis- 表否定）","example":"The injury disabled him for a year.","exampleCN":"这次受伤使他一年无法工作。"},{"word":"disabled","structure":"disable + -ed (past participle as adjective)","meaning":"having a condition that limits activity","meaningCN":"有残疾的；丧失能力的（-ed 构成形容词）","example":"The building has ramps for disabled visitors.","exampleCN":"这栋楼为残障访客设有坡道。"},{"word":"unable","structure":"un- (not) + able","meaning":"not able to do something","meaningCN":"不能的；无法的（un- 表否定）","example":"They were unable to reach the summit.","exampleCN":"他们没能到达山顶。"},{"word":"ably","structure":"able + -ly (adverb; -le becomes -ly)","meaning":"in a competent way","meaningCN":"能干地；出色地（-ly 构成副词，able 去 e 加 -ly）","example":"She ably defended the proposal.","exampleCN":"她出色地为这项提议作了辩护。"},{"word":"disablement","structure":"disable + -ment (noun of state)","meaning":"the state of being disabled, or the act of disabling","meaningCN":"丧失能力的状态；使失效（-ment 构成状态名词）","example":"The policy covers temporary disablement.","exampleCN":"这项保单涵盖暂时丧失工作能力的情况。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"rehabilitate","structure":"re- (again) + habilitare (make able)","meaning":"to restore someone to health or normal life","meaningCN":"使康复；使恢复正常生活（re-“再次”+ habilitare“使能够”）"},{"word":"rehabilitation","structure":"re- + habilitare + -tion","meaning":"the process of restoring health or ability","meaningCN":"康复；复健（同一拉丁词根的抽象名词）"},{"word":"habilitate","structure":"habilitas (ability) + -ate","meaning":"to equip or qualify; a rare learned verb","meaningCN":"使具备资格；使有能力（罕用的学术动词）"}]}},{"word":"abnormal","ipa_uk":"/æbˈnɔːml/","ipa_us":"/æbˈnɔːrml/","definition_zh":"反常的；异常的；不正常的","definition_en":"not normal; deviating from a usual rule, standard, or healthy condition","core_image":"一条线离开了作为标准的直尺","scene":"体检报告送到诊室，医生的笔停在几行数字上。 The blood test showed an abnormal value, so the doctor turned the report toward the patient and explained each line.","sceneCN":"这里 abnormal 是「异常的」（第 3 个义项：医学上偏离健康常态）；句意：血液检查显示一项数值异常，医生把报告转向病人，逐行解释。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"反常的；异常的；不正常的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"异常的人或事物（罕用，常带贬义，宜避免）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"abnormal behavior","zh":"反常行为"},{"phrase":"abnormal condition","zh":"异常状态"},{"phrase":"abnormal cells","zh":"异常细胞"},{"phrase":"abnormal psychology","zh":"变态心理学；异常心理学"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more abnormal"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most abnormal"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"abnormality","pos":"n.","zh":"异常；反常事物"},{"word":"abnormally","pos":"adv.","zh":"异常地；反常地"},{"word":"abnormous","pos":"adj.","zh":"畸形的；反常的（古旧用法）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Deviation from the norm","titleCN":"偏离常规：不按规矩","definition":"not following the usual rule, standard, or pattern","definitionCN":"不遵循通常的规则、标准或模式","example":"Such a long delay is abnormal for this airline.","exampleCN":"对这家航空公司来说，延误这么久是反常的。","why":"Latin norma meant a carpenter's square, the tool that draws a straight line. Abnormal is literally 'away from the rule': the line leaves the square.","whyCN":"拉丁语 norma 指木匠的直角尺，是画直线的工具。abnormal 字面就是“离开规矩”：那条线离开了直尺。"},{"no":"02","title":"Unusual: much less common than expected","titleCN":"不寻常：比预期少见得多","definition":"much rarer or more extreme than is usual for a place or time","definitionCN":"对某个地点或时间而言，比通常情况罕见得多或极端得多","example":"The heat in October was abnormal for the region.","exampleCN":"对这个地区来说，十月的炎热很不寻常。","why":"The same departure from the rule can be measured by frequency. What almost never happens inside the normal range stands outside it as abnormal.","whyCN":"同一种“离开常规”也可以用出现频率来衡量。几乎不发生在正常范围内的事，就站到了范围之外，成为 abnormal。"},{"no":"03","title":"Medical: atypical in the body","titleCN":"医学异常：身体偏离健康常态","definition":"showing a condition that is not healthy or typical for the body","definitionCN":"表现出对身体而言不健康或不典型的状态","example":"The scan found abnormal cells in the tissue.","exampleCN":"扫描在组织里发现了异常细胞。","why":"Medicine treats health as the norm and illness as departure from it. A cell that does not follow the body's usual pattern is abnormal in the clinical sense.","whyCN":"医学把健康当作常规，把疾病当作对常规的偏离。不遵循身体通常模式的细胞，在临床意义上就是 abnormal。"},{"no":"04","title":"Statistical: far outside the normal range","titleCN":"统计离群：远离正常区间","definition":"lying well outside the expected range of a distribution or series","definitionCN":"明显落在分布或数据序列的预期范围之外","example":"The model flags abnormal trading volumes.","exampleCN":"这个模型会标记异常的交易量。","why":"A statistical norm is a band of expected values. A point far outside that band is abnormal, even when nothing is physically wrong.","whyCN":"统计上的“正常”是一段预期数值区间。远远落在区间之外的点就是 abnormal，即使并没有任何实体损坏。"},{"no":"05","title":"Psychological: behavior outside accepted norms","titleCN":"心理行为：偏离被接受的社会规范","definition":"used in psychology for behavior that departs from what a society considers normal","definitionCN":"心理学用语，指偏离社会所认为的正常标准的行为","example":"Abnormal psychology studies unusual patterns of behavior.","exampleCN":"异常心理学研究不寻常的行为模式。","why":"Here the ruler is social rather than physical. The word describes the gap between a person's behavior and the line a community draws, so it carries a judgment as well as a measurement.","whyCN":"这里的直尺是社会性的，而不是物理性的。这个词描述个人行为与社群所画之线之间的差距，因此它既是一种测量，也带有评判。"},{"no":"06","title":"Finance: returns above or below expectation","titleCN":"金融：超出预期的收益","definition":"in finance, returns that differ from the return expected from the market","definitionCN":"金融中指偏离市场预期水平的收益","example":"The fund reported abnormal returns after the announcement.","exampleCN":"公告发布后，该基金报告了超额收益。","why":"The expected market return is the rule; a return far from it is abnormal. The word keeps its neutral statistical meaning and does not imply anything illegal.","whyCN":"市场预期收益就是那条规矩；远离它的收益就是 abnormal。这里保留中性的统计含义，并不暗示违法。"},{"no":"07","title":"Noun: a deviant person or thing","titleCN":"名词：异常的人或物","definition":"a person or thing that deviates from the norm, usually plural and now dated or pejorative","definitionCN":"偏离常规的人或物，通常用复数，如今显得过时且带贬义","example":"Older medical texts grouped such patients as abnormals.","exampleCN":"较早的医学文献把这类病人归为“异常者”。","why":"Once the adjective names a departure, it can also name the departure itself; the usage survives mainly in old writing, where the label carried a judgment.","whyCN":"形容词一旦指称“偏离”，也就能指称偏离者本身；这种用法主要留在旧文献里，标签本身带着评判。"},{"no":"08","title":"Transport: a load beyond normal limits","titleCN":"运输：超出常规限值的货物","definition":"a load that is wider, longer, or heavier than ordinary limits allow and needs a special permit and escort","definitionCN":"在宽度、长度或重量上超过常规限值、需要特别许可与护送的超限货物","example":"The abnormal load moved at night under police escort.","exampleCN":"这批超限货物在警车护送下夜间运输。","why":"The ruler here is the size limit on a road. A load that leaves that limit is abnormal in the plain sense, but the industry treats it as a known category with its own rules.","whyCN":"这里的直尺是道路的尺寸限值。离开限值的货物按字面就是“异常”，但行业把它当成一个有专门规则的可预期类别。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Abnormal is a 19c. learned reshaping of an older word, not a direct inheritance from Greek. Its surface ab- was added under the influence of Latin norma, which is why the history is often called a chain of pseudo-etymological changes.","cn":"abnormal 是 19 世纪对旧词的学术性改写，并非直接继承自希腊语。表面的 ab- 是在拉丁语 norma 影响下加上的，所以这段历史常被称为一连串“伪词源式”改动。"},"items":[{"era":"1835","en":"Abnormal is recorded from 1835 as a remodelling of anormal, influenced by Latin abnormalis 'deviating from a fixed rule, irregular'.","cn":"abnormal 于 1835 年被记录，是对 anormal 的改写，受拉丁语 abnormalis“偏离固定规则、不规则”的影响。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin abnormalis = ab 'off, away from' + norma 'rule, carpenter's square'. The literal sense is 'away from the rule'.","cn":"拉丁语 abnormalis = ab“离开、偏离”+ norma“规则、直角尺”。字面义就是“离开规矩”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH / MEDIEVAL LATIN","en":"The older form anormal (13c. French) came from Medieval Latin anormalus, an altered borrowing of Greek anomalos 'uneven, irregular'.","cn":"更早的形式 anormal（13 世纪法语）来自中世纪拉丁语 anormalus，这是对希腊语 anomalos“不平整、不规则”的改写借词。"},{"era":"GREEK","en":"Greek anomalos = an- 'not' + homalos 'even', from homos 'same'. The Greek prefix was an-, not ab-; the b was introduced later by association with norma.","cn":"希腊语 anomalos = an-“不”+ homalos“平整”，后者来自 homos“相同”。希腊语前缀是 an-，不是 ab-；b 是后来因联想到 norma 才加进去的。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Homes shares PIE *sem- (1) 'one; as one, together with'. The Greek link is documented, but any claim that the modern ab- was original is source uncertain.","cn":"homos 与原始印欧语 *sem-（1）“一；作为一体”同源。希腊语这一环有据可查，但若说现代词形里的 ab- 原本就存在，则来源不确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Two groups: spelling neighbours first, then words that share the meaning of departure from a norm.","cn":"两组：先看拼写相近的词，再看同样表示“偏离常规”的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"anormal","ipa":"/æˈnɔːml/","tag":"older variant","definition":"the older form of abnormal, now archaic. It keeps the Greek an- without the later b.","definitionCN":"abnormal 的旧形式，现已古旧。它保留希腊语 an-，没有后来加入的 b。"},{"word":"abnormous","ipa":"/æbˈnɔːməs/","tag":"archaic adjective","definition":"an archaic adjective meaning misshapen or irregular; it looks like abnormal but has a different ending.","definitionCN":"古旧形容词，意为畸形的、不规则的；看起来像 abnormal，但词尾不同。"},{"word":"abnegate","ipa":"/ˈæbnɪɡeɪt/","tag":"ab- neighbour","definition":"to give something up or deny oneself something. It starts with ab- like abnormal but is unrelated in meaning.","definitionCN":"放弃；克制自己。它和 abnormal 一样以 ab- 开头，但词义无关。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"anomalous","ipa":"/əˈnɒmələs/","tag":"irregular","definition":"not fitting an established pattern; anomalous is the direct Greek branch behind the older anormal.","definitionCN":"不符合既有模式的；anomalous 正是旧词 anormal 背后的希腊语直系分支。"},{"word":"atypical","ipa":"/eɪˈtɪpɪkl/","tag":"not typical","definition":"not representative of its type. It is often more neutral than abnormal, especially in medicine.","definitionCN":"不典型的；不能代表其类型的。它常比 abnormal 更中性，医学语境尤其如此。"},{"word":"irregular","ipa":"/ɪˈreɡjələ/","tag":"not regular","definition":"not following a regular pattern in time, shape, or behavior.","definitionCN":"不规则的；在时间、形状或行为上不遵循规律模式的。"},{"word":"aberrant","ipa":"/əˈberənt/","tag":"deviating","definition":"deviating from what is normal or accepted, often used in biology and psychology.","definitionCN":"偏离正常或公认标准的，常用于生物学和心理学。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts and real relatives: ab- + normal, the norma family, and the Greek anomaly branch.","cn":"真实构词成分与真实同族词：ab- + normal、norma 词族，以及希腊语 anomaly 分支。"},"normal":[{"en":"ab- 'away from' + normal: abnormal is the line that leaves the rule. The ab- was added later, but the image fits the meaning.","cn":"ab-“离开”+ normal：abnormal 就是离开规矩的那条线。ab- 是后来加上的，但这个意象与词义吻合。"},{"en":"norma meant a carpenter's square, a tool for drawing straight lines; norm, normal, normalize and enormous belong to this family.","cn":"norma 指木匠的直角尺，是画直线的工具；norm、normal、normalize、enormous 都属于这个词族。"},{"en":"anomaly and anomalous come from Greek an- + homalos, the older branch behind anormal.","cn":"anomaly 和 anomalous 来自希腊语 an- + homalos，正是 anormal 背后的旧分支。"},{"en":"Abnormal psychology and abnormal cells are fixed technical collocations, not loose descriptions.","cn":"abnormal psychology 和 abnormal cells 是固定的专业搭配，不是随意的描述。"},{"en":"The noun is abnormality and the adverb is abnormally; the adjective itself usually takes more and most.","cn":"名词是 abnormality，副词是 abnormally；形容词本身通常用 more 和 most 构成比较级、最高级。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a straight ruler and a hand-drawn line that slowly leaves it: the gap between the line and the ruler is abnormality.","cn":"想象一把直尺和一条手画的线慢慢偏离它：线与尺之间的空隙就是“异常”。"},{"en":"The line can leave the ruler in degree (unusual), in the body (medical), in a data set (statistical) or in money (returns).","cn":"这条线可以在程度上离开直尺（不寻常）、在身体上离开（医学）、在数据集中离开（统计），或在金钱上离开（收益）。"},{"en":"When the ruler is drawn by society, abnormal behavior becomes a judgment about a person, not only a measurement of a body.","cn":"当直尺是由社会画出来的时候，abnormal behavior 就变成对人的评判，而不只是对身体的测量。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The doctor was worried by the abnormal rhythm of the heartbeat.","cn":"医生对异常的心跳节律感到担忧。"},{"en":"It is abnormal to see snow here in May.","cn":"这里五月下雪是不正常的。"},{"en":"The software alerts staff when an abnormal pattern appears.","cn":"出现异常模式时，软件会提醒工作人员。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿布诺莫”——阿布不按正常规矩来 → abnormal 反常的、异常的","word":"abnormal"},"root":"拉丁语 ab“离开”+ norma“规矩、直角尺”，字面义“离开规矩”；其中 ab- 是后世学术改写加上的。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of abnormal, all variations of one image: a line leaves the ruler. The ruler may be a rule, a frequency band, a healthy body, a society's norm, or a road's size limit.","cn":"abnormal 的八个义项都围绕同一个意象：线离开了直尺。这把直尺可以是规则、频率区间、健康身体、社会规范，也可以是道路的尺寸限值。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a line departing from the straight edge of a rule.","cn":"核心意象：一条线偏离了直尺的直边。"},"chain":["THE RULER","AWAY FROM THE RULER","THE BODY","THE DATA RANGE","THE NAME FOR THE DEVIANT","THE PERMIT LOAD"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"THE MEASURE ITSELF: a line leaves the ruler, and that plain departure is the first sense.","cn":"度量本身：线离开了直尺，这个最朴素的偏离就是第一个义项。"},{"senses":"02","en":"RARITY: what happens far less often than expected has already left the usual range.","cn":"稀少：发生频率远低于预期的事，已经站到了常规范围之外。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"BODY AND BEHAVIOUR: medicine and psychology each set a norm, then read departures from it.","cn":"身体与行为：医学与心理学各自设定一条常规，再读取对它的偏离。"},{"senses":"04 · 06","en":"NUMBER AND MONEY: a point outside the expected band, and a return outside the expected range.","cn":"数字与金钱：落在预期区间之外的点，以及超出预期区间的收益。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"NAMED EXCEPTIONS: the word also names the deviant itself, and a load allowed to exceed the rule by permit.","cn":"被命名的例外：这个词也用来指偏离者本身，以及获准越过规则的超限货物。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Abnormal looks like ab- + normal, and that is how modern speakers read it, although the ab- was added to an older Greek-derived word.","cn":"abnormal 看起来像 ab- + normal，现代说话者也是这样理解的，尽管 ab- 是后来加到旧希腊来源词上的。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on norma 'rule, carpenter's square': norm, normal, normalize and enormous (e-normis 'outside the norm') all belong here.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 norma“规矩、直角尺”上：norm、normal、normalize 以及 enormous（e-normis“在规矩之外”）都属于此。"},"items":[{"word":"abnormality","structure":"abnormal + -ity","meaning":"the state of being abnormal; an abnormal thing","meaningCN":"异常状态；反常事物（-ity 构成抽象名词）","example":"The test detected a minor abnormality in the blood.","exampleCN":"这项检查发现了血液中的轻微异常。"},{"word":"abnormally","structure":"abnormal + -ly","meaning":"in an abnormal way","meaningCN":"异常地；反常地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The engine was running abnormally hot.","exampleCN":"发动机运行温度异常偏高。"},{"word":"abnormous","structure":"ab- + norm + -ous","meaning":"misshapen, irregular (archaic)","meaningCN":"畸形的；不规则的（古旧用法，-ous 构成形容词）","example":"The old text describes an abnormous growth on the tree.","exampleCN":"旧文献描述这棵树上有一处畸形的生长物。"},{"word":"abnormity","structure":"ab- (away from) + norm + -ity","meaning":"a malformation or irregularity","meaningCN":"畸形；异常事物（-ity 构成名词）","example":"The scan revealed a slight abnormity in the joint.","exampleCN":"扫描显示关节处有一处轻微畸形。"},{"word":"norm","structure":"Latin norma (carpenter’s square, rule)","meaning":"the standard or average against which others are measured","meaningCN":"规范；常态（拉丁语 norma“直角尺、规矩”）","example":"Long hours have become the norm in this industry.","exampleCN":"长时间工作在这个行业已成常态。"},{"word":"normal","structure":"norm + -al (relating to)","meaning":"conforming to the standard","meaningCN":"正常的；标准的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"The engine is running at normal temperature.","exampleCN":"发动机在正常温度下运转。"},{"word":"normality","structure":"normal + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the condition of being normal","meaningCN":"正常状态（-ity 构成名词）","example":"The city slowly returned to normality.","exampleCN":"这座城市慢慢恢复了常态。"},{"word":"normalize","structure":"normal + -ize (make)","meaning":"to make something conform to a standard","meaningCN":"使正常化；使标准化（-ize 表示“使成为”）","example":"The two sides agreed to normalize trade relations.","exampleCN":"双方同意使贸易关系正常化。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"norm","structure":"norma (rule, square)","meaning":"a standard or rule of behavior","meaningCN":"规范；准则（直接来自 norma）"},{"word":"normal","structure":"norma + -alis","meaning":"following a standard; usual","meaningCN":"正常的；标准的（按规矩的）"},{"word":"normalize","structure":"normal + -ize","meaning":"to make normal or standard","meaningCN":"使正常化；使标准化"},{"word":"enormous","structure":"e- (out of) + norma (rule) + -ous","meaning":"literally 'outside the rule', hence extremely large","meaningCN":"字面义“在规矩之外”，因而表示“巨大的、庞大的”"}]}},{"word":"abolish","ipa_uk":"/əˈbɒlɪʃ/","ipa_us":"/əˈbɑːlɪʃ/","definition_zh":"废除；废止；消灭","definition_en":"to officially end a law, system, or practice, or to destroy something completely","core_image":"把写在黑板上的规则彻底擦掉","scene":"议会大厅里，议员们就一项延续百年的旧法律举手表决。 The parliament voted to abolish the century-old law.","sceneCN":"这里 abolish 是「废除」（第 1 个义项：正式终止法律）；句意：议会投票废除这项延续百年的旧法律。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"废除；废止（法律、制度、习俗）"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"消灭；彻底消除（古义偏“抹去、毁灭”）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"abolish slavery","zh":"废除奴隶制"},{"phrase":"abolish a law","zh":"废除一项法律"},{"phrase":"abolish the death penalty","zh":"废除死刑"},{"phrase":"abolish the monarchy","zh":"废除君主制"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"abolishes"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"abolished"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"abolished"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"abolishing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"abolition","pos":"n.","zh":"废除；废止（尤指奴隶制等制度）"},{"word":"abolishment","pos":"n.","zh":"废除；废止（较中性的名词形式）"},{"word":"abolitionist","pos":"n.","zh":"废奴主义者；主张废除者"},{"word":"abolitionism","pos":"n.","zh":"废奴主义；废除主义"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Formally end a law","titleCN":"废除法律：正式终止","definition":"to officially end a law or legal rule","definitionCN":"正式终止一项法律或法律规则","example":"Parliament voted to abolish the old tax.","exampleCN":"议会投票废除了这项旧税。","why":"A law is a written rule. To abolish it is to erase the writing by official act, so the word always carries the idea of a formal ending rather than a gradual fading.","whyCN":"法律是写下来的规则。废除它，就是通过官方行为把这段文字抹掉，所以这个词始终带有“正式终止”的意味，而不是逐渐消失。"},{"no":"02","title":"End an institution or system","titleCN":"废除制度：让机构不复存在","definition":"to put an end to an institution or a system of organization","definitionCN":"终止一个机构或一套组织制度","example":"The country abolished the monarchy in the twentieth century.","exampleCN":"这个国家在二十世纪废除了君主制。","why":"Institutions are held together by rules and offices. Abolishing them removes the structure itself, not just one rule inside it.","whyCN":"制度靠规则和职位维系。废除制度，是把整个结构拿掉，而不只是删掉其中一条规则。"},{"no":"03","title":"End a practice or custom","titleCN":"废止习俗：停止长期做法","definition":"to stop a practice or custom that has existed for a long time","definitionCN":"停止一项长期存在的做法或习俗","example":"The reform abolished the custom of charging for school.","exampleCN":"这项改革废止了上学收费的惯例。","why":"A custom is an unwritten rule followed by repetition. Abolishing it means declaring that the repetition should stop, even if no statute is involved.","whyCN":"习俗是靠重复遵循的不成文规则。废止它，就是宣布这种重复应当停止，即使不涉及成文法。"},{"no":"04","title":"Wipe out a harmful condition","titleCN":"消灭有害状况","definition":"to remove something completely, especially something harmful or unjust","definitionCN":"彻底消除某事物，尤指有害或不公正的事物","example":"The new rules aim to abolish child labour.","exampleCN":"新规旨在消除童工现象。","why":"The erasure is now aimed at a condition rather than a text. What remains is not a blank page but a society without that condition.","whyCN":"这里擦掉的不是文字，而是一种状况。留下的不是一张白纸，而是一个不再有这种状况的社会。"},{"no":"05","title":"Cancel an office or post","titleCN":"撤销职位：让岗位消失","definition":"to eliminate a position or office officially","definitionCN":"正式取消一个职位或机构岗位","example":"The agency abolished ten vacant posts.","exampleCN":"该机构撤销了十个空缺职位。","why":"A post exists only as long as the organization recognizes it. Cancelling the recognition erases the post without dismissing a person.","whyCN":"职位只有在组织承认时才存在。取消承认，就在不辞退任何人的情况下把这个职位抹掉了。"},{"no":"06","title":"Destroy utterly (archaic)","titleCN":"彻底摧毁（古旧义）","definition":"in older usage, to destroy or efface something so that no trace remains","definitionCN":"较古的用法：彻底毁灭或抹去，使不留下痕迹","example":"Time had abolished every trace of the old road.","exampleCN":"时间抹去了那条旧路的所有痕迹。","why":"The oldest Latin sense was 'destroy, efface, annihilate'. Modern English mostly keeps the institutional senses, but the image of total erasure still explains the word.","whyCN":"最古老的拉丁义就是“毁灭、抹去、消灭”。现代英语主要保留制度性义项，但“彻底擦除”的意象仍然是这个词的底层解释。"},{"no":"07","title":"Abolition: the ending of a system","titleCN":"废除：结束某制度的行为","definition":"the act or movement of ending a law, institution, or practice, especially slavery","definitionCN":"终止某项法律、制度或做法的行为或运动，尤指废除奴隶制","example":"The abolition of the law did not abolish the customs built around it.","exampleCN":"废除这项法律，并没有废除围绕它形成的习俗。","why":"The verb names the act; the noun names that act as an event with a date and a campaign behind it, which is why abolition became the name of a movement.","whyCN":"动词指动作本身，名词则把这个动作当成有日期、有运动支撑的事件，因此 abolition 成了一个运动的名称。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abolitionist: one who campaigns to abolish","titleCN":"废奴主义者：主张废除的人","definition":"a person who works to end a law, institution, or practice, especially slavery","definitionCN":"致力于终止某项法律、制度或做法的人，尤指主张废除奴隶制者","example":"The abolitionists pressed Parliament to abolish the trade at once.","exampleCN":"废奴主义者推动议会立即废除这项贸易。","why":"The suffix -ist marks the person who holds the purpose of the verb; the hand that erases the rule belongs to someone, and this word names that someone.","whyCN":"后缀 -ist 标出以该动词为目的的人；擦掉规则的那只手属于某个人，而这个词指的就是那个人。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Abolish came through French from Latin abolere 'destroy, efface'. The word's internal make-up is genuinely disputed, so the deepest link is marked uncertain rather than smoothed over.","cn":"abolish 经由法语来自拉丁语 abolere“毁灭、抹去”。这个词的内部构造确实有争议，因此最深层联系被明确标为不确定，而不是被强行讲通。"},"items":[{"era":"MID-15C.","en":"First recorded mid-15c. meaning 'to put an end to, do away with'.","cn":"最早记录于 15 世纪中期，意为“终止、去除”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"From the stem aboliss- of Old French abolir (15c.) 'to abolish'.","cn":"来自古法语 abolir（15 世纪）“废除”的现在分词词干 aboliss-。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"From Latin abolere 'destroy, efface, annihilate; cause to die out, retard the growth of'. The first element is ab- 'away'; the second is disputed.","cn":"来自拉丁语 abolere“毁灭、抹去、消灭；使灭绝、抑制生长”。第一个成分是 ab-“离开”；第二个成分有争议。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT (DISPUTED)","en":"One analysis takes ab- + adolere 'grow, magnify' as an opposite formation; another connects it with Greek olluein 'destroy'. Standard references present both, so the root affiliation is source uncertain.","cn":"一种分析把它拆成 ab- + adolere“生长、增大”，视为反义构词；另一种把它与希腊语 olluein“毁灭”联系起来。通行资料并列两说，故词根归属来源不确定。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"The 'grow' analysis would connect adolere to PIE *al- (2) 'to grow, nourish'. Because the Latin analysis itself is conditional, the PIE link is also conditional and source uncertain.","cn":"若采用“生长”分析，adolere 可连到原始印欧语 *al-（2）“生长、滋养”。由于拉丁语分析本身是有条件的，这一原始印欧语联系也同样来源不确定。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Abolition (1520s) and abolishment (1540s) took over the noun work. Abolition became the usual word for ending institutions, especially slavery.","cn":"abolition（16 世纪 20 年代）和 abolishment（16 世纪 40 年代）承担了名词功能。abolition 成为指废除制度、尤其是奴隶制的常用词。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Spelling neighbours are separated from near-synonyms, because several words ending in -lish have nothing to do with abolishing.","cn":"拼写相近词与近义词分开列出，因为好几个以 -lish 结尾的词与“废除”毫无关系。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"polish","ipa":"/ˈpɒlɪʃ/","tag":"spelling","definition":"to make a surface smooth and shiny. It differs only in the first letter and has no connection with abolishing.","definitionCN":"抛光；使表面光滑发亮。它只差第一个字母，与“废除”毫无关系。"},{"word":"demolish","ipa":"/dɪˈmɒlɪʃ/","tag":"spelling and meaning","definition":"to tear down a building. It shares the -lish ending and the idea of removal, but its object is physical.","definitionCN":"拆除建筑。它同样以 -lish 结尾，也含“去除”之意，但对象是实体建筑。"},{"word":"establish","ipa":"/ɪˈstæblɪʃ/","tag":"opposite partner","definition":"to set up an institution or system. It is the usual opposite of abolish in institutional contexts.","definitionCN":"建立机构或制度。在制度语境中，它常是 abolish 的反义词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"repeal","ipa":"/rɪˈpiːl/","tag":"law","definition":"to officially cancel a law. It is narrower than abolish and used mainly for statutes.","definitionCN":"正式废止法律。它比 abolish 窄，主要用于成文法。"},{"word":"revoke","ipa":"/rɪˈvəʊk/","tag":"permission or right","definition":"to cancel a permission, licence, or right, often because of a violation.","definitionCN":"撤销许可、执照或权利，常因违规而撤销。"},{"word":"annul","ipa":"/əˈnʌl/","tag":"legal status","definition":"to declare a marriage, contract, or decision invalid from the start.","definitionCN":"宣布婚姻、合同或决定自始无效。"},{"word":"eradicate","ipa":"/ɪˈrædɪkeɪt/","tag":"completely remove","definition":"to destroy something completely, especially a disease or a harmful practice.","definitionCN":"彻底消灭，尤指疾病或有害做法。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real morphology and real word pairs: abolish/abolition mirrors demolish/demolition.","cn":"真实构词与真实词对：abolish/abolition 与 demolish/demolition 构成同样的对应。"},"normal":[{"en":"Abolish pairs with abolition exactly as demolish pairs with demolition: verb in -ish, noun in -ition.","cn":"abolish 与 abolition 的对应，正像 demolish 与 demolition：动词以 -ish 结尾，名词以 -ition 结尾。"},{"en":"The ab- in abolere is felt as 'away', even though the deeper root is disputed: something is taken away until nothing remains.","cn":"abolere 中的 ab- 给人的感觉是“去掉”，尽管更深词根有争议：某物被拿走到什么都不剩。"},{"en":"Abolishment is the plain noun; abolition is the usual word for ending slavery and other institutions.","cn":"abolishment 是平实的名词；abolition 则是指废除奴隶制等制度的常用词。"},{"en":"Abolish a law, abolish slavery, abolish the death penalty and abolish the monarchy are fixed collocations.","cn":"“abolish a law”、“abolish slavery”、“abolish the death penalty”、“abolish the monarchy”都是固定搭配。"},{"en":"Abolish and establish are institutional opposites: one takes a system away, the other sets it up.","cn":"abolish 与 establish 是制度层面的反义词：一个拿掉制度，一个建立制度。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture chalk writing on a blackboard and a hand erasing it until no trace remains: abolish is the erasure of a rule.","cn":"想象黑板上用粉笔写的字，一只手把它擦到不留痕迹：abolish 就是对规则的擦除。"},{"en":"The erasure can target a law, an institution, a custom, a post or a harmful condition.","cn":"擦除的对象可以是法律、制度、习俗、职位或有害状况。"},{"en":"Unlike demolish, which leaves rubble, abolish aims at no visible remains at all.","cn":"demolish 会留下瓦砾，而 abolish 目标是连可见的残留都不留。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The new government promised to abolish the tax within a year.","cn":"新政府承诺一年内废除这项税。"},{"en":"Campaigners worked for decades to abolish slavery.","cn":"运动者们为废除奴隶制努力了几十年。"},{"en":"The company abolished the old approval process.","cn":"公司废除了旧的审批流程。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿波利什”——阿波把旧规定一笔划掉 → abolish 废除、废止","word":"abolish"},"root":"源自拉丁语 abolere“抹去、毁灭”，词首 ab- 带“去掉”意味；更深词根归属存疑。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of abolish, all acts of erasing: a law, an institution, a custom, a harmful condition, a post, every trace of a thing, and the movement and the people who carry it out.","cn":"abolish 的八个义项都是“擦除”行为：擦掉法律、制度、习俗、有害状况、职位、某物的所有痕迹，以及推动废除的运动与推动它的人。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a hand erases a rule from the board until nothing is left.","cn":"核心意象：一只手把规则从黑板上擦掉，直到什么都不剩。"},"chain":["WRITTEN RULE","OFFICIAL ERASURE","INSTITUTION ENDED","PRACTICE STOPPED","TOTAL EFFACEMENT","THE MOVEMENT AND ITS PEOPLE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"THE INSTRUMENT: a written law is erased by the authority that made it.","cn":"工具本身：成文的法律由制定它的权威擦除。"},{"senses":"02 · 05","en":"THE INSTITUTION: a system and a post both stop existing when the rule behind them is removed.","cn":"制度层面：支撑它们的规则一旦撤掉，制度与职位都不复存在。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"THE PRACTICE: a custom is stopped, and a harmful condition is wiped out.","cn":"做法层面：长期的做法被叫停，有害的状况被清除。"},{"senses":"06","en":"TOTAL EFFACEMENT: the older, stronger sense removes every trace, not just the rule.","cn":"彻底抹去：更古更强的义项去掉的不只是规则，而是所有痕迹。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"NOT ONLY A VERB: the act becomes a named cause, and the person who carries it out is named too.","cn":"不止是动词：这个动作成了有名称的事业，推动它的人也有了专门的称呼。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Abolish takes two noun suffixes: -tion gives abolition, the usual institutional noun, and -ment gives abolishment, the plainer one.","cn":"abolish 可接两个名词后缀：-tion 构成 abolition，是制度语境中的常用名词；-ment 构成较平实的 abolishment。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin abolere is the immediate source, but no separate Latin cognate family is securely established. The Latin entries are therefore left empty rather than filled with invented relatives.","cn":"拉丁语 abolere 是直接来源，但并没有可靠确立的另一支拉丁同族词。因此拉丁词族条目留空，而不是用编造的亲属词填充。"},"items":[{"word":"abolition","structure":"abolish + -tion (noun of action)","meaning":"the official ending of a law, institution, or practice","meaningCN":"废除；废止（-tion 构成行为名词）","example":"The abolition of slavery took decades.","exampleCN":"废除奴隶制花了几十年。"},{"word":"abolishment","structure":"abolish + -ment (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of abolishing something","meaningCN":"废除；废止的行为（-ment 构成行为名词）","example":"The abolishment of the rule surprised everyone.","exampleCN":"这项规则的废止让所有人吃惊。"},{"word":"abolitionist","structure":"abolition + -ist (person who supports)","meaning":"a person who campaigns to end a practice, especially slavery","meaningCN":"废奴主义者；主张废除者（-ist 表示支持者）","example":"The abolitionists published pamphlets against slavery.","exampleCN":"废奴主义者印行小册子反对奴隶制。"},{"word":"abolitionism","structure":"abolition + -ism (movement or doctrine)","meaning":"the movement or belief that a practice should be abolished","meaningCN":"废奴主义；废除主义（-ism 表示运动或主张）","example":"Abolitionism spread across the northern states.","exampleCN":"废奴主义在北方各州传播开来。"},{"word":"abolishable","structure":"abolish + -able (able to be)","meaning":"capable of being abolished","meaningCN":"可废除的（-able 表示“可以被……”）","example":"The tax is legally abolishable by a simple vote.","exampleCN":"这项税只需一次简单表决便可依法废除。"},{"word":"abolisher","structure":"abolish + -er (person who does)","meaning":"a person who abolishes something","meaningCN":"废除者（-er 表示施事者）","example":"The reform had many friends and one loud abolisher.","exampleCN":"这项改革支持者众多，却有一个高声主张废除的人。"},{"word":"abolished","structure":"abolish + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"done away with, ended by law","meaningCN":"被废除的（-ed 构成过去分词）","example":"Slavery was abolished in the nineteenth century.","exampleCN":"奴隶制在十九世纪被废除。"},{"word":"abolishing","structure":"abolish + -ing (present participle and gerund)","meaning":"the act or process of ending something","meaningCN":"废除（动名词）；正在废除（现在分词）","example":"Abolishing the old rule took two years.","exampleCN":"废除那条旧规用了两年。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"absence","ipa_uk":"/ˈæbsəns/","ipa_us":"/ˈæbsəns/","definition_zh":"缺席；不在；缺乏","definition_en":"the state of not being present, or the lack of something","core_image":"一把空着的椅子：本该在那里的东西不在","scene":"老师照着点名册抬起头，看见一个空座位。 The teacher looked up from the roll book, saw one empty seat, and marked that student's absence in the column.","sceneCN":"这里 absence 是「缺席」（第 1 个义项：不在场）；句意：老师从点名册上抬起头，看见一个空座位，便在对应栏里记下那名学生的缺席。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"缺席；不在场"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"缺乏；没有"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"in the absence of","zh":"在缺少……的情况下"},{"phrase":"absence from school","zh":"缺课；未到校"},{"phrase":"leave of absence","zh":"准假；请假"},{"phrase":"a long absence","zh":"长期的离开"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"absences"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"absent","pos":"adj.","zh":"缺席的；不在的"},{"word":"absentee","pos":"n.","zh":"缺席者；未到者"},{"word":"absently","pos":"adv.","zh":"心不在焉地"},{"word":"absent-minded","pos":"adj.","zh":"心不在焉的；健忘的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Not present in a place","titleCN":"不在场：该在的地方没有人","definition":"the state of not being present in a place where one is expected","definitionCN":"不在预期该出现的地点","example":"Her absence from the meeting was noticed at once.","exampleCN":"大家立刻注意到她没有出席会议。","why":"Latin abesse is literally 'to be away from': ab- 'away' + esse 'to be'. The word begins with a body that is simply not in its expected place.","whyCN":"拉丁语 abesse 字面就是“离开着存在”：ab-“离开”+ esse“存在”。这个词的起点，是一个不在预期位置的身体。"},{"no":"02","title":"A period of being away","titleCN":"离开的期间","definition":"a length of time during which someone is away from a place or role","definitionCN":"某人离开某地或某职位的一段时间","example":"After a long absence, he returned to teaching.","exampleCN":"离开很长一段时间后，他重新回到教学岗位。","why":"Absence can be counted in time. The empty chair stays empty for a stretch, and that stretch becomes a noun in its own right.","whyCN":"absence 也可以按时间计量。空椅子在一段时间里一直空着，这段长度本身就变成了一个名词。"},{"no":"03","title":"Lack of something needed","titleCN":"缺乏：缺少所需之物","definition":"the state of not having something that is needed or expected","definitionCN":"缺少所需或所期待之物","example":"The absence of clean water is the village's main problem.","exampleCN":"缺乏干净的水是这个村子的主要问题。","why":"The empty place is no longer a chair but a slot in a supply. What should be there is missing, so absence shifts from 'not here' to 'not available'.","whyCN":"空着的位置不再是一把椅子，而是供应中的一格。本该在那里的东西缺失了，于是 absence 从“不在这里”转为“没有”。"},{"no":"04","title":"Absence of mind: inattention","titleCN":"心不在焉：注意力不在场","definition":"a momentary failure to pay attention, as if the mind is elsewhere","definitionCN":"一时没有注意，仿佛心思在别处","example":"His absence of mind during the drive almost caused a crash.","exampleCN":"他开车时心不在焉，差点造成事故。","why":"The body can be present while the mind is away. The same word moves inward: attention itself is the thing that is not in its place.","whyCN":"身体可以在场，而心思却在别处。同一个词转向内部：这次不在位的是注意力本身。"},{"no":"05","title":"Unauthorized absence","titleCN":"擅离：未获准的缺勤","definition":"the failure to be at a required place, especially in school or military contexts","definitionCN":"未出现在规定应在的地点，尤用于学校或军队语境","example":"The soldier was punished for absence without leave.","exampleCN":"这名士兵因擅离职守受到处罚。","why":"Here the empty place is enforced by an institution. Being away is not neutral any more: the rule turns absence into an offence.","whyCN":"这里空着的位置是由制度强制要求的。离开不再是中性的事实：规则把 absence 变成了一种违规。"},{"no":"06","title":"In the absence of: without something","titleCN":"在缺少……的情况下","definition":"in the phrase in the absence of, meaning 'because someone or something is not there'","definitionCN":"用于“in the absence of”，表示“因为某人或某物不在”","example":"In the absence of a doctor, the nurse took charge.","exampleCN":"在没有医生的情况下，护士负起了责任。","why":"The phrase turns the empty slot into a condition. The thing that is not there becomes the background against which an action happens.","whyCN":"这个短语把空位变成一种条件。不在场的事物成了行动发生的背景。"},{"no":"07","title":"Absence makes the heart grow fonder","titleCN":"距离产生思念","definition":"in the proverb absence makes the heart grow fonder, distance increases affection","definitionCN":"用于谚语“absence makes the heart grow fonder”，表示距离会让感情更深","example":"She missed him more each month: absence makes the heart grow fonder.","exampleCN":"她每个月都更想念他：距离产生思念。","why":"The missing person leaves a shape behind. The longer the shape stays empty, the more the mind fills it with longing, so absence can intensify feeling.","whyCN":"缺席的人留下了一个形状。这个形状空得越久，心里就用思念把它填得越满，所以 absence 也能加深感情。"},{"no":"08","title":"Leave of absence: permitted time away","titleCN":"准假：获准离开的一段时间","definition":"official permission to be away from work, school, or duty for a stated period","definitionCN":"获准在工作、学业或职务上离开一段明确时间的正式许可","example":"She took a leave of absence to care for her father.","exampleCN":"她请了准假去照顾父亲。","why":"The empty seat is now covered by a record: the absence is expected, dated and allowed, so it stops being a fault.","whyCN":"空着的座位如今有一纸记录兜住：这次不在是预期之内、有日期、被允许的，因此不再算过失。"},{"no":"09","title":"Medicine: a brief lapse of awareness","titleCN":"医学：短暂失神的发作","definition":"a short epileptic seizure in which a person briefly stops responding, often for only a few seconds","definitionCN":"一种短暂的癫痫发作，患者会短暂停止反应，往往只有几秒钟","example":"The child's absence seizures went unnoticed until a teacher reported them.","exampleCN":"孩子的失神发作一直没被发现，直到老师报告。","why":"The mind is the thing that is absent: the body stays upright and awake-looking while awareness drops out for a moment, so the clinical name describes exactly that gap.","whyCN":"缺席的是心智：身体仍站得直、看起来清醒，意识却短暂掉了出去，临床名称描述的正是这段空白。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Absence is a Latin abstract noun built on the verb 'to be away'. It came to English through French and has stayed close to the literal image of not being in place.","cn":"absence 是建立在“离开着存在”这一动词之上的拉丁抽象名词，经由法语进入英语，始终贴近“不在原位”的字面意象。"},"items":[{"era":"LATE 14C.","en":"First recorded late 14c. meaning 'state of not being present'.","cn":"最早记录于 14 世纪晚期，意为“不在场的状态”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"From Old French absence (14c.), from Latin absentia.","cn":"来自古法语 absence（14 世纪），再往上为拉丁语 absentia。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin absentia is an abstract noun from absentem, the present participle of abesse 'be away from' = ab 'away' + esse 'to be'.","cn":"拉丁语 absentia 是抽象名词，来自 abesse“离开着存在”的现在分词 absentem；abesse = ab“离开”+ esse“存在”。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Esse goes back to PIE *es- 'to be', the same root behind present, essence and entity.","cn":"esse 可追溯到原始印欧语 *es-“存在”，present、essence、entity 也都出自这个词根。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English uses absence for both physical nonattendance and lack. The adjective absent and the noun absentee divide the persons and the states.","cn":"现代英语用 absence 兼指身体不在场和事物缺乏。形容词 absent 与名词 absentee 则分担“人”和“状态”的不同用法。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is about spelling and endings; the second is about words that also describe something missing.","cn":"第一组看拼写和词尾；第二组看同样表示“缺失”的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"absinthe","ipa":"/ˈæbsɪnθ/","tag":"spelling","definition":"a strong green alcoholic drink. It begins with abs- like absence but is a different word entirely.","definitionCN":"一种浓烈的绿色酒精饮料。它和 absence 一样以 abs- 开头，但完全是另一个词。"},{"word":"essence","ipa":"/ˈesns/","tag":"shared ending","definition":"the central quality of something. It shares the -sence ending and the Latin verb esse, but not the 'away' prefix.","definitionCN":"本质；核心性质。它同样以 -sence 结尾，也来自拉丁语 esse，但没有“离开”的前缀。"},{"word":"absentee","ipa":"/ˌæbsənˈtiː/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"a person who is absent, especially from work or school.","definitionCN":"缺席者，尤指缺勤或缺课的人。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"lack","ipa":"/læk/","tag":"shortage","definition":"the state of not having enough of something. It is more general than absence and often implies a need.","definitionCN":"缺少；不足。它比 absence 更泛，常暗示一种需要。"},{"word":"scarcity","ipa":"/ˈskeəsəti/","tag":"supply","definition":"a situation in which something is hard to obtain because there is too little of it.","definitionCN":"稀缺；因数量太少而难以获得的情况。"},{"word":"deficiency","ipa":"/dɪˈfɪʃnsi/","tag":"technical lack","definition":"a lack of something needed, especially a nutrient or a quality; often technical.","definitionCN":"缺乏；不足，尤指营养或某种性质，常为技术用语。"},{"word":"nonattendance","ipa":"/ˌnɒnəˈtendəns/","tag":"formal absence","definition":"failure to attend a meeting, class, or event; a formal synonym for one branch of absence.","definitionCN":"未出席；未参加，是 absence“缺席”这一支的正式同义词。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts and real relatives: ab- 'away' + esse 'to be', plus the present/essence family.","cn":"真实构词与真实同族词：ab-“离开”+ esse“存在”，以及 present/essence 词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"ab- 'away' + esse 'to be' = 'to be away'. That is the whole core of absence.","cn":"ab-“离开”+ esse“存在”=“离开着存在”。这就是 absence 的全部核心。"},{"en":"Absent, absentee and absently keep the same image of someone or something not in place.","cn":"absent、absentee、absently 都保留同一个意象：某人或某物不在原位。"},{"en":"In the absence of is a fixed phrase meaning 'without'; it turns the empty slot into a condition.","cn":"“in the absence of”是固定短语，意为“在没有……的情况下”；它把空位变成一种条件。"},{"en":"Absence of mind is the old phrase for inattention: the mind is away even when the body is present.","cn":"absence of mind 是表示“心不在焉”的旧短语：即使身体在场，心思也离开了。"},{"en":"Present is the mirror image: prae- 'before' + esse 'to be', literally 'being before you'.","cn":"present 是镜像：prae-“在前”+ esse“存在”，字面就是“在你面前存在”。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a chair with no one in it: absence is the shape of the missing body.","cn":"想象一把没有人坐的椅子：absence 就是那个缺失身体留下的形状。"},{"en":"That empty shape can be in a room (not present), in a supply (lack) or in attention (the mind is elsewhere).","cn":"这个空形状可以出现在房间里（不在场）、出现在供应里（缺乏），也可以出现在注意力里（心思在别处）。"},{"en":"Distance makes the empty chair feel larger, which is why absence makes the heart grow fonder.","cn":"距离让空椅子显得更大，这就是为什么 absence 会让思念更深。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The manager took over in the absence of the director.","cn":"主任不在时，经理接手了工作。"},{"en":"Three weeks of absence from class left him far behind.","cn":"缺课三周让他落下很多。"},{"en":"The absence of a signature made the form invalid.","cn":"缺少签名使这张表格无效。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿布森斯”——阿布没来上课，座位一直空着 → absence 缺席、不在","word":"absence"},"root":"拉丁语 ab“离开”+ esse“存在”，字面义“不在场、离开着存在”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of absence, all variants of one empty shape: a body missing, a period away, a missing supply, a mind elsewhere, a rule broken, a condition without something, affection grown from distance, authorised leave, and a few seconds of lost awareness.","cn":"absence 的九个义项都围绕同一个“空形状”：缺席的身体、离开的时段、缺失的供应、走神的心思、被违反的出勤规则、没有某物的条件、因距离加深的感情、获准的假期，以及几秒钟的失神。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: an empty place where something or someone should be.","cn":"核心意象：某物或某人本该在的位置空着。"},"chain":["A BODY","AWAY","THE EMPTY PERIOD","LACK","THE MIND ELSEWHERE","INSTITUTIONAL AND MEDICAL TIME"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 05","en":"A BODY MISSING: the seat is empty, whether by permission or in breach of the rule.","cn":"缺席的身体：座位空着，无论是获准的还是违反规定的。"},{"senses":"02 · 07","en":"TIME AWAY: a stretch of days, and the affection that distance can create.","cn":"离开的时间：一段日子，以及距离反而养出的感情。"},{"senses":"03 · 06","en":"LACK: what is needed is not there, and the phrase for acting without it.","cn":"缺乏：所需之物不在，以及表示在没有它的情况下行事的那一短语。"},{"senses":"04","en":"THE MIND: attention drops out while the body stays in place.","cn":"心智：身体留在原地，注意力却掉了出去。"},{"senses":"08 · 09","en":"RECORDED ABSENCE: leave with a date on file, and a few seconds of lost awareness with a clinical name.","cn":"有记录的缺席：有日期可查的准假，以及有了临床名称的几秒钟失神。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Absence is a noun of state in -ence. English builds absent, absentee, absently and absent-minded from the same 'away' core.","cn":"absence 是带 -ence 的状态名词。英语从同一个“离开”核心构成 absent、absentee、absently 和 absent-minded。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on esse 'to be' (PIE *es-): present 'being before', essence 'being itself', entity 'a being', and interest 'it is between' all belong here.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 esse“存在”（原始印欧语 *es-）上：present“在面前存在”、essence“存在本身”、entity“存在者”、interest“位于其间”都属于此。"},"items":[{"word":"absent","structure":"ab- (away) + esse (be) + -ent","meaning":"not present in a place","meaningCN":"缺席的；不在的（-ent 构成形容词）","example":"Two students were absent today.","exampleCN":"今天有两名学生缺席。"},{"word":"absentee","structure":"absent + -ee (person affected)","meaning":"a person who is absent","meaningCN":"缺席者；缺勤者（-ee 表示受影响的人）","example":"The company keeps a record of absentees.","exampleCN":"公司记录缺勤人员。"},{"word":"absently","structure":"absent + -ly","meaning":"in an inattentive way","meaningCN":"心不在焉地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"She nodded absently while reading.","exampleCN":"她一边看书一边心不在焉地点头。"},{"word":"absent-minded","structure":"absent + mind + -ed","meaning":"often forgetting things because one's mind is elsewhere","meaningCN":"心不在焉的；健忘的","example":"The absent-minded professor forgot his keys again.","exampleCN":"那位心不在焉的教授又忘带钥匙了。"},{"word":"absenteeism","structure":"absentee + -ism (practice or condition)","meaning":"the habit of regularly staying away from work or school","meaningCN":"旷工；旷课（-ism 表示行为或状态）","example":"Absenteeism rose sharply after the shift change.","exampleCN":"换班之后旷工率急剧上升。"},{"word":"absent-mindedness","structure":"absent-minded + -ness (quality)","meaning":"the quality of being forgetful or distracted","meaningCN":"心不在焉（-ness 构成抽象名词）","example":"His absent-mindedness lost him the keys again.","exampleCN":"他心不在焉，又把钥匙弄丢了。"},{"word":"absented","structure":"absent + -ed (past tense and past participle of the verb)","meaning":"kept oneself away deliberately","meaningCN":"缺席的（absent 作动词时的过去式与过去分词）","example":"She absented herself from the meeting.","exampleCN":"她故意没去参加那次会议。"},{"word":"absenting","structure":"absent + -ing (present participle and gerund)","meaning":"the act of keeping oneself away","meaningCN":"缺席（动名词）；正在缺席（现在分词）","example":"Absenting himself from class did him no good.","exampleCN":"他逃课对自己毫无好处。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"present","structure":"prae- (before) + esse (be)","meaning":"being here, before someone","meaningCN":"在场的；现在的（字面义“在面前存在”）"},{"word":"essence","structure":"esse (be) + -entia","meaning":"the being or nature of something","meaningCN":"本质；实质（存在本身）"},{"word":"entity","structure":"ens (being) + -ity","meaning":"a thing that exists","meaningCN":"实体；存在者"},{"word":"interest","structure":"inter- (between) + esse (be)","meaning":"literally 'it is between', hence concern or benefit","meaningCN":"兴趣；利益（字面义“位于其间”，因而引申为关切、利害）"}]}},{"word":"absolute","ipa_uk":"/ˈæbsəluːt/","ipa_us":"/ˈæbsəluːt/","definition_zh":"绝对的；完全的；不受限制的","definition_en":"complete and total, or not limited by anything else","core_image":"所有绳结都被解开，没有任何东西再牵着它","scene":"法庭上，法官面前摆着王冠的图案和一本法律文本。 The judge ruled that the king could not hold absolute power and had to answer to the law.","sceneCN":"这里 absolute 是「不受限制的」（第 2 个义项：权力不受法律限制）；句意：法官裁定国王不能拥有不受限制的权力，必须受法律约束。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"完全的；绝对的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"不受限制的；专制的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"absolute power","zh":"绝对权力"},{"phrase":"absolute majority","zh":"绝对多数"},{"phrase":"absolute zero","zh":"绝对零度"},{"phrase":"absolute certainty","zh":"绝对确定"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more absolute"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most absolute"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"absolutely","pos":"adv.","zh":"绝对地；完全地"},{"word":"absoluteness","pos":"n.","zh":"绝对性；完全性"},{"word":"absolutism","pos":"n.","zh":"专制主义；绝对主义"},{"word":"absolutist","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"专制主义者；绝对主义者"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Complete and utter","titleCN":"完全的：没有任何保留","definition":"complete and total, used to emphasize a quality","definitionCN":"完全的、彻底的，用来强调某种性质","example":"The room was in absolute silence.","exampleCN":"房间里一片绝对的寂静。","why":"Latin absolvere meant 'to set free, complete, bring to an end'. Something absolute has been finished off and loosened from every qualification, so it is complete with nothing left out.","whyCN":"拉丁语 absolvere 意为“释放、完成、结束”。绝对的东西已经被完成，并从一切限定中松开，因此它是完整无缺的。"},{"no":"02","title":"Unlimited in power or right","titleCN":"权力不受限制","definition":"not limited by law, authority, or conditions","definitionCN":"不受法律、权威或条件限制","example":"The dictator claimed absolute power over the country.","exampleCN":"独裁者声称对国家拥有绝对权力。","why":"If every restraint is a knot tying power down, absolute power has had all those knots cut. Nothing outside it can limit it.","whyCN":"如果每一种约束都是把权力捆住的绳结，那么绝对权力就是所有绳结都被剪断的权力。它之外没有任何东西能限制它。"},{"no":"03","title":"Not relative","titleCN":"非相对的：不靠比较成立","definition":"existing or true independently, not judged in relation to something else","definitionCN":"独立存在或成立，不靠与其他事物比较来判断","example":"Philosophers debated whether any truth is absolute.","exampleCN":"哲学家们争论是否存在绝对真理。","why":"A relative value depends on a comparison; an absolute one is loosened from the comparison altogether. It stands on its own, without a reference point.","whyCN":"相对价值依赖比较；绝对价值则完全从比较中松开。它独自成立，不需要参照点。"},{"no":"04","title":"Definite and certain","titleCN":"确定无疑","definition":"definite and not open to doubt","definitionCN":"确定且不容置疑","example":"I have absolute confidence in her.","exampleCN":"我对她有绝对的信心。","why":"Doubt is a condition attached to a claim. When that condition is removed, confidence becomes absolute: nothing is left to qualify it.","whyCN":"怀疑是附在断言上的一个条件。当这个条件被拿掉，信心就变成绝对的：没有任何东西再来限定它。"},{"no":"05","title":"Grammar: absolute construction","titleCN":"语法：独立结构","definition":"a phrase that is grammatically independent of the rest of the sentence","definitionCN":"在语法上独立于句子其余部分的短语","example":"In 'The weather being fine, we went out', the first clause is absolute.","exampleCN":"在“The weather being fine, we went out”中，前半部分就是独立结构。","why":"The construction is 'loosened' from the main clause: it does not depend on the subject or verb. The grammatical name repeats the Latin image of release.","whyCN":"这种结构从主句上“松开”：它不依赖主语或谓语。这个语法名称重复了拉丁语“释放”的意象。"},{"no":"06","title":"Despotic: ruling without checks","titleCN":"专制的：统治不受制约","definition":"using power without checks or balances, often with disapproval","definitionCN":"行使权力时没有制衡，常含贬义","example":"They lived under an absolute ruler for generations.","exampleCN":"他们几代人都生活在专制统治者的治下。","why":"This is the political judgment of sense 2. Power with no knot is admired as sovereignty and feared as despotism, depending on who holds it.","whyCN":"这是第 2 个义项的政治评判。没有绳结的权力，既可能被赞为主权，也可能被惧为专制，取决于谁握着它。"},{"no":"07","title":"Physics: absolute zero","titleCN":"物理：绝对零度","definition":"the lowest possible temperature, taken as zero on the Kelvin scale","definitionCN":"可能达到的最低温度，在开尔文温标上记为零","example":"At absolute zero, particle motion is at its minimum.","exampleCN":"在绝对零度，粒子运动达到最低限度。","why":"Absolute zero is a floor that cannot be gone below. The word marks a limit that is not relative to any scale; it is the end point of temperature itself.","whyCN":"绝对零度是一条不能再往下的底线。这个词标记的是一个不相对任何温标的界限；它就是温度本身的终点。"},{"no":"08","title":"Politics: more than half of all votes","titleCN":"政治：超过全体半数","definition":"a majority larger than half of the total number of possible votes, not merely more than the other side","definitionCN":"超过可能总票数一半的多数，而不只是比对方多","example":"The bill passed with an absolute majority of the assembly.","exampleCN":"该法案以议会绝对多数通过。","why":"The word removes comparison: an ordinary majority is measured against the opposing side, while this one is measured against the whole, so nothing outside it can change the result.","whyCN":"这个词去掉了比较：普通多数是相对于对方来量，而这一种是对全体来量，外部任何变化都改不了结果。"},{"no":"09","title":"Mathematics: size without sign","titleCN":"数学：不带符号的大小","definition":"the distance of a number from zero, written without regard to whether it is positive or negative","definitionCN":"一个数到零的距离，不论其为正还是为负","example":"The absolute value of minus five is five.","exampleCN":"负五的绝对值是五。","why":"Comparison with other numbers is stripped away: only the magnitude remains, and the minus sign, which depends on direction, is dropped.","whyCN":"与其他数比较的成分被剥掉：只剩大小，表示方向的负号则被去掉。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Absolute comes from the past participle of Latin absolvere 'to loosen away, set free, complete'. The modern senses of 'complete' and 'unlimited' both grow out of that image of release.","cn":"absolute 来自拉丁语 absolvere“松开、释放、完成”的过去分词。现代的“完全”和“不受限制”两个义项，都从这个“释放”意象生长出来。"},"items":[{"era":"LATE 14C.","en":"First recorded late 14c. meaning 'unrestricted, free from limitation; complete, perfect'. The sense 'not relative' appears in the mid-15c.","cn":"最早记录于 14 世纪晚期，意为“不受限制的、摆脱限定的；完全的、完美的”。“非相对”义在 15 世纪中期出现。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"From Latin absolutus, past participle of absolvere 'to set free, acquit; complete, bring to an end; make separate'.","cn":"来自拉丁语 absolutus，即 absolvere 的过去分词，意为“释放、宣告无罪；完成、结束；使分离”。"},{"era":"LATIN MORPHOLOGY","en":"Absolvere = ab 'off, away from' + solvere 'to loosen, untie, release, detach'. The literal image is 'loosened away from' every restraint.","cn":"absolvere = ab“离开、脱离”+ solvere“松开、解开、释放、拆开”。字面意象是“从一切约束中松开”。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Solvere is analysed as *se-lu-, from the reflexive pronoun *s(w)e- + *leu- 'to loosen, divide, cut apart'.","cn":"solvere 被分析为 *se-lu-，由反身代词 *s(w)e- 加词根 *leu-“松开、分开、切开”构成。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English extends the word through 'absolute power' (unchecked rule), 'absolute majority' (more than half), 'absolute zero' (the lowest temperature) and the grammar term 'absolute construction'.","cn":"现代英语把该词扩展到 absolute power（不受制约的统治）、absolute majority（超过半数）、absolute zero（最低温度）以及语法术语 absolute construction（独立结构）。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The spelling group shares the Latin participle ending -solute; the meaning group shares the idea of something without limits.","cn":"拼写组共享拉丁分词词尾 -solute；近义组共享“没有限制”的含义。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"resolute","ipa":"/ˈrezəluːt/","tag":"shared ending","definition":"firm and determined. It shares the -solute ending but means 'having a fixed purpose', almost the opposite of 'unlimited'.","definitionCN":"坚决的；有决心的。它同样以 -solute 结尾，但意思是“目标坚定”，几乎与“不受限制”相反。"},{"word":"dissolute","ipa":"/ˈdɪsəluːt/","tag":"shared ending","definition":"living in a morally loose way. The -solute ending here points to looseness of behavior, not absence of limits.","definitionCN":"放荡的；道德松懈的。这里的 -solute 指向行为上的松弛，而不是没有限制。"},{"word":"obsolete","ipa":"/ˈɒbsəliːt/","tag":"near sound","definition":"no longer used or useful. It sounds close to absolute but comes from a different Latin verb.","definitionCN":"过时的；不再使用的。它听起来接近 absolute，但来自另一个拉丁动词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"complete","ipa":"/kəmˈpliːt/","tag":"whole","definition":"having all the necessary parts; total. It stresses wholeness rather than freedom from limits.","definitionCN":"完整的；全部的。它强调“齐全”，而不是“不受限制”。"},{"word":"total","ipa":"/ˈtəʊtl/","tag":"whole amount","definition":"including everything; complete in amount. It is often interchangeable with absolute in the 'complete' sense.","definitionCN":"总的；全部的。在“完全”这一义项上常可与 absolute 互换。"},{"word":"unconditional","ipa":"/ˌʌnkənˈdɪʃənl/","tag":"no conditions","definition":"not limited by conditions or terms. It is close to absolute in the sense of 'with nothing attached'.","definitionCN":"无条件的；不受条件或条款限制的。在“没有附加条件”这一层上接近 absolute。"},{"word":"arbitrary","ipa":"/ˈɑːbɪtrəri/","tag":"unchecked power","definition":"based on personal will rather than reason or law; it is the negative side of absolute power.","definitionCN":"任意的；基于个人意志而非理性或法律的，是绝对权力负面的一面。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real etymology and real relatives: ab- 'away' + solvere 'loosen', with absolve, solution and dissolve in the same family.","cn":"真实词源与真实同族词：ab-“离开”+ solvere“松开”，absolve、solution、dissolve 都在同一词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"ab- 'away' + solvere 'loosen' = loosened away from every limit. That is the core of absolute.","cn":"ab-“离开”+ solvere“松开”=从一切限制中松开。这就是 absolute 的核心。"},{"en":"Absolve and solution share solvere: to absolve is to loosen someone from guilt, and a solution is a loosening of a difficulty.","cn":"absolve 和 solution 都共享 solvere：absolve 是把人从罪责中松开，solution 是把困难松开。"},{"en":"Absolute power is power with no legal knot holding it down.","cn":"absolute power 就是没有法律绳结把它捆住的权力。"},{"en":"An absolute majority is a complete share (more than half), not a relative plurality.","cn":"absolute majority 是完整的份额（超过半数），而不是相对的多数。"},{"en":"Absolute zero is the floor of temperature: a limit that cannot be gone below.","cn":"absolute zero 是温度的底：一条不能再往下的界限。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a rope tied around a box and a hand cutting every knot: absolute is the state after the last knot is cut.","cn":"想象一根绳子捆着一个箱子，一只手把所有绳结逐个剪断：absolute 就是最后一个结被剪断后的状态。"},{"en":"The same 'no knots' idea applies to power (no limits), truth (no comparison) and certainty (no doubt).","cn":"同一种“没有绳结”的意象可以用于权力（没有限制）、真理（没有比较）和确定性（没有怀疑）。"},{"en":"Once every relative tie is cut, what remains is complete and alone; that is the double feeling of absolute.","cn":"当一切相对的联系都被剪断，剩下的东西既完整又孤立；这就是 absolute 的双重感觉。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The witnesses gave an absolute account of what they saw.","cn":"目击者对所见之事给出了完全完整的叙述。"},{"en":"No government should have absolute control over the press.","cn":"任何政府都不应拥有对新闻界的绝对控制权。"},{"en":"The laboratory cooled the gas almost to absolute zero.","cn":"实验室把气体冷却到接近绝对零度。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿布索卢特”——阿布把绳子全部解开，不受任何限制 → absolute 绝对的、不受限制的","word":"absolute"},"root":"拉丁语 absolvere“解开、释放”，由 ab“离开”+ solvere“松开”构成，核心是“摆脱一切限制”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of absolute, all built on release: complete, unlimited, free of comparison, free of doubt, grammatically detached, politically unchecked, at the lowest limit, a majority over the whole, and a value without sign.","cn":"absolute 的九个义项都建立在“松开”上：完整无缺、权力不受限、脱离比较、脱离怀疑、语法上独立、政治上不受制衡、处于最低极限、按全体计算的多数，以及不带符号的数值。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: every knot is cut, so nothing outside can hold or limit it.","cn":"核心意象：所有绳结都被剪断，外部再没有任何东西能牵住或限制它。"},"chain":["BOUND","LOOSENED","COMPLETE","UNLIMITED","NOT RELATIVE","DETACHED AND CERTAIN"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"COMPLETE: nothing is held back or left out of the thing described.","cn":"完整：所描述之物没有任何保留或被漏掉的部分。"},{"senses":"02 · 06","en":"UNLIMITED POWER: the same absence of restraint is praised as sovereignty and feared as despotism, depending on who holds it.","cn":"无限的权力：同一种“没有约束”，既可能被赞为主权，也可能被惧为专制，取决于谁握着它。"},{"senses":"03 · 08 · 09","en":"FREE OF COMPARISON: not relative to anything, a majority measured against the whole, a value written without sign.","cn":"脱离比较：不与任何事物相对，按全体来量的多数，以及不带符号的数值。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"CERTAIN AND DETACHED: no doubt is left, and a phrase is cut loose from the main clause.","cn":"确定与独立：不留疑问，以及从主句上松开的一个短语。"},{"senses":"07","en":"THE FLOOR: the lowest limit a temperature can reach, below which nothing moves.","cn":"底线：温度能够到达的最低极限，再往下便没有任何运动。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Absolute is built on the Latin participle absolutus. English adds -ly and -ness, and makes the political nouns absolutism and absolutist.","cn":"absolute 建立在拉丁分词 absolutus 上。英语加 -ly 和 -ness，并构成政治名词 absolutism 与 absolutist。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on solvere 'loosen': absolve, solve, solution, dissolve and resolve all describe some kind of releasing or untying.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 solvere“松开”上：absolve、solve、solution、dissolve、resolve 都描述某种释放或解开。"},"items":[{"word":"absolutely","structure":"absolute + -ly","meaning":"completely; without doubt","meaningCN":"绝对地；完全地；毫无疑问（-ly 构成副词）","example":"You are absolutely right.","exampleCN":"你完全说得对。"},{"word":"absoluteness","structure":"absolute + -ness","meaning":"the quality of being absolute","meaningCN":"绝对性；完全性（-ness 构成性质名词）","example":"The absoluteness of the rule left no room for exceptions.","exampleCN":"这条规则的绝对性没有留下任何例外空间。"},{"word":"absolutism","structure":"absolute + -ism","meaning":"a system in which the ruler has unlimited power","meaningCN":"专制主义；绝对主义（-ism 表示制度或主张）","example":"Absolutism concentrated power in the monarchy.","exampleCN":"专制主义把权力集中在君主手中。"},{"word":"absolutist","structure":"absolute + -ist","meaning":"a supporter of unlimited rule","meaningCN":"专制主义者；绝对主义者（-ist 表示支持者）","example":"The absolutists rejected any written constitution.","exampleCN":"专制主义者拒绝任何成文宪法。"},{"word":"absolutistic","structure":"absolutist + -ic (relating to)","meaning":"relating to or favouring absolute rule","meaningCN":"绝对主义的（-ic 构成形容词）","example":"The party held an absolutistic view of authority.","exampleCN":"该党对权威持绝对主义观点。"},{"word":"absolutize","structure":"absolute + -ize (make)","meaning":"to treat something as absolute","meaningCN":"使绝对化（-ize 表示“使成为”）","example":"Do not absolutize a single experiment.","exampleCN":"不要把一次实验绝对化。"},{"word":"absolutization","structure":"absolutize + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of making something absolute","meaningCN":"绝对化（-ation 构成行为名词）","example":"The absolutization of the rule caused trouble.","exampleCN":"把规则绝对化带来了麻烦。"},{"word":"absolutive","structure":"absolute + -ive (relating to; grammatical case)","meaning":"a grammatical case marking the object of a transitive verb or the subject of an intransitive one","meaningCN":"绝对格（语法术语，-ive 构成形容词兼名词）","example":"Basque marks the object with the absolutive case.","exampleCN":"巴斯克语用绝对格标记宾语。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"absolve","structure":"ab- (away) + solvere (loosen)","meaning":"to declare someone free from guilt","meaningCN":"赦免；宣告无罪（把人从罪责中松开）"},{"word":"solve","structure":"solvere (loosen)","meaning":"to find the answer to a problem","meaningCN":"解决；解答（把难题“松开”）"},{"word":"solution","structure":"solvere + -tion","meaning":"an answer, or a liquid in which something is dissolved","meaningCN":"解决办法；溶液（两者都是“松开”的结果）"},{"word":"dissolve","structure":"dis- (apart) + solvere (loosen)","meaning":"to break apart into a liquid; to end an assembly","meaningCN":"溶解；解散（分开地松开）"},{"word":"resolve","structure":"re- (again, back) + solvere (loosen)","meaning":"to settle a problem or decide firmly","meaningCN":"解决；决心（重新松开并定下）"}]}},{"word":"absorb","ipa_uk":"/əbˈzɔːb/","ipa_us":"/əbˈzɔːrb/","definition_zh":"吸收；吸引；并入；承担","definition_en":"to take in a liquid, energy, or information, or to hold someone's attention completely","core_image":"海绵把周围的水吸进自己的孔隙里","scene":"桌上洒了一整滩水，旁边放着一块干海绵。 The sponge absorbed the whole puddle, and the table surface was dry again.","sceneCN":"这里 absorb 是「吸收液体」（第 1 个义项：把液体吸进内部）；句意：海绵吸走了整滩水，桌面重新变干。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"吸收（液体、光、热、声音等）"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"吸引（注意力）；使全神贯注"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"并入；同化；承担（费用）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"absorb water","zh":"吸收水分"},{"phrase":"absorb energy","zh":"吸收能量"},{"phrase":"be absorbed in","zh":"全神贯注于"},{"phrase":"absorb shock","zh":"缓冲震动；吸收冲击"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"absorbs"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"absorbed"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"absorbed"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"absorbing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"absorption","pos":"n.","zh":"吸收；同化；专注"},{"word":"absorbent","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"能吸收的；吸收剂"},{"word":"absorbed","pos":"adj.","zh":"全神贯注的；被吸收的"},{"word":"absorbing","pos":"adj.","zh":"引人入胜的；吸收的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Take in a liquid","titleCN":"吸收液体：把水吸进内部","definition":"to take in a liquid and hold it inside a material","definitionCN":"吸收液体并把它保存在材料内部","example":"The sponge absorbed all the water on the table.","exampleCN":"海绵把桌上的水都吸干了。","why":"Latin absorbere meant 'to swallow up'. The material opens its pores, the liquid enters, and it stays inside instead of remaining on the surface.","whyCN":"拉丁语 absorbere 意为“吞下”。材料张开孔隙，液体进入并留在内部，而不是停在表面。"},{"no":"02","title":"Take in energy, light, or sound","titleCN":"吸收能量、光或声音","definition":"to take in energy such as light, heat, or sound instead of reflecting or transmitting it","definitionCN":"吸收光、热或声等能量，而不是反射或透射","example":"Dark surfaces absorb more heat than light ones.","exampleCN":"深色表面比浅色表面吸收更多热量。","why":"The same 'taking in' works for energy. A surface receives the wave and converts it inside the material, so the energy does not bounce back.","whyCN":"同一种“吸入”也适用于能量。表面接收波，并在材料内部把它转化掉，所以能量不会反弹回来。"},{"no":"03","title":"Take in knowledge","titleCN":"吸收知识：把信息变成自己的","definition":"to take in and understand information, ideas, or experiences","definitionCN":"吸收并理解信息、想法或经验","example":"Children absorb new languages quickly.","exampleCN":"儿童吸收新语言很快。","why":"Information is liquid for the mind: it enters, is held, and becomes part of what the learner can use. Absorb makes learning feel like drinking rather than memorizing.","whyCN":"信息是心智的液体：它进入、被保存，并成为学习者可使用的一部分。absorb 让学习像“喝进去”，而不是“背下来”。"},{"no":"04","title":"Hold attention completely","titleCN":"完全吸引注意力","definition":"to interest someone so much that they give all their attention to it","definitionCN":"使某人极感兴趣，以致把所有注意力都放在其上","example":"She was absorbed in the book and did not hear the bell.","exampleCN":"她全神贯注于书中，没有听见铃声。","why":"Attention is a liquid too: the book takes it all in, leaving none on the surface for the room. Being absorbed means the mind has been drawn inside the task.","whyCN":"注意力也是一种液体：书把它全部吸进去，表面上不再留给房间任何一点。be absorbed 就是心智被拉进任务内部。"},{"no":"05","title":"Incorporate or assimilate","titleCN":"并入同化：让外来者成为内部一部分","definition":"to take in and make something part of a larger group or system","definitionCN":"吸收并使某物成为一个更大群体或系统的一部分","example":"The city absorbed the surrounding villages into its administration.","exampleCN":"这座城市把周边村庄并入了自己的行政体系。","why":"A larger body takes in a smaller one and makes it part of itself. What was outside becomes inside, just as liquid becomes part of the sponge.","whyCN":"较大的主体吸进较小的主体，并使其成为自身的一部分。原本在外的东西变成在内，就像液体成为海绵的一部分。"},{"no":"06","title":"Take in shock or impact","titleCN":"缓冲冲击：把力量吸收掉","definition":"to receive and reduce the force of a shock, impact, or change","definitionCN":"承受并减弱震动、冲击或变化的力量","example":"The thick walls absorb the shock of the explosion.","exampleCN":"厚墙吸收了爆炸的冲击。","why":"A shock is energy that must go somewhere. A material absorbs it by taking the force inside and spreading it out, so less reaches what it protects.","whyCN":"冲击是必须去某处的能量。材料把力量吸进内部并分散开，于是到达被保护对象的力就更少。"},{"no":"07","title":"Take on a cost or loss","titleCN":"承担成本或损失","definition":"to accept and deal with a cost, loss, or extra work","definitionCN":"接受并处理成本、损失或额外工作","example":"The company absorbed the extra shipping costs.","exampleCN":"公司承担了额外的运费。","why":"Money lost is like liquid that drains into a business instead of appearing on a bill. The one who absorbs it takes the loss inside and keeps the surface price unchanged.","whyCN":"损失的钱像液体，被企业吸进去，而不是出现在账单表面。承担者把损失收进内部，让表面价格保持不变。"},{"no":"08","title":"Business: take over a firm or unit","titleCN":"商业：兼并吸收公司或部门","definition":"to take over another company or unit so that it becomes part of the larger one","definitionCN":"接管另一家公司或部门，使其成为较大实体的一部分","example":"The group absorbed three small rivals in two years.","exampleCN":"该集团两年内吸收了三家小型竞争对手。","why":"A firm that is absorbed stops having a separate outline: its staff, contracts and name are drawn inside the buyer, exactly as liquid is drawn into a material.","whyCN":"被吸收的公司不再有独立轮廓：人员、合同与名称都被拉进买方内部，正如液体被吸进材料。"},{"no":"09","title":"Chemistry: take in a gas or solute","titleCN":"化学：吸收气体或溶质","definition":"of a solid or liquid, to take in and hold molecules of another substance, such as a gas","definitionCN":"固体或液体吸入并留住另一物质（如气体）的分子","example":"Activated carbon absorbs the gas from the air stream.","exampleCN":"活性炭吸收气流中的气体。","why":"This is the physical sense narrowed to molecules: the outside substance passes into the body of the material and stays there, which is why absorption can be measured by weight.","whyCN":"这是物理义收窄到分子层面：外部物质进入材料内部并留在那里，因此吸收量可以用重量来测。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Absorb came through French from Latin absorbere 'to swallow up'. The same root appears in absorption and absorbent, and the image has remained remarkably stable.","cn":"absorb 经由法语来自拉丁语 absorbere“吞下”。同一词根出现在 absorption 和 absorbent 中，意象至今非常稳定。"},"items":[{"era":"EARLY 15C.","en":"First recorded early 15c. meaning 'to drink in, suck up, take in by absorption'.","cn":"最早记录于 15 世纪早期，意为“吸入、吸干、通过吸收而纳入”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"From Old French absorbir / assorbir (13c., modern French absorber), from Latin absorbere.","cn":"来自古法语 absorbir / assorbir（13 世纪，现代法语 absorber），再往上为拉丁语 absorbere。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin absorbere 'to swallow up, devour' = ab 'off, away from' + sorbere 'suck in'.","cn":"拉丁语 absorbere“吞下、吞噬”= ab“离开、脱离”+ sorbere“吸进”。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Sorbere goes back to PIE *srebh- 'to suck, absorb', also linked to Armenian arbi 'I drank' and Greek rhopheo 'gulp down'.","cn":"sorbere 可追溯到原始印欧语 *srebh-“吸、吸收”，也与亚美尼亚语 arbi“我喝了”和希腊语 rhopheo“大口吞下”有关。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The figurative sense 'to occupy the attention completely' is recorded from 1763. Absorption is the noun, and absorbent appears in 1718.","cn":"比喻义“完全占据注意力”记录于 1763 年。名词是 absorption，absorbent 出现于 1718 年。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is about spelling and word shape; the second is about other ways of taking something in.","cn":"第一组看拼写和词形；第二组看其他“把东西纳入内部”的说法。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"adsorb","ipa":"/ədˈzɔːb/","tag":"one-letter difference","definition":"to hold molecules on a surface, not inside the material. The difference between absorb and adsorb is surface versus interior.","definitionCN":"把分子吸附在表面，而不是吸进材料内部。absorb 与 adsorb 的区别正是“内部”与“表面”。"},{"word":"absolve","ipa":"/əbˈzɒlv/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"to declare someone free from guilt. It shares ab- and the general shape but comes from solvere 'loosen'.","definitionCN":"赦免；宣告无罪。它同样以 ab- 开头、词形接近，但来自 solvere“松开”。"},{"word":"absorption","ipa":"/əbˈzɔːpʃn/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the noun from absorb: the process of taking something in.","definitionCN":"absorb 派生的名词：吸收的过程。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"ingest","ipa":"/ɪnˈdʒest/","tag":"into the body","definition":"to take food or a substance into the body. It is more specific and biological than absorb.","definitionCN":"摄入；把食物或物质吃进体内。它比 absorb 更具体、更偏生物语境。"},{"word":"assimilate","ipa":"/əˈsɪməleɪt/","tag":"into a system","definition":"to take in and make part of a larger system, especially people, ideas, or nutrients.","definitionCN":"吸收并成为更大系统的一部分，尤用于人、观念或营养。"},{"word":"soak up","ipa":"/səʊk ʌp/","tag":"phrasal verb","definition":"to take in liquid or information gradually, like a sponge. It is the everyday equivalent of one branch of absorb.","definitionCN":"吸收液体或信息，像海绵一样。它是 absorb 某一支的日常说法。"},{"word":"engross","ipa":"/ɪnˈɡrəʊs/","tag":"attention","definition":"to occupy someone's attention completely. It overlaps with be absorbed in but is more formal.","definitionCN":"使全神贯注。它与 be absorbed in 重叠，但更正式。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts and real relatives: ab- + sorbere 'suck', with absorption, absorbent and the Latin sorb- family.","cn":"真实构词与真实同族词：ab- + sorbere“吸”，以及 absorption、absorbent 和拉丁 sorb- 词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"ab- 'away' + sorbere 'suck in' = to suck something away into oneself. That is the physical core.","cn":"ab-“离开”+ sorbere“吸进”=把东西吸进自己体内。这就是它的物理核心。"},{"en":"Absorption is the noun and absorbent is the adjective or material: a paper towel is absorbent.","cn":"absorption 是名词，absorbent 是形容词或材料名：纸巾就是 absorbent。"},{"en":"Be absorbed in a book means the book has taken all your attention inside it.","cn":"“be absorbed in a book”意思是书把你的注意力全部吸进去了。"},{"en":"Adsorb is the surface cousin: molecules stick to the outside instead of entering the inside.","cn":"adsorb 是“表面”表亲：分子黏在外面，而不是进入内部。"},{"en":"A business absorbs costs the way a sponge absorbs water: the loss goes inside and the surface price stays the same.","cn":"企业承担成本就像海绵吸水：损失进入内部，表面价格保持不变。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a sponge: dry and full of holes, then heavy and quiet after it drinks. Absorb is that change from empty to filled.","cn":"想象一块海绵：干的时候满是孔洞，吸饱水后变得沉重而安静。absorb 就是从“空”到“满”的变化。"},{"en":"The same filling can happen to a mind (knowledge), an eye (light), an ear (sound), or an organization (people).","cn":"同一种“填满”可以发生在心智（知识）、眼睛（光）、耳朵（声音）或组织（人）上。"},{"en":"What is absorbed stops being outside: it becomes part of the thing that took it in.","cn":"被吸收的东西不再属于外部：它成为吸入者自身的一部分。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"This soil absorbs rainwater slowly.","cn":"这种土壤吸水很慢。"},{"en":"The audience was absorbed in the performance.","cn":"观众全神贯注于演出。"},{"en":"The firm absorbed the smaller company last year.","cn":"这家公司去年兼并了那家较小的公司。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿布佐布”——阿布把水全部吸进布里 → absorb 吸收","word":"absorb"},"root":"拉丁语 ab“离开”+ sorbere“吸进”，核心是“把外部之物吸进内部”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of absorb, all one movement from outside to inside: liquid, energy, information, attention, a group, a firm, shock, cost, and a gas held in a solid.","cn":"absorb 的九个义项都是同一种“由外到内”的运动：液体、能量、信息、注意力、群体、公司、冲击、成本，以及被固体留住的气体。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a porous material draws something from outside into itself.","cn":"核心意象：多孔材料把外部之物吸进自身。"},"chain":["OUTSIDE","SUCK IN","HOLD INSIDE","ASSIMILATE","TAKE THE FORCE OR COST","SWALLOW WHOLLY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"MATTER AND ENERGY: liquid into a material, and light, heat or sound into a surface.","cn":"物质与能量：液体进入材料，光、热或声音进入表面。"},{"senses":"03","en":"KNOWLEDGE: information enters a mind and becomes usable there.","cn":"知识：信息进入心智，并在那里变得可用。"},{"senses":"04","en":"ATTENTION: the whole mind is taken up by one task, leaving nothing outside it.","cn":"注意力：整个心智被一项任务占满，外面什么都不剩。"},{"senses":"05 · 08","en":"FOLDED IN: a group is assimilated and a firm is taken over until neither has an outline of its own.","cn":"被折进内部：群体被同化，公司被兼并，直到两者都不再有独立轮廓。"},{"senses":"06 · 07 · 09","en":"WHAT IS HELD AND KEPT: shock, cost and gas are each taken in and stay inside, and chemistry makes the holding measurable.","cn":"被吸入并留住的东西：冲击、成本与气体都被吸入并留在内部，化学则让这种留持可以计量。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Absorb forms absorption with -tion and absorbent with -ent; absorbing works as both a participle and an adjective meaning 'very interesting'.","cn":"absorb 用 -tion 构成 absorption，用 -ent 构成 absorbent；absorbing 既是分词，也可作形容词表示“引人入胜的”。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on sorbere 'suck in': adsorb (surface), resorb (absorb again), and sorption are the scientific relatives.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 sorbere“吸进”上：adsorb（表面吸附）、resorb（再吸收）和 sorption 是它的科学同族词。"},"items":[{"word":"absorption","structure":"absorb + -tion","meaning":"the process of taking something in","meaningCN":"吸收；专注（-tion 构成过程名词）","example":"The absorption of water by the soil takes time.","exampleCN":"土壤吸收水分需要时间。"},{"word":"absorbent","structure":"absorb + -ent","meaning":"able to take in liquid","meaningCN":"能吸收的；吸收剂（-ent 构成形容词或名词）","example":"Use an absorbent cloth to dry the surface.","exampleCN":"用一块吸水的布擦干表面。"},{"word":"absorbing","structure":"absorb + -ing","meaning":"holding attention; very interesting","meaningCN":"引人入胜的；吸收的（-ing 构成形容词）","example":"The lecture was surprisingly absorbing.","exampleCN":"这场讲座出人意料地引人入胜。"},{"word":"absorbency","structure":"absorb + -ency","meaning":"the quality of being able to absorb liquid","meaningCN":"吸水性；吸收能力","example":"The towel's absorbency decreased after many washes.","exampleCN":"洗了很多次之后，毛巾的吸水性下降了。"},{"word":"absorbable","structure":"absorb + -able (able to be)","meaning":"capable of being taken in by a body or surface","meaningCN":"可吸收的（-able 表示“可以被……”）","example":"The new stitches are fully absorbable.","exampleCN":"这种新缝线可以被完全吸收。"},{"word":"absorber","structure":"absorb + -er (thing that does)","meaning":"a device or material that takes in energy or liquid","meaningCN":"吸收器；吸收体（-er 表示施事者）","example":"The shock absorber was replaced last month.","exampleCN":"减震器上个月换过了。"},{"word":"absorbate","structure":"absorb + -ate (thing acted upon; technical term)","meaning":"the substance that has been absorbed","meaningCN":"被吸收物（-ate 表示受事的技术名词）","example":"Chemists measured the absorbate on the filter.","exampleCN":"化学家测量了滤纸上的被吸收物。"},{"word":"absorptive","structure":"absorb + -ive (tending to)","meaning":"having the power to absorb","meaningCN":"有吸收力的（-ive 表示倾向于）","example":"The absorptive layer holds moisture well.","exampleCN":"这一吸收层保水性很好。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"adsorb","structure":"ad- (to) + sorbere (suck)","meaning":"to hold molecules on a surface","meaningCN":"吸附（把分子吸在表面，而不是吸进内部）"},{"word":"resorb","structure":"re- (again) + sorbere (suck)","meaning":"to absorb again, especially in the body","meaningCN":"再吸收（尤指身体重新吸收物质）"}]}},{"word":"abstract","ipa_uk":"/ˈæbstrækt/","ipa_us":"/ˈæbstrækt/","definition_zh":"抽象的；摘要；提取","definition_en":"existing as an idea rather than a physical thing; a summary; to take something out or separate it","core_image":"把本质从具体事物里抽出来，只剩骨架","scene":"美术馆里，观众站在一幅只有色块的画前。 The visitor stood in front of a painting made only of colored blocks, and the label beside it said abstract art.","sceneCN":"这里 abstract 是「抽象的」（第 2 个义项：抽象艺术）；句意：观众站在一幅只有色块的画前，旁边的展签写着抽象艺术。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"抽象的；理论上的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"摘要；抽象概念"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"提取；抽取；概括（动词重音为 /əbˈstrækt/）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"abstract concept","zh":"抽象概念"},{"phrase":"abstract art","zh":"抽象艺术"},{"phrase":"in the abstract","zh":"抽象地；在理论上"},{"phrase":"abstract from","zh":"从……中提取／概括出"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"abstracts"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"abstracted"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"abstracted"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"abstracting"},{"label":"比较级（形容词，用 more）","form":"more abstract"},{"label":"最高级（形容词，用 most）","form":"most abstract"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"abstraction","pos":"n.","zh":"抽象；抽象概念；提取"},{"word":"abstractly","pos":"adv.","zh":"抽象地"},{"word":"abstracted","pos":"adj.","zh":"心不在焉的；被提取的"},{"word":"abstractionism","pos":"n.","zh":"抽象主义（艺术流派）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Existing as an idea, not a physical thing","titleCN":"抽象的：只作为概念存在","definition":"existing as an idea or quality rather than as a physical object","definitionCN":"作为观念或性质存在，而不是作为实体物件存在","example":"Freedom is an abstract idea until it is taken away.","exampleCN":"自由在被剥夺之前，只是一个抽象观念。","why":"Latin abstrahere meant 'to draw away'. The mind draws the quality out of the object and keeps it alone, so justice, beauty and freedom can be thought without any one physical thing.","whyCN":"拉丁语 abstrahere 意为“抽走”。心智把性质从事物中抽出来，单独保留它，因此正义、美、自由可以被思考，而不必依附于某个具体物件。"},{"no":"02","title":"Abstract art: form without a real model","titleCN":"抽象艺术：不描摹实物","definition":"art that does not try to represent recognisable objects, but uses shapes, colours, and forms","definitionCN":"不试图再现可辨认物体的艺术，而使用形状、颜色和形式","example":"The gallery devoted a whole room to abstract art.","exampleCN":"美术馆用整整一个展厅陈列抽象艺术。","why":"If the subject has been drawn away, what remains is the visual structure itself. Abstract art keeps the colour and shape but removes the recognisable object.","whyCN":"如果对象被抽走，剩下的就是视觉结构本身。抽象艺术保留颜色和形状，却去掉了可辨认的物件。"},{"no":"03","title":"A summary of a longer work","titleCN":"摘要：从长文中抽出要点","definition":"a short summary of the main points of a paper, article, or book","definitionCN":"论文、文章或书籍要点的简短概括","example":"Read the abstract before the full paper.","exampleCN":"先读摘要，再读全文。","why":"A summary is what the mind draws out of a long text. The essential points are separated from the detail, exactly as the verb abstrahere separates a part from the whole.","whyCN":"摘要就是心智从长文中抽出的东西。要点被从细节中分离出来，正如动词 abstrahere 把部分从整体中分离。"},{"no":"04","title":"Remove or take out","titleCN":"提取：把某物拿走","definition":"to remove something from a place or source, often in a technical process","definitionCN":"从某处或某来源取出某物，常用于技术过程","example":"The process abstracts a metal from the ore.","exampleCN":"这个过程从矿石中提取金属。","why":"Here the Latin 'draw away' is physical again: something is pulled out of the mass that contains it. The object is separated and taken elsewhere.","whyCN":"这里拉丁语的“抽走”又回到物理层面：某物被从包含它的整体中拉出来，被分离并拿到别处。"},{"no":"05","title":"Generalize from particulars","titleCN":"概括：从具体中提炼一般","definition":"to separate a general idea or pattern from specific examples","definitionCN":"从具体例子中分离出一般观念或模式","example":"We can abstract a rule from these cases.","exampleCN":"我们可以从这些案例中概括出一条规则。","why":"The mind draws the common pattern out of many examples and leaves the details behind. This is the intellectual version of extracting metal from ore.","whyCN":"心智从许多例子中抽出共同模式，把细节留在后面。这是“从矿石中提取金属”的智力版本。"},{"no":"06","title":"Abstracted: absent-minded","titleCN":"心不在焉：心思被抽走","definition":"in the adjective abstracted, with the mind somewhere else","definitionCN":"形容词 abstracted 表示心思在别处、心不在焉","example":"He looked abstracted and did not answer.","exampleCN":"他看起来心不在焉，没有回答。","why":"If attention can be drawn away from the room, the person left behind looks abstracted. The mind has been extracted from the present situation.","whyCN":"如果注意力能被从房间里抽走，留下的人看起来就心不在焉。心智被从当前情境中抽离了。"},{"no":"07","title":"Grammar: abstract noun","titleCN":"语法：抽象名词","definition":"in grammar, an abstract noun names a quality, state, or idea rather than a physical thing","definitionCN":"语法中，抽象名词命名性质、状态或观念，而不是实体物件","example":"Happiness and courage are abstract nouns.","exampleCN":"happiness 和 courage 都是抽象名词。","why":"Grammar uses the same separation: the noun names what has been drawn out of things, not the things themselves.","whyCN":"语法使用同一种分离：这类名词命名的是从事物中抽出的东西，而不是事物本身。"},{"no":"08","title":"Computing: defined without an implementation","titleCN":"计算机：只定义、不实现","definition":"in programming, describing a type or class that states behaviour without providing a working implementation","definitionCN":"编程中指只声明行为、不提供可运行实现的类型或类","example":"An abstract class cannot be instantiated on its own.","exampleCN":"抽象类不能单独实例化。","why":"The concrete code is drawn away and only the shape of the behaviour is left: the class exists as a specification, and the running body must be supplied elsewhere.","whyCN":"具体的代码被抽走，只留下行为的形状：这个类作为规格存在，真正运行的实体要在别处提供。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Abstract comes from Latin abstrahere 'to draw away'. The word was first used in grammar, then for summaries, then for ideas separated from physical things.","cn":"abstract 来自拉丁语 abstrahere“抽走”。这个词先用于语法，再指摘要，最后指从实体事物中分离出来的观念。"},"items":[{"era":"LATE 14C.","en":"First recorded late 14c. in grammar, for a noun that does not name a concrete thing. The noun 'summary' is mid-15c.; the verb appears in the 1540s.","cn":"最早记录于 14 世纪晚期，用于语法中不命名具体事物的名词。名词义“摘要”见于 15 世纪中期；动词义出现于 16 世纪 40 年代。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"From Latin abstractus 'drawn away', past participle of abstrahere 'to drag away, detach, pull away, divert'.","cn":"来自拉丁语 abstractus“被抽走的”，即 abstrahere“拖走、分离、拉走、转移”的过去分词。"},{"era":"LATIN MORPHOLOGY","en":"Abstrahere = abs- (a form of ab 'off, away from') + trahere 'to draw'.","cn":"abstrahere = abs-（ab“离开、脱离”的变体）+ trahere“拉、拖”。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Trahere is traced by Watkins to PIE *tragh- 'to draw, drag, move', with a possible variant *dhragh-. The reconstruction is attributed to Watkins, so this link is source uncertain.","cn":"Watkins 把 trahere 追溯到原始印欧语 *tragh-“拉、拖、移动”，并提到可能的变体 *dhragh-。该重构归于 Watkins，故此环节来源不确定。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps the grammar term abstract noun, the summary sense, the verb 'extract', and the adjective 'not concrete'. Abstracted adds the sense 'with the mind elsewhere'.","cn":"现代英语保留语法术语 abstract noun、摘要义、动词“提取”义，以及形容词“非具体”义。abstracted 另增加“心不在焉”的含义。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is about spelling and the shared -tract shape; the second is about ideas that are separated from concrete things.","cn":"第一组看拼写与共同的 -tract 词形；第二组看“从具体事物中分离出来的观念”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"abstruse","ipa":"/æbˈstruːs/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"hard to understand. It looks close to abstract but means 'difficult', not 'separated from reality'.","definitionCN":"深奥难懂的。它词形接近 abstract，但意思是“难懂”，而不是“脱离现实”。"},{"word":"extract","ipa":"/ɪkˈstrækt/","tag":"same Latin verb","definition":"to take something out. It shares the Latin verb trahere 'draw' and is close to the 'remove' sense of abstract.","definitionCN":"提取；取出。它共享拉丁动词 trahere“拉”，接近 abstract 的“取出”义。"},{"word":"abstracted","ipa":"/æbˈstræktɪd/","tag":"derived form","definition":"the past participle used as an adjective: absorbed in thought, or physically removed.","definitionCN":"过去分词作形容词：陷入沉思的，或已被提取的。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"conceptual","ipa":"/kənˈseptʃuəl/","tag":"idea-based","definition":"based on ideas or concepts rather than physical things; close to abstract in the idea sense.","definitionCN":"概念性的；基于观念而非实物的，在“观念”义上接近 abstract。"},{"word":"theoretical","ipa":"/ˌθɪəˈretɪkl/","tag":"not practical","definition":"based on theory rather than practice; it often contrasts with practical rather than with physical.","definitionCN":"理论上的；基于理论而非实践的，常与 practical 相对，而不是与 physical 相对。"},{"word":"summary","ipa":"/ˈsʌməri/","tag":"short account","definition":"a short statement of the main points; the everyday equivalent of an abstract of a paper.","definitionCN":"摘要；要点的简短陈述，是论文 abstract 的日常同义词。"},{"word":"abstruse","ipa":"/æbˈstruːs/","tag":"hard to grasp","definition":"difficult to understand because it is remote from everyday experience.","definitionCN":"深奥的；因远离日常经验而难以理解的。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real etymology and real relatives: abs- 'away' + trahere 'draw', with extract, contract, attract and distract in the same family.","cn":"真实词源与真实同族词：abs-“离开”+ trahere“拉”，extract、contract、attract、distract 都在同一词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"abs- 'away' + trahere 'draw' = drawn away. An abstract idea is what remains after the physical details are drawn off.","cn":"abs-“离开”+ trahere“拉”=被抽走。抽象观念就是物理细节被抽走后剩下的东西。"},{"en":"Extract, contract, attract and distract all contain trahere 'draw': to pull out, pull together, pull toward, pull apart.","cn":"extract、contract、attract、distract 都含有 trahere“拉”：拉出、拉合、拉向、拉开。"},{"en":"An abstract of a paper is the part the mind draws out of the full text.","cn":"论文的 abstract 就是心智从全文中抽出的那部分。"},{"en":"Abstract art keeps colour and shape but draws away the recognisable object.","cn":"抽象艺术保留颜色和形状，却把可辨认的物件抽走。"},{"en":"Abstracted looks like the past participle because the mind has been 'drawn away' from the room.","cn":"abstracted 看起来像过去分词，因为心智被从房间里“抽走”了。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a chair reduced to a wire frame: the shape remains, the material is gone. Abstract thinking keeps the frame and drops the chair.","cn":"想象一把椅子被简化成铁丝骨架：形状还在，材料没了。抽象思维保留骨架，放下椅子本身。"},{"en":"The drawing-away can produce an idea, a summary, a metal extracted from ore, or a general rule taken from cases.","cn":"这种“抽走”可以产生一个观念、一份摘要、从矿石中提取的金属，或从案例中抽出的一般规则。"},{"en":"If the mind itself is drawn away from the present, the person looks abstracted; the same arrow now points inward.","cn":"如果心智本身被从当下抽走，这个人看起来就心不在焉；同一个箭头现在指向内部。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The concept of justice is abstract but still shapes real courts.","cn":"正义的概念是抽象的，却仍塑造着真实的法庭。"},{"en":"Please send an abstract of the report by Friday.","cn":"请在周五前发来报告摘要。"},{"en":"The machine abstracts water from the air.","cn":"这台机器从空气中提取水。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿布斯特拉克特”——阿布把具体外壳剥掉，只剩概念骨架 → abstract 抽象的","word":"abstract"},"root":"拉丁语 abs“离开”+ trahere“拉”，字面义“抽走、拉开”，核心是“从具体中抽出本质”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of abstract, all one gesture of drawing away: an idea from things, form from a model, a summary from a text, metal from ore, a rule from cases, the mind from the room, a noun from a quality, and a class from its implementation.","cn":"abstract 的八个义项都是同一个“抽走”动作：从事物抽出观念、从实物抽出形式、从全文抽出摘要、从矿石抽出金属、从案例抽出规则、从房间抽走心智、从性质抽出名词、从实现体抽出类。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: draw the essential part away and leave the concrete shell behind.","cn":"核心意象：把本质部分抽走，把具体外壳留在后面。"},"chain":["DRAW","AWAY","SEPARATE","NON-PHYSICAL","SUMMARY","THE MIND ELSEWHERE"],"branches":[{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"DRAWING OUT: metal from ore, and the general rule pulled from particular cases.","cn":"抽出来：从矿石中取出金属，从具体个案中提炼一般规则。"},{"senses":"02 · 08","en":"FORM WITHOUT A MODEL: art with no real subject, and a class with no implementation.","cn":"没有原型的形：不描摹实物的艺术，以及没有实现体的类。"},{"senses":"01 · 07","en":"THE NON-PHYSICAL: an idea rather than a thing, and the noun that names such a quality.","cn":"非实体：作为观念而非实物存在，以及用来指称这类性质的名词。"},{"senses":"03","en":"THE SUMMARY: the short text drawn from the long one, keeping what matters.","cn":"摘要：从长文里抽出的短文，只留下要紧的部分。"},{"senses":"06","en":"MIND ELSEWHERE: attention abstracted from the room while the body stays.","cn":"心思不在场：注意力从房间里被抽走，身体却还留着。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Abstract forms abstraction with -tion and abstractly with -ly; abstracted and abstractionism show how the participle and the art movement branch off.","cn":"abstract 用 -tion 构成 abstraction，用 -ly 构成 abstractly；abstracted 和 abstractionism 展示了分词与艺术流派的分支。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on trahere 'to draw': tract, attract, contract, extract, distract and subtract all describe pulling in different directions.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 trahere“拉”上：tract、attract、contract、extract、distract、subtract 都描述不同方向的“拉”。"},"items":[{"word":"abstraction","structure":"abstract + -tion","meaning":"the act of abstracting; an abstract idea","meaningCN":"抽象；抽象观念（-tion 构成行为或结果名词）","example":"The abstraction of the model makes it hard to apply.","exampleCN":"这个模型过于抽象，难以应用。"},{"word":"abstractly","structure":"abstract + -ly","meaning":"in an abstract way","meaningCN":"抽象地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"He spoke abstractly about justice.","exampleCN":"他抽象地谈论正义。"},{"word":"abstracted","structure":"abstract + -ed","meaning":"lost in thought; or removed","meaningCN":"心不在焉的；被提取的（-ed 构成形容词）","example":"She gave an abstracted smile.","exampleCN":"她心不在焉地笑了笑。"},{"word":"abstractionism","structure":"abstraction + -ism","meaning":"an art movement that avoids representing real objects","meaningCN":"抽象主义（避免再现真实物体的艺术流派）","example":"Abstractionism dominated the gallery in the 1950s.","exampleCN":"二十世纪五十年代，抽象主义主导了这家美术馆。"},{"word":"abstractness","structure":"abstract + -ness (quality)","meaning":"the quality of being abstract","meaningCN":"抽象性（-ness 构成抽象名词）","example":"Critics debated the abstractness of his later work.","exampleCN":"批评家议论他后期作品的抽象性。"},{"word":"abstractive","structure":"abstract + -ive (tending to)","meaning":"tending to draw away or summarize","meaningCN":"抽离的；抽象化的（-ive 表示倾向于）","example":"Reading is an abstractive act.","exampleCN":"阅读是一种抽象化的行为。"},{"word":"abstractionist","structure":"abstraction + -ist (person who)","meaning":"an artist who works in abstraction","meaningCN":"抽象派艺术家（-ist 表示人）","example":"The gallery showed three abstractionists from the 1950s.","exampleCN":"画廊展出了三位二十世纪五十年代的抽象派画家。"},{"word":"abstractedly","structure":"abstracted + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in an absent-minded, distracted way","meaningCN":"心不在焉地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"He nodded abstractedly at the question.","exampleCN":"他心不在焉地对那个问题点了点头。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"tract","structure":"trahere (draw)","meaning":"an area of land; also a short written work","meaningCN":"地带；短文（两者都与“拉、延展”有关）"},{"word":"attract","structure":"ad- (to) + trahere (draw)","meaning":"to draw something toward oneself","meaningCN":"吸引（把某物拉向自己）"},{"word":"contract","structure":"con- (together) + trahere (draw)","meaning":"to draw together; a binding agreement","meaningCN":"收缩；合同（把双方拉到一起）"},{"word":"extract","structure":"ex- (out) + trahere (draw)","meaning":"to draw something out","meaningCN":"提取；拔出（把某物拉出来）"},{"word":"distract","structure":"dis- (apart) + trahere (draw)","meaning":"to draw attention apart from the task","meaningCN":"分散注意力（把注意力拉开）"}]}},{"word":"abundant","ipa_uk":"/əˈbʌndənt/","ipa_us":"/əˈbʌndənt/","definition_zh":"丰富的；大量的；充足的","definition_en":"existing in large quantities; more than enough","core_image":"水从容器里满出来，越过边缘往外流","scene":"果园里苹果堆满一排木箱，园主站在旁边。 The apple harvest was so abundant that the boxes filled a whole row of wooden crates.","sceneCN":"这里 abundant 是「充足的、大量的」（第 1 个义项：数量很多）；句意：苹果收成十分充足，装箱后摆满了整整一排木箱。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"大量的；丰富的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"富于……的；盛产……的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"abundant resources","zh":"丰富的资源"},{"phrase":"abundant evidence","zh":"大量证据"},{"phrase":"abundant rainfall","zh":"充沛的降雨"},{"phrase":"abundant in","zh":"富于……；盛产……"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more abundant"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most abundant"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"abundance","pos":"n.","zh":"丰富；充裕；大量"},{"word":"abundantly","pos":"adv.","zh":"大量地；丰富地"},{"word":"abound","pos":"v.","zh":"大量存在；富于"},{"word":"overabundant","pos":"adj.","zh":"过于丰富的；过剩的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Present in large quantities","titleCN":"大量存在：数量很多","definition":"existing in large quantities; plentiful","definitionCN":"大量存在；数量充足","example":"The region has abundant fruit in autumn.","exampleCN":"这个地区秋天水果很多。","why":"Latin abundare meant 'overflow, run over', from unda 'a wave'. The image is a container so full that its contents pour over the edge, which is why abundant means more than can be held.","whyCN":"拉丁语 abundare 意为“溢出、漫出”，来自 unda“波浪”。意象是一个容器满到内容物越过边缘流出来，因此 abundant 表示“多到装不下”。"},{"no":"02","title":"More than enough","titleCN":"充足：超过所需","definition":"more than enough for a need or purpose","definitionCN":"对某种需要或目的而言足够有余","example":"There is abundant time to finish the work.","exampleCN":"有充足的时间完成这项工作。","why":"The overflow is measured against a need. When the supply passes the fill line, the surplus is what makes it abundant rather than merely sufficient.","whyCN":"溢出是相对于需求来衡量的。当供应越过“满线”，多出来的部分才使它成为“充足有余”，而不只是“够用”。"},{"no":"03","title":"Rich in a quality","titleCN":"富于某种性质","definition":"having a great deal of a particular quality or element","definitionCN":"具有大量某种性质或成分","example":"The soil is abundant in minerals.","exampleCN":"这片土壤富含矿物质。","why":"What overflows need not be water. A place or material can pour over with a quality, so abundant in means 'full of' that element.","whyCN":"溢出的不一定是水。一个地方或材料也可以“溢出”某种性质，所以 abundant in 表示富含那种成分。"},{"no":"04","title":"Producing plentiful crops","titleCN":"丰产：产出很多","definition":"producing a large amount of crops, fruit, or goods","definitionCN":"产出大量庄稼、水果或商品","example":"The valley is an abundant farming area.","exampleCN":"这个山谷是丰产的农业区。","why":"A harvest is a container filled by the land. When the land fills it past the brim, the area itself is called abundant.","whyCN":"收成是土地装满的容器。当土地把它装到漫出边缘，这个地区本身就被称为“丰产的”。"},{"no":"05","title":"Naturally plentiful","titleCN":"自然资源丰富","definition":"having large natural supplies of water, oil, forest, or other resources","definitionCN":"拥有大量水、石油、森林等自然资源","example":"The country is abundant in oil and gas.","exampleCN":"这个国家石油和天然气资源丰富。","why":"Nature can be the container. A country whose reserves overflow its needs is abundant in those resources, even if the word does not say they are used well.","whyCN":"自然也可以是那个容器。一个国家的储量漫过自身需求，就在这些资源上 abundant，尽管这个词并不说明它们是否被善用。"},{"no":"06","title":"Ecology: high abundance","titleCN":"生态学：丰度高","definition":"in ecology, present in high numbers within a community or habitat","definitionCN":"生态学中，在某个群落或栖息地内数量很多","example":"The species is abundant in the shallow water.","exampleCN":"这个物种在浅水中数量很多。","why":"Ecologists count individuals per area. When the count runs over the expected level, the species is abundant; the word becomes a measurable technical label.","whyCN":"生态学家按单位面积计数个体。当数量超过预期水平，这个物种就是 abundant；这个词变成了可测量的技术标签。"},{"no":"07","title":"Mathematics: a number above its divisors","titleCN":"数学：真因数之和大于自身的数","definition":"of a number, having proper divisors whose sum is greater than the number itself","definitionCN":"指真因数之和大于该数本身的正整数","example":"Twelve is an abundant number because its proper divisors add up to sixteen.","exampleCN":"十二是盈数，因为它的真因数之和为十六。","why":"The surplus image turns into an exact test: the parts are added up and shown to exceed the whole, so the number is literally more than itself.","whyCN":"盈余的意象变成一个精确判断：把各部分加起来，结果超过整体，于是这个数“多于自己”。"},{"no":"08","title":"Finance: ample money in a market","titleCN":"金融：市场资金充裕","definition":"of money or credit, available in such supply that borrowing is easy","definitionCN":"指资金或信贷供给充足，借贷十分容易","example":"Cheap credit kept liquidity abundant for a decade.","exampleCN":"廉价信贷使流动性充裕了十年。","why":"A market is a container: when money flows in faster than it is used, the level rises past need and the supply becomes abundant in the plain physical sense.","whyCN":"市场是一个容器：资金流入快于消耗时，水位超过所需，供给就像字面上的“漫出”那样充裕。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Abundant came into English from French and Latin at the same time. Its core image is water overflowing a full container, and the root is unda 'wave'.","cn":"abundant 同时从法语和拉丁语进入英语。它的核心意象是水从满容器里溢出，词根是 unda“波浪”。"},"items":[{"era":"LATE 14C.","en":"First recorded late 14c. meaning 'present in great quantity, plentiful'.","cn":"最早记录于 14 世纪晚期，意为“大量存在、丰富”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH AND LATIN","en":"Borrowed from Old French abundant and Latin abundantem (nominative abundans) 'overflowing, full; rich, abounding', the present participle of abundare.","cn":"同时借自法语 abundant 和拉丁语 abundantem（主格 abundans）“溢出的、满的；富足的”，即 abundare 的现在分词。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"Abundare 'overflow, run over' = ab 'off, away from' + undare 'rise in a wave', from unda 'a wave'.","cn":"abundare“溢出、漫出”= ab“离开、向外”+ undare“像波浪般涌起”，后者来自 unda“波浪”。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Unda is a nasalized form of PIE *wed- (1) 'water; wet', the same root behind water and wet.","cn":"unda 是原始印欧语 *wed-（1）“水、湿”的鼻化形式，water 和 wet 也出自这个词根。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"English keeps abundant for quantity and for 'rich in' (abundant in minerals). The verb abound and the noun abundance carry the same overflow image.","cn":"英语用 abundant 表示数量，也表示“富含”（abundant in minerals）。动词 abound 和名词 abundance 承载同一个溢出意象。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Spelling neighbours are separated from words that also mean 'more than enough'.","cn":"拼写相近词与同样表示“足够有余”的词分开列出。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"abundance","ipa":"/əˈbʌndəns/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the noun from abundant: a large quantity or a state of plenty.","definitionCN":"abundant 派生的名词：大量或充裕的状态。"},{"word":"abandon","ipa":"/əˈbændən/","tag":"spelling","definition":"to leave or give up. It shares ab- and a similar rhythm but has nothing to do with plenty.","definitionCN":"放弃；遗弃。它同样以 ab- 开头、节奏相似，但与“丰富”毫无关系。"},{"word":"abound","ipa":"/əˈbaʊnd/","tag":"same family","definition":"to exist in large numbers; the verb behind abundant.","definitionCN":"大量存在；是 abundant 背后的动词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"plentiful","ipa":"/ˈplentɪfl/","tag":"everyday","definition":"available in large amounts; the everyday synonym closest to abundant.","definitionCN":"大量的；充足的，是最接近 abundant 的日常同义词。"},{"word":"ample","ipa":"/ˈæmpl/","tag":"enough and more","definition":"enough or more than enough for a purpose; often used for space or time.","definitionCN":"充足的；足够的，常用于空间或时间。"},{"word":"copious","ipa":"/ˈkəʊpiəs/","tag":"formal quantity","definition":"produced or supplied in large amounts; formal and often used with notes or detail.","definitionCN":"大量的；丰富的，较正式，常与笔记、细节搭配。"},{"word":"profuse","ipa":"/prəˈfjuːs/","tag":"excessive plenty","definition":"given or produced in very large amounts, sometimes more than is wanted.","definitionCN":"大量的；过多的，有时超过所需。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts and real relatives: ab- 'away/out' + unda 'wave', with abound, abundance and inundate in the same family.","cn":"真实构词与真实同族词：ab-“向外”+ unda“波浪”，abound、abundance、inundate 都在同一词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"Abundant is 'overflowing': a full container whose contents run over the edge.","cn":"abundant 就是“溢出”：装满的容器，内容物漫过边缘。"},{"en":"Abound is the verb and abundance the noun; all three keep the same wave image.","cn":"abound 是动词，abundance 是名词；三者都保留同一个波浪意象。"},{"en":"Inundate 'flood' belongs here too: water rising in waves until it covers everything.","cn":"inundate“淹没”也属于这里：水以波浪涌起，直到覆盖一切。"},{"en":"Abundant in minerals is a fixed pattern: the thing that overflows is a quality, not water.","cn":"abundant in minerals 是固定搭配：溢出的不是水，而是一种成分。"},{"en":"Water and wet share the same PIE root *wed- as unda, so the word is literally about water at its deepest level.","cn":"water、wet 与 unda 共享原始印欧语词根 *wed-，所以这个词在最深层字面上就是关于水的。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a cup filled past the brim and water running down the side: that overflow is abundance.","cn":"想象一只杯子倒水超过杯沿，水顺着杯壁流下：这种溢出就是“充裕”。"},{"en":"The cup can hold fruit, time, evidence, minerals or animals; whatever runs over is abundant.","cn":"杯子里可以装水果、时间、证据、矿物或动物；无论什么溢出，都是 abundant。"},{"en":"Abundance is not the same as usefulness: a country can be abundant in oil and still waste it.","cn":"充裕不等于善用：一个国家可以石油丰富，却仍然浪费它。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The forest is abundant in birds and insects.","cn":"这片森林鸟类和昆虫丰富。"},{"en":"We had abundant food for the long journey.","cn":"我们有充足的食物应付长途旅行。"},{"en":"Fish were abundant in the river before the dam was built.","cn":"建坝之前，河里的鱼很多。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿班登特”——阿班的水桶装得太满，水漫出来了 → abundant 丰富的、充足的","word":"abundant"},"root":"拉丁语 ab“向外”+ unda“波浪”，字面义“像波浪一样涌出、溢出”，核心是“多到装不下”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of abundant, all built on overflow: many in number, more than enough, rich in a quality, producing much, naturally plentiful, numerous in an ecosystem, in surplus by arithmetic, and plentiful as money in a market.","cn":"abundant 的八个义项都建立在“溢出”上：数量多、超过所需、富于某种性质、产出多、自然资源丰富、生态上数量多、按算术属于盈余，以及市场上资金充裕。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a container so full that its contents overflow the edge.","cn":"核心意象：容器满到内容物漫过边缘。"},"chain":["FULL","OVERFLOW","LARGE QUANTITY","MORE THAN ENOUGH","RICH IN SOMETHING","COUNTED AND PRICED"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"MANY: the plain sense is a large number or amount of something.","cn":"很多：最朴素的义项就是数量或数目很大。"},{"senses":"02 · 04","en":"MORE THAN NEEDED: past sufficiency, and land or trees that keep producing past need.","cn":"超过所需：越过充足线，以及土地或树木持续产出超过所需。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"RICH IN: a quality present in quantity, and natural resources that need no cultivation.","cn":"富于：某种性质大量存在，以及无需耕作就有的自然资源。"},{"senses":"06","en":"ECOLOGY: high numbers of one species in a place.","cn":"生态学：某一物种在某一地点数量很多。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"TWO COUNTED USES: a number whose divisors exceed it, and money so plentiful that borrowing is easy.","cn":"两种可计量的用法：真因数之和超过自身的数，以及多到借钱容易的资金。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Abundant is the adjective; abundance is the noun, abundantly the adverb, and abound the verb. All keep the same overflow image.","cn":"abundant 是形容词，abundance 是名词，abundantly 是副词，abound 是动词，全部保留“溢出”意象。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on unda 'wave': inundate 'flood', undulate 'move in waves', and redundant 'overflowing in words' all belong here.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 unda“波浪”上：inundate“淹没”、undulate“波动”、redundant“言语溢出、冗余”都属于此。"},"items":[{"word":"abundance","structure":"abundant + -ance","meaning":"a large quantity; the state of having plenty","meaningCN":"丰富；充裕（-ance 构成状态名词）","example":"There was an abundance of fresh fruit.","exampleCN":"有大量新鲜水果。"},{"word":"abundantly","structure":"abundant + -ly","meaning":"in large amounts; very clearly","meaningCN":"大量地；非常清楚地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The land is abundantly watered.","exampleCN":"这片土地水源充沛。"},{"word":"abound","structure":"a- (on, in) + unda (wave)","meaning":"to exist in large numbers; to be rich in","meaningCN":"大量存在；富于（动词形式）","example":"Wild flowers abound in the valley.","exampleCN":"山谷里野花遍地。"},{"word":"overabundant","structure":"over- (too much) + abundant","meaning":"more plentiful than is wanted","meaningCN":"过剩的；过于丰富的（over- 表示“过度”）","example":"Overabundant deer damaged the young trees.","exampleCN":"过多的鹿破坏了幼树。"},{"word":"overabundance","structure":"over- (too much) + abundance","meaning":"more than is needed or wanted","meaningCN":"过剩；过多（over- 表过度）","example":"An overabundance of advice confused the team.","exampleCN":"建议过多反而把团队弄糊涂了。"},{"word":"superabundant","structure":"super- (above, beyond) + abundant","meaning":"abundant beyond what is usual","meaningCN":"极其丰富的；过多的（super- 表超出）","example":"The region has superabundant rainfall in summer.","exampleCN":"这个地区夏季雨水极多。"},{"word":"superabundance","structure":"super- (above, beyond) + abundance","meaning":"an extreme amount","meaningCN":"极大量；过剩（super- 表超出）","example":"A superabundance of algae choked the pond.","exampleCN":"过量的藻类让池塘窒息。"},{"word":"inundate","structure":"in- (on, into) + unda (wave) + -ate (same Latin root)","meaning":"to flood, or to overwhelm with a great quantity","meaningCN":"淹没；使应接不暇（与 unda“波浪”同根）","example":"Requests inundated the small office.","exampleCN":"大量请求淹没了这个小办公室。"},{"word":"undulate","structure":"unda (wave) + -ulate (same Latin root)","meaning":"to move in a wave-like way","meaningCN":"波动；起伏（-ulate 表示反复动作，与 unda 同根）","example":"The hills undulate toward the coast.","exampleCN":"丘陵向海岸起伏绵延。"},{"word":"redundant","structure":"re- (again) + unda (wave) + -ant; literally “overflowing”","meaning":"more than is needed; no longer necessary","meaningCN":"多余的；冗余的（源自“溢出”，与 unda 同根）","example":"The report repeats itself and is redundant.","exampleCN":"这份报告自我重复，内容冗余。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"inundate","structure":"in- (into) + unda (wave) + -ate","meaning":"to flood; to overwhelm with a large amount","meaningCN":"淹没；使应接不暇（水涌入成波）"},{"word":"undulate","structure":"unda (wave) + -ate","meaning":"to move with a wave-like motion","meaningCN":"波动；起伏（像波浪一样运动）"},{"word":"redundant","structure":"re- (again) + unda (wave) + -ant","meaning":"more than is needed; overflowing in words","meaningCN":"多余的；冗余的（字面义“再次涌出”，引申为言语溢出）"}]}},{"word":"abuse","ipa_uk":"/əˈbjuːs/ (noun); /əˈbjuːz/ (verb)","ipa_us":"/əˈbjuːs/ (noun); /əˈbjuːz/ (verb)","definition_zh":"滥用；虐待；辱骂","definition_en":"the wrong use of power or a substance, cruel treatment of a person or animal, or rude harmful words","core_image":"把“使用”偏离原本用途，变成伤害","scene":"护工把老人手臂上的淤青拍进手机。 The caregiver photographed the bruises on the old man's arm to keep evidence of abuse.","sceneCN":"这里 abuse 是「虐待」（第 2 个义项：残酷对待他人）；句意：护工拍下老人手臂上的淤青，留作虐待的证据。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"滥用；虐待；辱骂"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"滥用；虐待；辱骂"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"abuse of power","zh":"滥用权力"},{"phrase":"child abuse","zh":"虐待儿童"},{"phrase":"drug abuse","zh":"滥用药物"},{"phrase":"verbal abuse","zh":"言语辱骂"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"abuses"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"abused"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"abused"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"abusing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"abusive","pos":"adj.","zh":"辱骂的；虐待的；滥用的"},{"word":"abuser","pos":"n.","zh":"施虐者；滥用者"},{"word":"disabuse","pos":"v.","zh":"使纠正错误想法；使醒悟"},{"word":"self-abuse","pos":"n.","zh":"自我伤害（旧时也指手淫，属过时委婉语）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Misuse of power","titleCN":"滥用权力：把权力用歪","definition":"the use of power or authority for a wrong purpose","definitionCN":"为错误目的使用权力或权威","example":"The report accused the manager of abuse of power.","exampleCN":"报告指控经理滥用权力。","why":"Latin abuti meant 'to use up, misuse', built on ab 'away' + uti 'use'. The use has moved away from its proper purpose, so power becomes a tool of harm.","whyCN":"拉丁语 abuti 意为“用完、误用”，由 ab“离开”+ uti“使用”构成。使用偏离了正当目的，于是权力变成了伤害的工具。"},{"no":"02","title":"Cruel treatment of a person or animal","titleCN":"虐待：残酷对待","definition":"cruel or violent treatment that hurts a person or animal","definitionCN":"伤害人或动物的残酷或暴力对待","example":"The charity protects children from abuse.","exampleCN":"这个慈善机构保护儿童免受虐待。","why":"A person is not an object to be used, but abuse treats them as one: their body or trust is consumed for someone else's purpose. The misuse branch turns into mistreatment.","whyCN":"人不是可供使用的物件，但 abuse 把人当成物件：他们的身体或信任被消耗来实现别人的目的。“误用”这一支由此变成“虐待”。"},{"no":"03","title":"Insulting language","titleCN":"辱骂：用语言伤害","definition":"rude, insulting, or threatening words directed at someone","definitionCN":"针对某人的粗鲁、侮辱性或威胁性言语","example":"The player was punished for verbal abuse.","exampleCN":"这名球员因言语辱骂受到处罚。","why":"Words can also be 'used away' from their purpose of communicating. When speech is turned into a weapon, the result is verbal abuse.","whyCN":"语言也可以偏离“沟通”的用途。当言语被变成武器，结果就是言语辱骂。"},{"no":"04","title":"Drug or substance abuse","titleCN":"药物滥用：把药物用成伤害","definition":"the harmful or excessive use of drugs or alcohol","definitionCN":"对毒品或酒精的有害或过度使用","example":"The clinic treats people with drug abuse problems.","exampleCN":"这家诊所治疗有药物滥用问题的人。","why":"A medicine is meant to heal, but when it is used outside that purpose it damages the user. The same 'use away from the purpose' produces substance abuse.","whyCN":"药物的用途是治疗，但若在治疗之外使用，就会伤害使用者。同一种“偏离用途的使用”产生了 substance abuse。"},{"no":"05","title":"Use something wrongly","titleCN":"误用某物","definition":"to use something in a wrong or improper way, especially to damage it","definitionCN":"以错误或不恰当的方式使用某物，尤指造成损坏","example":"He abused the equipment until it broke.","exampleCN":"他乱用设备，直到把它弄坏。","why":"This is the plainest sense: a tool is used beyond what it was made for. The object does not gain a new purpose; it simply suffers from the wrong one.","whyCN":"这是最朴素的义项：工具被用在超出其设计用途的地方。物件并没有获得新用途，只是被错误用途损害了。"},{"no":"06","title":"Deceive (archaic)","titleCN":"欺骗（古旧义）","definition":"in older use, to deceive or take advantage of someone","definitionCN":"较古的用法：欺骗或占某人便宜","example":"The old story tells how the merchant abused the villagers.","exampleCN":"这个古老的故事讲述商人如何欺骗村民。","why":"Old French abuser meant 'to deceive'. Misuse easily becomes deception when the person being used does not know what is happening.","whyCN":"古法语 abuser 意为“欺骗”。当被使用的人不知道发生了什么，“误用”就很容易变成“欺骗”。"},{"no":"07","title":"Sexual abuse: forced sexual contact","titleCN":"性虐待：强迫的性接触","definition":"sexual contact forced on a person, especially by someone with power over them","definitionCN":"强加于人的性接触，尤指由对其有权力者实施","example":"The inquiry found that the coach had committed sexual abuse.","exampleCN":"调查认定这名教练实施了性虐待。","why":"The bent purpose reaches the body: a relationship of trust and care is used for a purpose that destroys it, which is why the term is a separate legal category.","whyCN":"扭弯的用途落到身体上：本应给予信任与照顾的关系被用于摧毁它的目的，因此这一说法成为独立的法律类别。"},{"no":"08","title":"Law: abuse of a position of trust","titleCN":"法律：滥用信任地位","definition":"the misuse of a role of authority or trust for personal gain or harm","definitionCN":"为私利或伤害而滥用具有权威或信任的职务","example":"Taking the money was an abuse of the trust placed in him.","exampleCN":"拿走这笔钱，是对他人托付信任的滥用。","why":"Here the thing misused is neither an object nor a person but a relationship: trust itself becomes the instrument, and the law treats that as a distinct wrong.","whyCN":"这里被误用的既不是物件也不是人，而是一段关系：信任本身成了工具，法律把这视为一种独立的过错。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Abuse came through French from Latin abuti 'to use up, misuse'. The base verb uti 'use' has an uncertain deeper origin, so the chain is marked uncertain at the bottom.","cn":"abuse 经由法语来自拉丁语 abuti“用完、误用”。基础动词 uti“使用”的更深来源不明，因此这条链的最底层标为不确定。"},"items":[{"era":"EARLY 15C.","en":"First recorded early 15c. as a verb meaning 'to misuse, misapply'; the noun follows in the mid-15c. with the sense 'improper practice'.","cn":"最早记录于 15 世纪早期，动词义为“误用、滥用”；名词随后于 15 世纪中期出现，义为“不当做法”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"From Old French abuser (14c.) 'to deceive, abuse, misuse'.","cn":"来自古法语 abuser（14 世纪）“欺骗、滥用、误用”。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"From Latin abusus, past participle of abuti 'use up, consume; misuse, outrage' = ab 'off, away from' + uti 'use'.","cn":"来自拉丁语 abusus，即 abuti“用完、消耗；误用、侵害”的过去分词；abuti = ab“离开”+ uti“使用”。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"The deeper origin of uti 'use' is uncertain; standard references mark it as of uncertain origin, so any PIE root here is source uncertain.","cn":"uti“使用”的更深来源不确定；通行资料直接标为“来源不明”，因此这里任何原始印欧语词根都来源不确定。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps the noun with /s/ and the verb with /z/. The noun covers misuse, mistreatment, and insult; the verb covers all three actions.","cn":"现代英语名词读 /s/，动词读 /z/。名词覆盖滥用、虐待和辱骂；动词则覆盖这三种行为。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The spelling group contains words that look or sound close; the meaning group contains words for wrong use and cruel treatment.","cn":"拼写组收录看起来或听起来接近的词；近义组收录表示“误用”和“残酷对待”的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"amuse","ipa":"/əˈmjuːz/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"to make someone laugh or enjoy themselves. It differs by one letter and is unrelated in meaning.","definitionCN":"逗某人笑；使某人愉悦。它只差一个字母，词义无关。"},{"word":"abyss","ipa":"/əˈbɪs/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"a very deep hole or space. It begins with ab- but comes from Greek, not from uti.","definitionCN":"深渊；极深的空间。它以 ab- 开头，但来自希腊语，而不是 uti。"},{"word":"abuser","ipa":"/əˈbjuːzə/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"a person who abuses others or a substance.","definitionCN":"施虐者；滥用者。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"misuse","ipa":"/ˌmɪsˈjuːz/","tag":"wrong use","definition":"to use something wrongly or for the wrong purpose; the neutral counterpart of one branch of abuse.","definitionCN":"误用；为错误目的使用。它是 abuse 某一支的中性对应词。"},{"word":"mistreatment","ipa":"/ˌmɪsˈtriːtmənt/","tag":"cruelty","definition":"the act of treating someone badly or cruelly.","definitionCN":"虐待；残酷对待。"},{"word":"maltreatment","ipa":"/ˌmælˈtriːtmənt/","tag":"formal cruelty","definition":"cruel or violent treatment, especially of a person or animal; more formal than abuse.","definitionCN":"虐待；粗暴对待，尤指对人或者动物，比 abuse 更正式。"},{"word":"insult","ipa":"/ɪnˈsʌlt/","tag":"words","definition":"to say something rude that hurts or offends someone; the verbal branch of abuse.","definitionCN":"侮辱；辱骂，是 abuse 的言语分支。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts and real relatives: ab- 'away' + uti 'use', with disabuse, abusive and the Latin uti family.","cn":"真实构词与真实同族词：ab-“离开”+ uti“使用”，以及 disabuse、abusive 和拉丁 uti 词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"ab- 'away' + uti 'use' = to use something away from its purpose. That is the core of every sense.","cn":"ab-“离开”+ uti“使用”=把某物用到偏离其用途的地方。这就是所有义项的核心。"},{"en":"Abusive is the adjective and abuser the person; both keep the idea of a use that harms.","cn":"abusive 是形容词，abuser 是施动者；两者都保留“使用造成伤害”的意思。"},{"en":"Disabuse is the reverse: to take away a mistaken belief, literally to 'un-use' a false idea.","cn":"disabuse 是反向的：去除错误想法，字面上就是“不再使用”一个假观念。"},{"en":"Drug abuse is medicine used away from its healing purpose.","cn":"drug abuse 就是药物被用在偏离治疗目的的地方。"},{"en":"The noun ends in /s/ and the verb ends in /z/: abuse of power, but to abuse power.","cn":"名词结尾读 /s/，动词结尾读 /z/：abuse of power，但 to abuse power。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a hammer used to open a window: the tool still works, but the purpose has been bent.","cn":"想象一把锤子被用来撬窗户：工具还能用，但用途被扭弯了。"},{"en":"The bent purpose can point at power (misuse), at a person (mistreatment), at speech (insult), or at a drug (substance abuse).","cn":"被扭弯的用途可以指向权力（滥用）、指向人（虐待）、指向言语（辱骂）或指向药物（药物滥用）。"},{"en":"The most serious form turns a person into an object to be used, which is why abuse also means cruelty.","cn":"最严重的形式把人变成可供使用的物件，这就是 abuse 也指“残酷对待”的原因。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The judge abused his position to help a friend.","cn":"这名法官滥用职位帮助朋友。"},{"en":"Several workers reported verbal abuse from the supervisor.","cn":"几名工人报告遭到主管的言语辱骂。"},{"en":"Do not abuse antibiotics by taking them for a cold.","cn":"不要因为感冒就滥用抗生素。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿布斯”——阿布斯把好东西用歪了，还拿来伤人 → abuse 滥用、虐待","word":"abuse"},"root":"拉丁语 ab“离开”+ uti“使用”，字面义“把使用偏离本来用途”，核心是“误用而成伤害”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of abuse, all one bent purpose: power, a person, speech, a drug, an object, a body, a trust, or a role can be used away from what it is for.","cn":"abuse 的八个义项都是同一个“扭弯的用途”：权力、人、言语、药物、物件、身体、信任或职务，都可以被用到偏离本来的用途上。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: use turns away from its proper purpose and becomes harm.","cn":"核心意象：使用偏离本来用途，变成伤害。"},"chain":["USE","AWAY FROM PURPOSE","POWER OR OBJECT","A PERSON","WORDS AND SUBSTANCES","TRUST AND DECEPTION"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 05","en":"THE INSTRUMENT: power and an object are both turned from what they are for.","cn":"工具层面：权力与物件都被扭离本来的用途。"},{"senses":"02 · 07","en":"THE BODY: cruelty to a person or animal, including contact forced on a person.","cn":"身体层面：残酷对待人或动物，包括强加于人的性接触。"},{"senses":"03","en":"THE VOICE: language used to wound rather than to speak.","cn":"言语层面：语言被用来伤害，而不是用来表达。"},{"senses":"04","en":"THE SUBSTANCE: a drug taken for harm rather than for treatment.","cn":"物质层面：药物被用于伤害而不是治疗。"},{"senses":"06 · 08","en":"THE RELATIONSHIP: deceit in the older use, and the misuse of trust that the law now punishes.","cn":"关系层面：较古的“欺骗”义，以及如今受法律惩治的对信任的滥用。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Abuse forms abusive with -ive and abuser with -er. The prefix dis- in disabuse reverses the 'using' of a false belief.","cn":"abuse 用 -ive 构成 abusive，用 -er 构成 abuser。disabuse 中的 dis- 则反转了对假观念的“使用”。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on uti 'use': use, usage, usury and utilize all come from the same verb, whose deeper origin is uncertain.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 uti“使用”上：use、usage、usury、utilize 都来自同一动词，其更深来源不确定。"},"items":[{"word":"abusive","structure":"abuse + -ive","meaning":"using cruel words or violence; wrongly used","meaningCN":"辱骂的；虐待的；滥用的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"He was fired for abusive language.","exampleCN":"他因辱骂性语言被解雇。"},{"word":"abuser","structure":"abuse + -er","meaning":"a person who abuses someone or something","meaningCN":"施虐者；滥用者（-er 表示做该动作的人）","example":"The abuser was banned from the shelter.","exampleCN":"施虐者被禁止进入收容所。"},{"word":"disabuse","structure":"dis- (apart, away) + abuse (deceive, use wrongly)","meaning":"to free someone from a mistaken belief","meaningCN":"使纠正错误想法；使醒悟（dis- 表示去除）","example":"Let me disabuse you of that idea.","exampleCN":"让我纠正你这个想法。"},{"word":"abusively","structure":"abusive + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a hurtful or insulting way","meaningCN":"辱骂地；滥用地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"He spoke abusively to the staff.","exampleCN":"他对员工说话很刻薄。"},{"word":"abusiveness","structure":"abusive + -ness (quality)","meaning":"the quality of being abusive","meaningCN":"辱骂性；滥用性（-ness 构成抽象名词）","example":"The report noted the abusiveness of the messages.","exampleCN":"报告指出了这些信息的辱骂性质。"},{"word":"abused","structure":"abuse + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"wrongly used, or treated cruelly","meaningCN":"被滥用的；受虐待的（-ed 构成过去分词）","example":"The abused system was shut down.","exampleCN":"这个被滥用的系统已经关停。"},{"word":"abusing","structure":"abuse + -ing (present participle and gerund)","meaning":"the act of using something wrongly or treating someone cruelly","meaningCN":"滥用（动名词）；正在滥用（现在分词）","example":"Abusing the discount code is a breach of the terms.","exampleCN":"滥用折扣码违反了条款。"},{"word":"self-abuse","structure":"self- (oneself) + abuse (compound)","meaning":"harmful treatment of oneself","meaningCN":"自我伤害；糟蹋自己（self- 表自身构成的复合词）","example":"The text warns against self-abuse of the body.","exampleCN":"文中告诫不要糟蹋自己的身体。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"use","structure":"uti (use)","meaning":"to employ something for a purpose","meaningCN":"使用；利用（直接来自 uti）"},{"word":"usage","structure":"uti + -age","meaning":"the way something is used; habitual practice","meaningCN":"用法；惯用法"},{"word":"usury","structure":"usura (use, interest)","meaning":"the practice of lending money at excessive interest","meaningCN":"高利贷（拉丁语 usura“使用、利息”，指对钱的使用收费）"},{"word":"utilize","structure":"uti + -ize","meaning":"to make practical use of something","meaningCN":"利用；使用"}]}},{"word":"academic","ipa_uk":"/ˌækəˈdemɪk/","ipa_us":"/ˌækəˈdemɪk/","definition_zh":"学术的；学业的；纯理论的；学者","definition_en":"relating to education, research, or scholarship; also a university teacher or researcher","core_image":"柏拉图学园的林荫路上，一群人边走边讨论学问","scene":"大学图书馆里，学生抱着几本期刊准备开始研究。 The student carried a stack of academic journals into the library to begin her research.","sceneCN":"这里 academic 是「学术的」（第 1 个义项：与教育和研究有关）；句意：学生抱着一叠学术期刊走进图书馆，开始她的研究。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"学术的；教育的；学业的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"纯理论的；与实际无直接关系的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"大学教师；学者"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"academic year","zh":"学年"},{"phrase":"academic performance","zh":"学业表现；学习成绩"},{"phrase":"academic research","zh":"学术研究"},{"phrase":"academic journal","zh":"学术期刊"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（名词，多于一个）","form":"academics"},{"label":"比较级（形容词，用 more）","form":"more academic"},{"label":"最高级（形容词，用 most）","form":"most academic"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"academy","pos":"n.","zh":"学院；学会；研究院"},{"word":"academically","pos":"adv.","zh":"学业上；学术上"},{"word":"academician","pos":"n.","zh":"院士；学会会员"},{"word":"academe","pos":"n.","zh":"学术界；学院生活（文学用语）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Relating to education and research","titleCN":"学术的：与教育和研究有关","definition":"connected with education, universities, and serious study or research","definitionCN":"与教育、大学以及严谨的学习或研究有关","example":"She has a strong academic background in biology.","exampleCN":"她有很强的生物学学术背景。","why":"The word comes from the Academy, the garden where Plato taught. Anything belonging to that world of organised study and argument is academic.","whyCN":"这个词来自 Academy，即柏拉图讲学的园林。凡属于那个有组织地学习与论辩的世界的事物，就是 academic。"},{"no":"02","title":"Theoretical rather than practical","titleCN":"纯理论的：不直接解决实际问题","definition":"concerned with theory and study rather than with practical use","definitionCN":"关注理论与研究，而不是实际应用","example":"The question is of academic interest only.","exampleCN":"这个问题只有学术上的兴趣。","why":"Study can be separated from practice. When a matter stays inside the seminar room and never reaches the workshop, it is called academic, sometimes with a hint of 'not useful'.","whyCN":"学习可以与实践分开。当一件事只留在研讨室里、从不进入工坊，它就被称为 academic，有时暗含“不实用”的意味。"},{"no":"03","title":"Relating to school performance","titleCN":"学业的：与在校成绩有关","definition":"connected with progress, grades, or subjects studied at school or university","definitionCN":"与学校或大学的学习进度、成绩或科目有关","example":"His academic performance improved this term.","exampleCN":"他这学期的学业表现提高了。","why":"The Academy is not only a place of research but a place of assessment. Anything measured by grades and courses belongs to the academic side of school life.","whyCN":"学园不仅是研究之地，也是评估之地。凡是以成绩和课程来衡量的，都属于学校生活中的“学业”一面。"},{"no":"04","title":"A university teacher or researcher","titleCN":"学者：大学教师或研究人员","definition":"a person who teaches or does research at a university","definitionCN":"在大学任教或从事研究的人","example":"Several academics signed the open letter.","exampleCN":"几位学者签署了这封公开信。","why":"The adjective becomes a noun for the people who live inside the Academy. An academic is defined by membership in that institution, not by a particular subject.","whyCN":"这个形容词转成名词，指生活在学园里的人。academic 的身份由所属机构界定，而不是由某一具体学科界定。"},{"no":"05","title":"The academic year","titleCN":"学年：学校的日历","definition":"in the phrase academic year, the period of study from the start of one school year to the next","definitionCN":"用于 academic year，指从一学年开始到下一学年开始的在校期间","example":"The academic year begins in September.","exampleCN":"学年从九月开始。","why":"The institution keeps its own calendar. Its year is not the calendar year but the cycle of teaching and examination, so the adjective marks institutional time.","whyCN":"机构有自己的日历。它的“一年”不是自然年，而是教学与考试的周期，因此这个形容词标记的是机构时间。"},{"no":"06","title":"An academic question: irrelevant in practice","titleCN":"空谈的问题：实际无关紧要","definition":"in the phrase an academic question, a matter that has no practical effect","definitionCN":"用于 an academic question，指没有实际影响的问题","example":"Whether the design is elegant is academic; it must first work.","exampleCN":"设计是否优雅只是空谈；它首先得能用。","why":"This sense pushes 'theoretical' to 'irrelevant'. The question may be interesting inside the Academy, but outside it nothing changes, so the word becomes a polite dismissal.","whyCN":"这个义项把“理论的”推到“无关紧要”。问题在学园内部也许有趣，但在外面什么也改变不了，于是这个词变成一种礼貌的否定。"},{"no":"07","title":"Academic freedom: research without interference","titleCN":"学术自由：不受干预的研究","definition":"the principle that scholars may teach and publish without political or institutional interference","definitionCN":"学者可以教学与发表而不受政治或机构干预的原则","example":"Academic freedom protects a lecturer who challenges the syllabus.","exampleCN":"学术自由保护挑战教学大纲的讲师。","why":"The academy is a walled garden for study; this sense names the rule that keeps the wall from being used to shut ideas in.","whyCN":"学园是为研究围起的园子；这个义项讲的是防止这堵墙被用来把思想关在里面的那条规则。"},{"no":"08","title":"School sport: eligibility to compete","titleCN":"校园体育：参赛资格","definition":"in school and college sport, the requirement that an athlete keeps passing enough courses to compete","definitionCN":"在中学与大学体育中，要求运动员修够课程并保持成绩方能参赛","example":"The athlete lost academic eligibility after failing two courses.","exampleCN":"这名运动员两门课不及格，失去了参赛资格。","why":"The classroom reaches into the stadium: the student must still be a student in good standing, so the adjective marks the school rule that governs play.","whyCN":"教室伸手进了球场：学生必须仍是成绩合格的学生，因此这个形容词标出管着比赛的校规。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Academic comes from the name of Plato's school, the Academy. The school was named after a legendary Athenian, and the origin of that personal name is not established.","cn":"academic 来自柏拉图学园的名称 Academy。学园以一位传说中的雅典人命名，而这个人名的来源并未确立。"},"items":[{"era":"1580S","en":"First recorded in the 1580s as an adjective meaning 'relating to an academy; collegiate, scholarly'. The noun 'university student' is also recorded in the 1580s.","cn":"16 世纪 80 年代最早记录为形容词，意为“与学园有关的；学院的、学术的”；名词义“大学生”也见于 16 世纪 80 年代。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"From Latin academicus 'of the (classical Athenian) Academy', from Academia, the name of Plato's school.","cn":"来自拉丁语 academicus“（古典雅典）学园的”，再往上为 Academia，即柏拉图学园的名称。"},{"era":"GREEK","en":"From Greek Akadēmeia 'the grove of Akadēmos', a place outside Athens named after a legendary Athenian called Akadēmos.","cn":"来自希腊语 Akadēmeia“阿卡德摩斯的园林”，是雅典城外的一处地方，以传说中名叫阿卡德摩斯的雅典人命名。"},{"era":"PERSONAL NAME","en":"The name Akadēmos is said to mean 'of a silent district', but the analysis is not established; standard references do not give a secure Greek root. source uncertain.","cn":"据说 Akadēmos 这个名字意为“寂静之地的人”，但这一分析并未确立；通行资料没有给出可靠的希腊词根。来源不确定。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English uses academic for the adjective and the person. Academy keeps the institution, while academe is a literary word for the academic world.","cn":"现代英语用 academic 兼作形容词和人物名词。academy 保留机构义，academe 则是“学术界”的文学用语。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The spelling group shows the Academy family; the meaning group shows other words for study, theory, and learning.","cn":"拼写组展示 Academy 词族；近义组展示其他关于学习、理论与学问的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"academy","ipa":"/əˈkædəmi/","tag":"base institution","definition":"a school, society, or institution for study; the place behind academic.","definitionCN":"学院；学会；研究机构，是 academic 背后的机构名。"},{"word":"academe","ipa":"/ˈækədiːm/","tag":"literary variant","definition":"the academic world or life of study, used mainly in literary contexts.","definitionCN":"学术界；学院生活，主要用于文学语境。"},{"word":"academician","ipa":"/əˌkædəˈmɪʃn/","tag":"derived person","definition":"a member of an academy or learned society.","definitionCN":"院士；学会会员。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"scholarly","ipa":"/ˈskɒləli/","tag":"person or work","definition":"showing careful study and knowledge; close to academic but focused on the quality of the work.","definitionCN":"有学者风范的；显示严谨学识的，接近 academic，但更强调作品或人的品质。"},{"word":"educational","ipa":"/ˌedʒuˈkeɪʃənl/","tag":"teaching","definition":"relating to education or intended to teach; broader than academic and not limited to universities.","definitionCN":"教育的；有教育意义的，比 academic 更宽，不限于大学。"},{"word":"theoretical","ipa":"/ˌθɪəˈretɪkl/","tag":"theory","definition":"based on theory rather than practice; the core of the 'impractical' sense of academic.","definitionCN":"理论的；基于理论而非实践的，是 academic“不实用”义的核心。"},{"word":"pedantic","ipa":"/pɪˈdæntɪk/","tag":"negative","definition":"showing too much concern with small details or formal rules; the negative side of academic habits.","definitionCN":"迂腐的；过分拘泥细节的，是学术习气的负面一面。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real history and real relatives: Plato's Academy, academy, academe, academician, and the adjective -ic.","cn":"真实历史与真实同族词：柏拉图的 Academy、academy、academe、academician，以及形容词后缀 -ic。"},"normal":[{"en":"Academic points back to Plato's Academy, the garden where he taught; the adjective and the person both belong to that institution.","cn":"academic 指向柏拉图讲学的 Academy 园林；形语词和人称名词都属于那个机构。"},{"en":"Academy is the place, academic is what belongs to it, and an academic is a person inside it.","cn":"academy 是地方，academic 是属于它的性质，an academic 是身处其中的人。"},{"en":"Academic year is institutional time, not calendar time: the cycle of teaching and exams.","cn":"academic year 是机构时间，而不是日历时间：教学与考试的周期。"},{"en":"An academic question is one that matters inside the seminar but changes nothing outside it.","cn":"an academic question 是在研讨室里重要、在外面什么也改变不了的问题。"},{"en":"Academe and academician are the literary and institutional branches of the same name.","cn":"academe 和 academician 是同一个名称的文学分支与机构分支。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a walled garden with people walking and arguing: the wall is the Academy, and everything inside it is academic.","cn":"想象一座有围墙的园林，人们边走边辩论：围墙就是 Academy，墙内的一切都是 academic。"},{"en":"The wall protects study, but it also separates study from the street; that separation produces both 'scholarly' and 'impractical'.","cn":"围墙保护学问，也把学问与街道隔开；这种隔离同时产生了“学术的”和“不实用的”两层含义。"},{"en":"The people who live inside the wall are academics; the calendar they follow is the academic year.","cn":"住在墙内的人是 academics；他们遵循的日历就是 academic year。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The university is known for its academic excellence.","cn":"这所大学以学术卓越著称。"},{"en":"She left industry to pursue an academic career.","cn":"她离开产业界，去追求学术生涯。"},{"en":"The schedule follows the academic year.","cn":"日程按照学年安排。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿卡德米克”——阿卡在学院里读书做研究 → academic 学术的、学者","word":"academic"},"root":"源自柏拉图讲学的 Academy（Akadēmeia）一名，核心是“属于学园、属于系统研究的世界”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of academic, all inside or near the wall of Plato's Academy: research, theory, school performance, the people, the calendar, the question that never leaves the seminar room, the freedom to challenge, and the rules of eligibility.","cn":"academic 的八个义项都在柏拉图学园的墙内或附近：研究、理论、学业成绩、学园中的人、机构日历、走不出研讨室的问题、挑战观点的自由，以及参赛资格的规定。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a walled garden of study, the Academy.","cn":"核心意象：一座从事研究的围墙园林——学园。"},"chain":["THE ACADEMY","BELONGING TO STUDY","THEORY","RESULTS AND CALENDAR","PEOPLE INSIDE","FREEDOM AND ELIGIBILITY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"THE WALL: everything inside the Academy is academic in the plain sense.","cn":"围墙之内：学园里的一切，按字面都是“学术的”。"},{"senses":"02 · 06","en":"THEORY WITHOUT USE: a theoretical claim, and a question that changes nothing in practice.","cn":"无用的理论：纯理论的论断，以及在实践上改了也无用的问题。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"THE CALENDAR OF RESULTS: marks in a course, and the year that the institution runs on.","cn":"成绩与日历：课程里的分数，以及学校按之运转的学年。"},{"senses":"04","en":"THE PEOPLE: those who teach and research inside the wall.","cn":"墙里的人：在围墙之内教学与研究的人。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"RULES OF THE WALL: freedom to challenge ideas, and the course requirement that lets a student compete.","cn":"围墙的规则：挑战观点的自由，以及让学生得以参赛的课程要求。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Academic is a Latin adjective in -ic. The family is institutional rather than prefix-driven: academy, academe, academician.","cn":"academic 是带 -ic 的拉丁形容词。这个词族是机构性的，而不是靠前缀驱动的：academy、academe、academician。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The root is the Greek proper name Akadēmos, not a Latin common noun. There is no productive Latin root family to list, so the Latin entries are left empty rather than filled with guesswork.","cn":"这个词根是希腊语专名 Akadēmos，而不是拉丁普通名词。没有可列的能产拉丁词根家族，因此拉丁词族条目留空，而不是用猜测填充。"},"items":[{"word":"academy","structure":"Greek Akadēmeia via Latin Academia","meaning":"a school or learned society","meaningCN":"学院；学会；研究院","example":"She was elected to the national academy.","exampleCN":"她当选为全国学会会员。"},{"word":"academically","structure":"academic + -ally","meaning":"in relation to study or school performance","meaningCN":"学业上；学术上（-ally 构成副词）","example":"He is academically strong but quiet in class.","exampleCN":"他学业很强，但在课堂上很安静。"},{"word":"academician","structure":"academic + -ian (member)","meaning":"a member of an academy","meaningCN":"院士；学会会员（-ian 表示成员）","example":"The academician presented the annual report.","exampleCN":"这位院士作了年度报告。"},{"word":"academe","structure":"academy + -e (literary form)","meaning":"the academic world","meaningCN":"学术界；学院生活（文学用语）","example":"He left academe for a career in publishing.","exampleCN":"他离开学术界，进入出版业。"},{"word":"academicism","structure":"academic + -ism (doctrine or practice)","meaning":"emphasis on formal academic tradition","meaningCN":"学院主义；学究气（-ism 表示主义或作风）","example":"The painter avoided academicism in every brushstroke.","exampleCN":"这位画家每一笔都避开学究气。"},{"word":"academics","structure":"academic + -s (plural noun)","meaning":"the subjects, or the people, of higher education","meaningCN":"学科；学者（-s 构成复数名词）","example":"Academics from three countries joined the panel.","exampleCN":"来自三个国家的学者加入了这场讨论。"},{"word":"nonacademic","structure":"non- (not) + academic","meaning":"not connected with formal education","meaningCN":"非学术的；非学院的（non- 表否定）","example":"The journal accepts nonacademic writing too.","exampleCN":"这份刊物也接受非学术性文章。"},{"word":"academia","structure":"Latin Academia (same root as academic)","meaning":"the world of universities and research","meaningCN":"学术界（同源于拉丁语 Academia）","example":"She left industry for academia.","exampleCN":"她离开企业进了学术界。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"accelerate","ipa_uk":"/əkˈseləreɪt/","ipa_us":"/əkˈseləreɪt/","definition_zh":"加速；促进；提前","definition_en":"to make something happen faster or sooner, or to gain speed","core_image":"脚从刹车上移开，油门踩下去，速度表指针向右扫过","scene":"赛车驶出弯道，车手把脚放到油门上。 The race car came out of the curve, the driver pressed the pedal, and the car began to accelerate down the straight.","sceneCN":"这里 accelerate 是「加速」（第 1 个义项：使速度变快）；句意：赛车驶出弯道，车手踩下踏板，车子在直道上开始加速。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"使加速；促进；使提前发生"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"加速；速度增加"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"accelerate growth","zh":"促进增长"},{"phrase":"accelerate the process","zh":"加快进程"},{"phrase":"accelerate the pace","zh":"加快步伐"},{"phrase":"accelerate economic development","zh":"加快经济发展"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"accelerates"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"accelerated"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"accelerated"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"accelerating"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"acceleration","pos":"n.","zh":"加速；加速度；促进"},{"word":"accelerator","pos":"n.","zh":"加速器；油门"},{"word":"accelerant","pos":"n.","zh":"促进剂；助燃剂"},{"word":"accelerating","pos":"adj.","zh":"加速的；不断加快的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Make something move faster","titleCN":"使移动更快","definition":"to make a vehicle, person, or object move faster","definitionCN":"使车辆、人或物体移动得更快","example":"The car accelerated as it left the bend.","exampleCN":"赛车驶出弯道时加速了。","why":"Latin celer meant 'swift'. Accelerate is to add swifter motion to what is already moving, so the core is a change in speed rather than movement itself.","whyCN":"拉丁语 celer 意为“迅速的”。accelerate 是给已经在运动的东西再加上“更快”，所以核心是速度的变化，而不是运动本身。"},{"no":"02","title":"Make an event happen sooner","titleCN":"使事件提前发生","definition":"to make an event or process happen earlier or faster","definitionCN":"使事件或过程更早或更快地发生","example":"The new rules may accelerate the collapse of the old system.","exampleCN":"新规可能加速旧体系的崩溃。","why":"Time is the road, and the process is the vehicle. Accelerating it means shortening the road to the end point, so the event arrives sooner.","whyCN":"时间是路，过程是车。加速过程就是把通往终点的路缩短，于是事件更早到达。"},{"no":"03","title":"Increase the rate of growth","titleCN":"提高增长率","definition":"to increase the speed at which something grows, changes, or develops","definitionCN":"提高某物增长、变化或发展的速度","example":"The program accelerated economic growth in the region.","exampleCN":"这个项目加快了该地区的经济增长。","why":"A rate is the speed of a process. When the growth curve becomes steeper, the process is accelerating even if the total amount has not yet changed much.","whyCN":"比率是过程的速度。当增长曲线变陡，即使总量还没大幅变化，这个过程也在加速。"},{"no":"04","title":"Physics: gain speed","titleCN":"物理：速度增加","definition":"in physics, to change velocity so that speed increases","definitionCN":"物理学中，改变速度使速率增加","example":"The particle accelerates in the electric field.","exampleCN":"粒子在电场中加速。","why":"Physics separates velocity from acceleration. A body accelerates when its velocity changes, and in this branch the change is a gain in speed.","whyCN":"物理学把速度与加速度分开。当物体的速度发生变化时它就在加速，而这一支特指速度增加。"},{"no":"05","title":"Finance: pay or collect sooner","titleCN":"金融：提前支付","definition":"in finance, to arrange for payment, repayment, or benefits to occur earlier","definitionCN":"金融中安排付款、还款或收益更早发生","example":"The borrower accelerated the repayment of the loan.","exampleCN":"借款人提前偿还了贷款。","why":"A payment schedule is a timeline. To accelerate payment is to move its point on that timeline closer to the present, shortening the wait.","whyCN":"还款计划是一条时间轴。提前支付就是把时间轴上的那个点移向现在，缩短等待。"},{"no":"06","title":"Biology: speed up growth","titleCN":"生物：促进生长","definition":"to make a biological process such as growth or ripening happen faster","definitionCN":"使生长、成熟等生物过程更快发生","example":"Warm weather accelerated the ripening of the fruit.","exampleCN":"温暖的天气加快了果实的成熟。","why":"A living process has its own clock. Heat, light, or chemicals can push that clock forward, which is why accelerate is used for ripening and growth.","whyCN":"生命过程有自己的时钟。热量、光照或化学物质可以把时钟往前拨，所以 accelerate 也用于成熟和生长。"},{"no":"07","title":"Accounting: write off an asset faster","titleCN":"会计：加速折旧","definition":"in accounting and tax, to charge the cost of an asset against income over a shorter period than its useful life","definitionCN":"在会计与税务中，把资产成本在短于使用年限的期间内计入费用","example":"The firm used accelerated depreciation to cut its tax bill.","exampleCN":"这家公司用加速折旧来减少税负。","why":"Time is the thing made faster: the same total cost is spread over fewer years, so the deduction arrives sooner than the machine wears out.","whyCN":"被加快的是时间：同样的总成本摊到更少的年份上，于是扣减比机器磨损来得更早。"},{"no":"08","title":"Medicine: approve a drug sooner","titleCN":"医药：加快审批","definition":"of a regulator, to allow a treatment to reach patients before all the usual trials are complete","definitionCN":"指监管机构在常规试验全部完成前就允许疗法投入使用","example":"Regulators granted accelerated approval for the new drug.","exampleCN":"监管机构对该新药给予加速审批。","why":"The queue is what is shortened: the review is not skipped but compressed, so the medicine arrives earlier while follow-up data are still being collected.","whyCN":"缩短的是排队：审查没有跳过，只是被压缩，于是药物更早到达，而后续数据仍在收集。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Accelerate came straight from Latin accelerare 'to hasten'. Its root celer 'swift' survives in celerity and accelerator; the deeper PIE link is probable rather than certain.","cn":"accelerate 直接来自拉丁语 accelerare“催促、加快”。词根 celer“迅捷”保留在 celerity 和 accelerator 中；更深的原始印欧语联系只是可能，并非确定。"},"items":[{"era":"1520S","en":"First recorded in the 1520s meaning 'hasten the occurrence of'; the sense 'make quicker' appears in the 1590s.","cn":"15 世纪 20 年代最早记录，意为“使更早发生”；“使更快”义出现于 16 世纪 90 年代。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"From Latin acceleratus, past participle of accelerare 'to hasten, quicken'.","cn":"来自拉丁语 acceleratus，即 accelerare“催促、加快”的过去分词。"},{"era":"LATIN MORPHOLOGY","en":"Accelerare = ad 'to' + celerare 'hasten', from celer 'swift'.","cn":"accelerare = ad“向”+ celerare“催促”，后者来自 celer“迅捷的”。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Celer is connected 'perhaps' to PIE *keli- 'speeding', also seen in Sanskrit carati 'goes' and Greek keles 'fast horse or ship'. The reference marks it as probable, so this link is source uncertain.","cn":"celer 与原始印欧语 *keli-“快速行进”的联系只标为“perhaps”；同源例有梵语 carati“行走”和希腊语 keles“快马或快船”。资料将其标为可能，故此环节来源不确定。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English uses accelerate for vehicles, processes, growth, payments, and particles. The noun acceleration and the device accelerator keep the same root.","cn":"现代英语用 accelerate 指车辆、过程、增长、付款和粒子。名词 acceleration 和装置 accelerator 保留同一词根。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group looks at the -celer- spelling family; the second at verbs that mean 'make faster'.","cn":"第一组看 -celer- 拼写家族；第二组看表示“使更快”的动词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"acceleration","ipa":"/əkˌseləˈreɪʃn/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the noun from accelerate: the act or rate of speeding up.","definitionCN":"accelerate 派生的名词：加速的行为或加速度。"},{"word":"accelerator","ipa":"/əkˈseləreɪtə/","tag":"agent noun","definition":"a device or pedal that makes something go faster.","definitionCN":"加速器；油门。"},{"word":"celebrate","ipa":"/ˈselɪbreɪt/","tag":"near sound","definition":"to mark a happy event with a ceremony or party. It sounds close but comes from celeber 'crowded, famous'.","definitionCN":"庆祝；举行庆典。它听起来接近，但来自 celeber“拥挤的、著名的”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"hasten","ipa":"/ˈheɪsn/","tag":"make sooner","definition":"to make something happen sooner; close to accelerate in the time sense.","definitionCN":"催促；使更早发生，在时间义上接近 accelerate。"},{"word":"quicken","ipa":"/ˈkwɪkən/","tag":"make faster","definition":"to make something faster or more active; often used for the pulse or growth.","definitionCN":"加快；使更活跃，常用于脉搏或生长。"},{"word":"speed up","ipa":"/spiːd ʌp/","tag":"phrasal verb","definition":"the everyday phrasal verb for accelerating.","definitionCN":"加快；加速，是 accelerate 的日常短语动词。"},{"word":"expedite","ipa":"/ˈekspədaɪt/","tag":"formal process","definition":"to make a process happen more quickly, especially in business or administration.","definitionCN":"加快进程，尤用于商业或行政语境。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts and real relatives: ad- + celer 'swift', with celerity, accelerator, and decelerate.","cn":"真实构词与真实同族词：ad- + celer“迅捷”，以及 celerity、accelerator、decelerate。"},"normal":[{"en":"ad- 'to' + celer 'swift' = to add swiftness to something. The core is speed, not motion itself.","cn":"ad-“向”+ celer“迅捷”=给某物增添迅捷。核心是速度，而不是运动本身。"},{"en":"Celerity is the noun for swiftness; the accelerator is the pedal or device that adds it.","cn":"celerity 是“迅捷”的名词；accelerator 是增添迅捷的踏板或装置。"},{"en":"Decelerate is the mirror image: de- removes speed instead of adding it.","cn":"decelerate 是镜像：de- 去掉速度，而不是增加速度。"},{"en":"Accelerate the process and accelerate growth are fixed collocations in business and science.","cn":"accelerate the process 和 accelerate growth 是商业与科学中的固定搭配。"},{"en":"In physics, acceleration is the rate at which velocity changes, not simply 'fast'.","cn":"在物理学中，acceleration 是速度变化的比率，而不只是“快”。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a speedometer needle sweeping from left to right: accelerate is that sweep, not the car's position.","cn":"想象速度表指针从左向右扫过：accelerate 是这次扫动，而不是车的位置。"},{"en":"The same sweep can apply to a car, a process, a growth curve, a payment schedule, or a ripening fruit.","cn":"同一次扫动可以作用于汽车、过程、增长曲线、付款计划或成熟的果实。"},{"en":"To accelerate time is to move the end point closer, so the future arrives early.","cn":"加速时间就是把终点拉近，于是未来提前到达。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The train accelerated smoothly out of the station.","cn":"火车平稳地加速驶出车站。"},{"en":"New technology accelerated the pace of change.","cn":"新技术加快了变化的步伐。"},{"en":"Exercise can accelerate recovery after surgery.","cn":"锻炼可以加快术后恢复。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿克赛勒瑞特”——阿克一踩油门，速度表指针飞快右扫 → accelerate 加速","word":"accelerate"},"root":"拉丁语 ad“向”+ celer“迅捷”，字面义“给某物增添速度”，核心是“让速度变快或让事情提前”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of accelerate, all one gain in rate: a vehicle moves faster, an event comes sooner, growth steepens, a particle gains speed, payment moves earlier, a fruit ripens quickly, an asset is written off sooner, and a drug is approved sooner.","cn":"accelerate 的八个义项都是同一种“速率增加”：车更快、事件更早、增长更陡、粒子加速、付款提前、果实快熟、资产更早摊完、药物更早获批。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a speedometer needle sweeping to a higher number.","cn":"核心意象：速度表指针扫向更大的数字。"},"chain":["SWIFT","ADD SPEED","FASTER MOTION","EARLIER EVENT","STEEPER GROWTH","EARLIER MONEY OR APPROVAL"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 04","en":"MOTION: a vehicle pressed forward, and a body gaining speed in physics.","cn":"运动：车被往前推，以及物理学中速度增加的运动体。"},{"senses":"02","en":"THE CLOCK: the same event placed earlier on the calendar.","cn":"时钟：同一件事被提前放到日历上。"},{"senses":"03 · 06","en":"STEEPER CURVES: growth rates, and organisms that ripen sooner.","cn":"更陡的曲线：增长速率，以及更早成熟的生物。"},{"senses":"05","en":"MONEY: payment collected or made before its due date.","cn":"金钱：在到期日之前收付的款项。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"SANCTIONED SHORTCUTS: costs written off sooner, and a drug allowed to reach patients sooner.","cn":"被许可的捷径：成本更早摊完，药物也更早到达病人。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Accelerate forms acceleration with -tion and accelerator with -or; accelerant is the substance that speeds something up.","cn":"accelerate 用 -tion 构成 acceleration，用 -or 构成 accelerator；accelerant 是加快过程的物质。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on celer 'swift': celerity, accelerando, and decelerate all belong here.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 celer“迅捷”上：celerity、accelerando、decelerate 都属于此。"},"items":[{"word":"acceleration","structure":"accelerate + -tion","meaning":"the act of speeding up; the rate of change of velocity","meaningCN":"加速；加速度（-tion 构成名词）","example":"The car has strong acceleration.","exampleCN":"这辆车加速性能很强。"},{"word":"accelerator","structure":"accelerate + -or","meaning":"a device that makes something go faster","meaningCN":"加速器；油门（-or 表示装置）","example":"He pressed the accelerator to the floor.","exampleCN":"他把油门踩到底。"},{"word":"accelerant","structure":"accelerate + -ant","meaning":"a substance that makes fire or a process develop faster","meaningCN":"助燃剂；促进剂（-ant 表示起作用之物）","example":"The fire spread quickly because of an accelerant.","exampleCN":"由于有助燃剂，火势迅速蔓延。"},{"word":"accelerometer","structure":"accelerate + -meter (measure)","meaning":"an instrument that measures acceleration","meaningCN":"加速度计（-meter 表示测量仪器）","example":"The phone uses an accelerometer to detect movement.","exampleCN":"手机用加速度计检测运动。"},{"word":"accelerating","structure":"accelerate + -ing (present participle)","meaning":"speeding up","meaningCN":"加速中的（-ing 构成现在分词）","example":"The accelerating train left the platform.","exampleCN":"加速中的列车驶离站台。"},{"word":"accelerated","structure":"accelerate + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"made faster, or done ahead of the usual time","meaningCN":"加速的；提前完成的（-ed 构成过去分词）","example":"The plan entered an accelerated phase.","exampleCN":"该计划进入加速阶段。"},{"word":"decelerate","structure":"de- (down, from) + celer (swift) + -ate; the opposite of accelerate","meaning":"to slow down","meaningCN":"减速（de- 表向下，与 accelerate 相反）","example":"The car decelerated before the bend.","exampleCN":"车子在弯道前减速。"},{"word":"deceleration","structure":"decelerate + -ion (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of slowing down","meaningCN":"减速过程（-ion 构成行为名词）","example":"The device logs sudden deceleration.","exampleCN":"这个装置记录骤然的减速。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"celerity","structure":"celer (swift) + -ity","meaning":"speed or swiftness","meaningCN":"迅速；敏捷"},{"word":"accelerando","structure":"accelerare (hasten) + -ando","meaning":"a musical direction to gradually speed up","meaningCN":"渐快（音乐术语，逐渐加快）"},{"word":"decelerate","structure":"de- (down) + celerare (hasten)","meaning":"to slow down","meaningCN":"减速（去掉速度）"}]}},{"word":"access","ipa_uk":"/ˈækses/","ipa_us":"/ˈækses/","definition_zh":"进入；通道；使用权；访问","definition_en":"the right or opportunity to enter, use, or reach something; also a way of entering","core_image":"一道门打开了，只有持卡的人能走进去","scene":"大楼门口，保安拿起工牌准备刷卡。 The guard swiped his badge and opened the door, allowing entry only to people with access.","sceneCN":"这里 access 是「进入权」（第 2 个义项：获准进入的权利）；句意：保安刷工牌开门，只允许有进入权的人进入。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"进入权；使用权；接近的机会"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"通道；入口"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"访问；存取（计算机数据）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"access to","zh":"进入……的权利；使用……的机会"},{"phrase":"gain access","zh":"获得进入权；得以进入"},{"phrase":"have access to","zh":"可以使用；能够接触到"},{"phrase":"Internet access","zh":"互联网接入"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it，动词）","form":"accesses"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"accessed"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"accessed"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"accessing"},{"label":"复数（名词）","form":"accesses"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"accessible","pos":"adj.","zh":"可到达的；可使用的；易懂的"},{"word":"accession","pos":"n.","zh":"加入；就职；增添"},{"word":"accessibility","pos":"n.","zh":"可及性；无障碍程度"},{"word":"accede","pos":"v.","zh":"同意；就任；加入"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A way of entering","titleCN":"通道：进入的路径","definition":"a way of entering a place or reaching something","definitionCN":"进入某地或到达某物的路径","example":"The only access to the beach is through this path.","exampleCN":"通往海滩的唯一通道就是这条小路。","why":"Latin accessus meant 'a coming to, an approach; a way of approach'. The word begins with a route that leads up to a place, not with the place itself.","whyCN":"拉丁语 accessus 意为“来到、接近；接近的方式”。这个词的起点是通向某地的一条路线，而不是地点本身。"},{"no":"02","title":"The right to enter or use","titleCN":"进入权：获准使用","definition":"the right or permission to enter a place or use something","definitionCN":"进入某地或使用某物的权利或许可","example":"Only staff have access to the records room.","exampleCN":"只有员工才能进入档案室。","why":"A door can be open physically and still closed socially. Access is the permission that turns a route into an allowed route, so it becomes a right.","whyCN":"一扇门可以在物理上开着，却在社会意义上关着。access 是把“路线”变成“获准路线”的许可，因此它成为一种权利。"},{"no":"03","title":"The act of approaching","titleCN":"接近：靠近的动作","definition":"the act of coming near or reaching a person or thing, often in formal use","definitionCN":"接近或到达某人某物的动作，常用于正式语境","example":"The reporters demanded access to the minister.","exampleCN":"记者们要求接近部长。","why":"The oldest Latin sense is simply 'a coming to'. Before it is a right or a doorway, access is the movement of getting near someone important.","whyCN":"最古老的拉丁义就是“来到”。在成为权利或门口之前，access 是靠近某个重要人物的动作。"},{"no":"04","title":"Computing: reach data","titleCN":"计算机：访问数据","definition":"to open, read, or change data stored in a computer system","definitionCN":"打开、读取或修改计算机系统中存储的数据","example":"The program accesses the database every minute.","exampleCN":"这个程序每分钟访问一次数据库。","why":"Digital data sits behind a virtual door. Access is the route and the permission together: the system must let the request come near the data.","whyCN":"数字数据位于一道虚拟门后。access 同时是路线和许可：系统必须让请求靠近数据。"},{"no":"05","title":"An attack of illness (archaic)","titleCN":"疾病发作（古义）","definition":"in older medical use, the sudden onset or attack of a fever or illness","definitionCN":"较古的医学用法：发烧或疾病的突然发作","example":"The old record describes a sudden access of fever.","exampleCN":"旧记录描述了一次突发的发热。","why":"An illness 'comes to' the body, so the same movement of approach was used for a fever attack. Modern medical English has dropped this sense.","whyCN":"疾病“来到”身体，因此同一种“接近”的动作被用来指发烧发作。现代医学英语已不再使用这个义项。"},{"no":"06","title":"An opportunity to use","titleCN":"使用机会：能够接触到","definition":"the opportunity or ability to use something or reach a person","definitionCN":"使用某物或接触某人的机会或能力","example":"Students need access to reliable information.","exampleCN":"学生需要获得可靠信息的机会。","why":"The route and the right combine into an opportunity. If a resource can be reached and you are allowed to reach it, you have access in the everyday sense.","whyCN":"路线与权利合并成一种机会。如果一种资源可以被到达，而你又获准到达，你在日常意义上就拥有 access。"},{"no":"07","title":"A road built to reach a place","titleCN":"为到达某地修建的道路","definition":"a road or track built to let vehicles reach a site, such as a field, plant, or hospital","definitionCN":"为让车辆到达场地（如田地、工厂或医院）而修建的道路","example":"A new access road was built to the plant.","exampleCN":"为通往工厂修了一条新路。","why":"The abstract way in becomes asphalt: the sense narrows from any route to the specific piece of road a site needs before anything can be delivered.","whyCN":"抽象的“进入之路”变成柏油路：这个义项从任何路线收窄到场地在运货之前必须有的那一段路。"},{"no":"08","title":"Family law: a parent's time with a child","titleCN":"家庭法：探视子女的权利","definition":"in family law, the right of a parent who does not live with a child to spend time with that child","definitionCN":"家庭法中不与子女同住的父母与子女相处的权利","example":"The court granted the father access to his children every weekend.","exampleCN":"法院准许父亲每周末探视子女。","why":"The right of entry is applied to a relationship: the parent is allowed into the child's life at set times, and the word keeps the sense of a door that opens on a schedule.","whyCN":"进入权被用到一段关系上：父母获准在规定时间进入孩子的生活，这个词仍带着“按时刻表打开的门”的意思。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Access first meant a fever attack in English, then a way of approach, then the right to enter. The Latin verb behind it is accedere 'to go toward'.","cn":"access 在英语中最早指“发烧发作”，再指“接近的方式”，最后指“进入权”。其背后的拉丁动词是 accedere“走向”。"},"items":[{"era":"EARLY 14C.","en":"First recorded early 14c. with the medical sense 'an attack of fever'.","cn":"最早记录于 14 世纪早期，医学义为“发烧发作”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"From Old French acces 'onslaught, attack; onset (of an illness)', from Latin accessus.","cn":"来自古法语 acces“猛攻、发作；（疾病） onset”，再往上为拉丁语 accessus。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin accessus 'a coming to, an approach; way of approach, entrance' is a noun from accedere 'to approach'.","cn":"拉丁语 accessus“来到、接近；接近的方式、入口”是 accedere“接近”的名词形式。"},{"era":"LATIN MORPHOLOGY","en":"Accedere = ad- (to) + cedere 'go, move, withdraw'. The source is PIE *ked- 'to go, yield'.","cn":"accedere = ad-“向”+ cedere“走、移动、退让”。其来源为原始印欧语 *ked-“走、让”。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The 'entrance' sense is recorded from c. 1600 directly from Latin, and the 'right to approach a person' from late 14c. Computing access is a 20c. extension.","cn":"“入口”义约 1600 年直接取自拉丁语；“接近某人的权利”义见于 14 世纪晚期。计算机“访问”义是 20 世纪的扩展。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group contains words that look or sound close; the second contains words for entry and permission.","cn":"第一组是看起来或听起来接近的词；第二组是表示进入与许可的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"excess","ipa":"/ɪkˈses/","tag":"opposite prefix","definition":"more than is needed. It differs by the prefix ex- 'out' instead of ac- 'to'.","definitionCN":"过量；超过所需。它的前缀是 ex-“向外”，而不是 ac-“向”。"},{"word":"assess","ipa":"/əˈses/","tag":"near sound","definition":"to judge the quality or value of something. It sounds like access but comes from a different Latin verb.","definitionCN":"评估；判断价值。它听起来像 access，但来自另一个拉丁动词。"},{"word":"accession","ipa":"/əkˈseʃn/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the act of joining, taking office, or adding something.","definitionCN":"加入；就职；增添。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"entry","ipa":"/ˈentri/","tag":"going in","definition":"the act of going into a place, or a doorway; close to access but less about permission.","definitionCN":"进入；入口，接近 access，但较少强调许可。"},{"word":"admission","ipa":"/ədˈmɪʃn/","tag":"permission","definition":"permission to enter a place or organisation; it stresses the gatekeeper's yes.","definitionCN":"准许进入；入场许可，强调守门人的“同意”。"},{"word":"approach","ipa":"/əˈprəʊtʃ/","tag":"coming near","definition":"the act of coming near; also a way of dealing with something.","definitionCN":"接近；方法。"},{"word":"entryway","ipa":"/ˈentriweɪ/","tag":"physical route","definition":"a passage or door used to enter a building; the physical side of access.","definitionCN":"入口通道；门厅，是 access 的物理一面。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts and relatives: ad- 'to' + cedere 'go', with accede, accessible, accession and the cede family.","cn":"真实构词与同族词：ad-“向”+ cedere“走”，以及 accede、accessible、accession 和 cede 词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"ad- 'to' + cedere 'go' = to go toward. Access is first a movement toward a place, then the route, then the right to use that route.","cn":"ad-“向”+ cedere“走”=走向。access 先是朝某地移动，再是路线，最后是使用这条路的权利。"},{"en":"Accede is the verb 'to go to' a proposal or an office; accession is the noun for taking office or joining.","cn":"accede 是“走向”某个提议或职位的动词；accession 是就职或加入的名词。"},{"en":"Accessible is the adjective: a place that can be reached or a text that can be understood.","cn":"accessible 是形容词：一个能到达的地方，或一篇能读懂的文本。"},{"en":"Have access to is the everyday pattern: the route is open and permission is given.","cn":"have access to 是日常搭配：路线开着，许可也给了。"},{"en":"The old fever sense survives in medical history: an illness 'comes to' the body.","cn":"旧的“发烧发作”义保留在医学史中：疾病“来到”身体。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a corridor with a locked door at the end: the corridor is access as a route, the key is access as a right.","cn":"想象一条走廊，尽头有一扇锁着的门：走廊是作为路线的 access，钥匙是作为权利的 access。"},{"en":"The same corridor can lead to a building, a person, a database, or a service.","cn":"同一条走廊可以通向建筑、人、数据库或服务。"},{"en":"Access is complete only when the path is open and the key is in your hand.","cn":"只有当路开着、钥匙在你手里，access 才完整。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The hotel has direct access to the beach.","cn":"这家酒店可以直接通往海滩。"},{"en":"You need a password to access your account.","cn":"你需要密码才能访问账户。"},{"en":"Many families still lack access to clean water.","cn":"许多家庭仍然无法获得干净的水。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿克塞斯”——阿克拿着门卡，一路走到门边刷开 → access 进入、访问","word":"access"},"root":"拉丁语 ad“向”+ cedere“走”，字面义“走向、接近”，核心是“能走进去、能接触到”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of access, all one movement toward a place: a route, a right, an approach, a digital door, an archaic fever, an opportunity, a service road, and a parent's court-ordered time.","cn":"access 的八个义项都是同一种“朝某地移动”：路线、权利、接近、数字之门、古义的疾病来袭、使用机会、专用道路，以及法院规定的探视时间。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a path leads to a door, and permission opens it.","cn":"核心意象：一条路通向一道门，许可把门打开。"},"chain":["GO TOWARD","APPROACH","WAY IN","PERMISSION","DIGITAL ENTRY","THE OPPORTUNITY"],"branches":[{"senses":"03","en":"APPROACH: the act of coming near, before any door is opened.","cn":"接近：在门打开之前，靠近的动作本身。"},{"senses":"01 · 07","en":"THE WAY IN: a route, and the road built so that a site can be reached at all.","cn":"进入之路：一条路线，以及为了让场地能被到达而专门修的路。"},{"senses":"02 · 08","en":"THE RIGHT: permission to enter a place, and the court-ordered time with a child.","cn":"权利：获准进入某地，以及由法院规定的探视时间。"},{"senses":"04","en":"THE MACHINE: data reached and opened by a user rather than a person.","cn":"机器：由使用者而非人走过去打开的存取通道。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"OLD AND EVERYDAY: an archaic fever coming on, and the plain chance to use something.","cn":"古义与日常：古时所说的疾病来袭，以及日常的“有机会用上”。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Access is a Latin noun; English adds -ible for accessible and -ion for accession, and keeps accede as the plain verb.","cn":"access 是拉丁名词；英语加 -ible 构成 accessible，加 -ion 构成 accession，并保留 accede 作为普通动词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on cedere 'go, yield': accede, concede, exceed, proceed and succeed all describe going or yielding in different directions.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 cedere“走、让”上：accede、concede、exceed、proceed、succeed 都描述不同方向的走或让。"},"items":[{"word":"accessible","structure":"access + -ible","meaning":"able to be reached, used, or understood","meaningCN":"可到达的；可使用的；易懂的（-ible 表示“能够被……”）","example":"The building is accessible to wheelchair users.","exampleCN":"这栋建筑可供轮椅使用者进入。"},{"word":"accession","structure":"access + -ion","meaning":"the act of joining or taking office; an addition","meaningCN":"加入；就职；增添（-ion 构成行为名词）","example":"The museum announced the accession of three new paintings.","exampleCN":"博物馆宣布新增三幅画作。"},{"word":"accessibility","structure":"accessible + -ity","meaning":"the quality of being easy to reach or use","meaningCN":"可及性；无障碍程度","example":"The city improved accessibility for disabled residents.","exampleCN":"这座城市改善了残障居民的无障碍条件。"},{"word":"accede","structure":"ad- (to) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to agree to a request or take office","meaningCN":"同意；就任（走向某个提议或职位）","example":"The government finally acceded to the demand.","exampleCN":"政府最终同意了这一要求。"},{"word":"accessed","structure":"access + -ed (past tense and past participle)","meaning":"reached or entered","meaningCN":"访问过的；进入过的（-ed 构成过去式与过去分词）","example":"The file was last accessed in March.","exampleCN":"这个文件最近一次被访问是在三月。"},{"word":"accessing","structure":"access + -ing (present participle and gerund)","meaning":"the act of reaching or entering","meaningCN":"访问（动名词）；正在访问（现在分词）","example":"Accessing the archive requires a password.","exampleCN":"访问档案需要密码。"},{"word":"inaccessible","structure":"in- (not) + accessible","meaning":"impossible to reach or enter","meaningCN":"不可达的；进不去的（in- 表否定）","example":"The village is inaccessible in winter.","exampleCN":"这个村子冬天无法进入。"},{"word":"accessibly","structure":"accessible + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a reachable or easy-to-understand way","meaningCN":"可及地；易懂地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The museum presents its collection accessibly.","exampleCN":"这家博物馆把藏品呈现得通俗易懂。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"concede","structure":"con- (with, together) + cedere (go, yield)","meaning":"to admit or give way","meaningCN":"承认；让步（一起让出）"},{"word":"exceed","structure":"ex- (out) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to go beyond a limit","meaningCN":"超过；越过（走出界限）"},{"word":"proceed","structure":"pro- (forward) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to go forward or continue","meaningCN":"前进；继续进行（向前走）"},{"word":"succeed","structure":"sub- (after, near) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to come after; to achieve a goal","meaningCN":"接替；成功（跟在后面走，因而“接续、达成”）"}]}},{"word":"accessible","ipa_uk":"/əkˈsesəbl/","ipa_us":"/əkˈsesəbl/","definition_zh":"可到达的；可获得的；易懂的；平易近人的","definition_en":"able to be reached, used, obtained, or understood","core_image":"坡道接到门口，门也为轮椅敞开","scene":"图书馆门口新修了一道坡道。 The wheelchair rolled up the new ramp and through the library door, which now made the building accessible to everyone.","sceneCN":"这里 accessible 是「无障碍的、可进入的」（第 5 个义项：对行动不便者也便于使用）；句意：轮椅沿新修的坡道滚进图书馆大门，这座建筑如今对所有人都无障碍。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"可到达的；可进入的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"可获得的；易懂的；平易近人的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"easily accessible","zh":"容易到达的；容易获取的"},{"phrase":"accessible to the public","zh":"向公众开放的"},{"phrase":"wheelchair accessible","zh":"轮椅可进入的；无障碍的"},{"phrase":"readily accessible","zh":"随手可得的；便于使用的"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more accessible"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most accessible"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"accessibility","pos":"n.","zh":"可及性；无障碍程度"},{"word":"inaccessible","pos":"adj.","zh":"无法到达的；难以理解的"},{"word":"accessibly","pos":"adv.","zh":"可到达地；易懂地"},{"word":"access","pos":"n./v.","zh":"进入权；通道；访问"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Able to be reached","titleCN":"可到达：路能走到","definition":"able to be reached or entered, especially without difficulty","definitionCN":"能够到达或进入，尤指不费力地","example":"The village is accessible only by boat.","exampleCN":"这个村庄只能坐船到达。","why":"Access is a route plus permission; -ible turns that into a possibility. If a place can be approached along a route, it is accessible.","whyCN":"access 是路线加许可；-ible 把它变成一种可能性。如果一个地方能沿着某条路线接近，它就是 accessible。"},{"no":"02","title":"Able to be obtained or used","titleCN":"可获得：拿得到、用得上","definition":"able to be obtained, used, or afforded","definitionCN":"能够获得、使用或负担得起","example":"Good childcare should be accessible to all families.","exampleCN":"优质托育服务应当对所有家庭都可获得。","why":"The route now leads to a resource rather than a place. If the resource can be reached and used, it is accessible, even when no physical door exists.","whyCN":"路线现在通向资源，而不是地点。如果资源能被到达并使用，它就是 accessible，即使没有实体的门。"},{"no":"03","title":"Easy to understand","titleCN":"易懂：理解上没有门槛","definition":"easy to understand or appreciate, especially for ordinary people","definitionCN":"容易理解或欣赏，尤指对普通人而言","example":"The book is accessible to readers without a science background.","exampleCN":"没有科学背景的读者也能读懂这本书。","why":"Understanding is also a path the mind walks. When the ideas are laid out so that a non-specialist can follow them, the text is accessible.","whyCN":"理解也是心智走过的一条路。当观点被安排得让非专业者也能跟上，这篇文本就是 accessible。"},{"no":"04","title":"Friendly and easy to approach","titleCN":"平易近人：人容易接近","definition":"friendly and easy to talk to, especially for someone in a position of authority","definitionCN":"友好、容易交谈，尤指处于权威位置的人","example":"The director was surprisingly accessible to junior staff.","exampleCN":"这位主管出人意料地平易近人，愿意接触基层员工。","why":"A person can also have a door. When the door is open and the route is short, the person is accessible in the social sense.","whyCN":"人也可以有一道门。当门开着、路很短，这个人就在社交意义上 accessible。"},{"no":"05","title":"Designed for disabled users","titleCN":"无障碍：对行动不便者友好","definition":"designed so that people with disabilities can enter and use it","definitionCN":"经过设计，使残障人士能够进入和使用","example":"The new station is fully wheelchair accessible.","exampleCN":"新车站完全可供轮椅进入。","why":"This sense makes the physical route explicit: ramps, lifts, and wide doors remove the barriers that made access impossible for some bodies.","whyCN":"这个义项把物理路线说得很明确：坡道、电梯和宽门消除了让某些身体无法进入的障碍。"},{"no":"06","title":"Computing: able to be opened","titleCN":"计算机：可访问的","definition":"in computing, able to be opened, read, or used by a system or user","definitionCN":"计算机中，可被系统或用户打开、读取或使用","example":"The files are accessible only from the office network.","exampleCN":"这些文件只能从办公室网络访问。","why":"Data needs a route and a permission just as a room does. When both are present, the file is accessible to the system.","whyCN":"数据和房间一样，需要一条路线和一份许可。两者齐备时，文件对系统就是 accessible。"},{"no":"07","title":"Affordable: within people's means","titleCN":"可负担：在人们能力之内","definition":"of housing, healthcare, or a service, cheap enough for ordinary people to obtain","definitionCN":"指住房、医疗或服务价格低到普通人可以负担","example":"The scheme aims to make housing accessible to low-income families.","exampleCN":"该计划旨在让低收入家庭也能负担住房。","why":"The barrier is now a price rather than a step: what cannot be afforded is out of reach, so lowering the cost lowers the same threshold.","whyCN":"这时的门槛是价格而不是台阶：付不起的东西就在手够不到的地方，因此降低价格就是降低同一道门槛。"},{"no":"08","title":"Records opened to the public","titleCN":"档案公开：向公众开放","definition":"of documents or information, no longer restricted and available for anyone to read","definitionCN":"指文件或信息不再受限，任何人都可以查阅","example":"The archive made the files accessible after thirty years.","exampleCN":"三十年后，档案馆让这批文件对外开放。","why":"The door that opens is a legal one: a file moves from restricted to available, and nothing physical changes except the rule that kept it shut.","whyCN":"打开的是法律意义上的门：文件从受限变为可用，除了那道关着它的规定，什么都不用改动。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Accessible came from French and Late Latin as the adjective of access. Its history is short but follows the same 'go toward' root.","cn":"accessible 作为 access 的形容词，从法语和晚期拉丁语进入英语。它的历史不长，但同样沿着“走向”这个词根。"},"items":[{"era":"C. 1400","en":"First recorded c. 1400 meaning 'affording access, capable of being approached or reached'.","cn":"约 1400 年最早记录，意为“提供进入途径的、能够被接近或到达的”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH AND LATE LATIN","en":"From Old French accessible and Late Latin accessibilis, an adjective built on accessus.","cn":"来自古法语 accessible 和晚期拉丁语 accessibilis，后者是基于 accessus 构成的形容词。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"Accessus is the noun from accedere 'to approach, go to, come near, enter upon' = ad- 'to' + cedere 'go'.","cn":"accessus 是 accedere“接近、走向、靠近、进入”的名词；accedere = ad-“向”+ cedere“走”。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Cedere goes back to PIE *ked- 'to go, yield', the same root behind accede and succeed.","cn":"cedere 可追溯到原始印欧语 *ked-“走、让”，accede 和 succeed 也出自这个词根。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'easy to reach' is recorded from the 1640s, and the sense 'easy to understand' (of art or writing) from 1961. The disability sense develops in the 20c.","cn":"“容易到达”义记录于 17 世纪 40 年代；“（艺术或文字）易懂”义记录于 1961 年；残障无障碍义在 20 世纪发展起来。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The spelling group is easy to mistake for accessible; the meaning group contains words for reachable and available.","cn":"拼写组很容易与 accessible 混淆；近义组收录表示“可到达、可获得”的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"assessable","ipa":"/əˈsesəbl/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"able to be evaluated or taxed. It looks close but comes from assess, not access.","definitionCN":"可评估的；可征税的。它看起来接近，但来自 assess，而不是 access。"},{"word":"accessibly","ipa":"/əkˈsesəbli/","tag":"derived adverb","definition":"the adverb from accessible, meaning in an easy-to-reach or easy-to-understand way.","definitionCN":"accessible 派生的副词，表示以易于到达或易于理解的方式。"},{"word":"accessary","ipa":"/əkˈsesəri/","tag":"archaic spelling","definition":"an old spelling of accessory, a person who helps in a crime; unrelated to access.","definitionCN":"accessory 的旧拼法，指协助犯罪者，与 access 无关。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"reachable","ipa":"/ˈriːtʃəbl/","tag":"physical","definition":"able to be reached; the plainest synonym for the physical sense of accessible.","definitionCN":"可到达的，是 accessible 物理义最平实的同义词。"},{"word":"available","ipa":"/əˈveɪləbl/","tag":"obtainable","definition":"able to be obtained or used; close to accessible in the resource sense.","definitionCN":"可获得的；可用的，在资源义上接近 accessible。"},{"word":"approachable","ipa":"/əˈprəʊtʃəbl/","tag":"person","definition":"friendly and easy to talk to; the personal sense of accessible.","definitionCN":"平易近人的；容易交谈的，是 accessible 的人物义。"},{"word":"understandable","ipa":"/ˌʌndəˈstændəbl/","tag":"comprehensible","definition":"able to be understood; the plainest synonym for the 'easy to understand' sense.","definitionCN":"可理解的；易懂的，是“易懂”义最平实的同义词。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real morphology: access + -ible 'able to be', with inaccessible as the negative and accessibility as the noun.","cn":"真实构词：access + -ible“能够被……”，否定形式是 inaccessible，名词是 accessibility。"},"normal":[{"en":"access + -ible = able to be accessed. The suffix simply turns a route and a right into a possibility.","cn":"access + -ible = 能够被接近。后缀只是把路线和权利变成一种可能性。"},{"en":"Inaccessible is the negated form: the door is locked, the ramp is missing, or the text is too hard.","cn":"inaccessible 是否定形式：门锁着、坡道缺失，或文本太难。"},{"en":"Wheelchair accessible is a fixed label on buildings and transport.","cn":"wheelchair accessible 是建筑和交通工具上的固定标识。"},{"en":"Accessible to the public is the standard phrase for open institutions.","cn":"“accessible to the public”是开放机构的固定说法。"},{"en":"The same word moves from places to resources to texts to people: all are 'reachable'.","cn":"同一个词从地点移到资源、文本和人：它们都是“够得着的”。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a ramp joining a pavement to a door: accessible is the moment the two levels meet.","cn":"想象一条坡道把人行道接到门口：accessible 就是两个高度接上的那一刻。"},{"en":"The ramp can be physical (a building), economic (a price), intellectual (a text), or social (a person).","cn":"这条坡道可以是物理的（建筑）、经济的（价格）、智力的（文本）或社交的（人）。"},{"en":"Something accessible asks for no extra climb; something inaccessible keeps a step you cannot take.","cn":"accessible 的东西不要求额外攀爬；inaccessible 的东西保留着一级你跨不过去的台阶。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The museum is accessible by bus and train.","cn":"这座博物馆可以乘公交和火车到达。"},{"en":"The service is accessible to low-income families.","cn":"这项服务对低收入家庭也可获得。"},{"en":"Her writing is clear and accessible.","cn":"她的写作清晰易懂。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿克塞斯波”——阿克塞斯坡上修了坡道，轮椅也能进 → accessible 可进入的、无障碍的","word":"accessible"},"root":"access + -ible“能够被……”，核心是“路线通、门槛低，能够被到达或使用”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of accessible, all one low threshold: a place reached, a resource obtained, a text understood, a person approached, a building without steps, a file opened, a price people can pay, and records released.","cn":"accessible 的八个义项都是同一个“低门槛”：地方能到达、资源能获得、文本能读懂、人能接近、建筑无障碍、文件能打开、价格能负担、档案能公开。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a ramp reaches the door and the door opens without a step.","cn":"核心意象：坡道接到门口，门打开时没有台阶。"},"chain":["ACCESS","ABLE TO BE REACHED","ABLE TO BE OBTAINED","ABLE TO BE UNDERSTOOD","EASY TO APPROACH","OPEN TO EVERYONE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 05","en":"REACHED: a place one can walk to, and a building with no step in the way.","cn":"到得了：能走到的地点，以及没有台阶拦着的建筑。"},{"senses":"02 · 07","en":"OBTAINED: a resource one can get hold of, and a price ordinary people can pay.","cn":"拿得到：能够取得的资源，以及普通人付得起的价格。"},{"senses":"03","en":"UNDERSTOOD: a text that asks nothing extra of the reader.","cn":"读得懂：不向读者额外索取什么的文本。"},{"senses":"04","en":"APPROACHED: a person who is easy to talk to.","cn":"接近得了：一个好说话、容易接近的人。"},{"senses":"06 · 08","en":"OPENED: a file that can be read by a program, and records released from restriction.","cn":"被打开：程序读得到的文件，以及解除限制后公开的档案。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Accessible is access + -ible. The negative is inaccessible, the noun is accessibility, and the adverb is accessibly.","cn":"accessible 是 access + -ible。否定形式是 inaccessible，名词是 accessibility，副词是 accessibly。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on cedere 'go': access, accession, accede, concede and exceed all describe going toward, beyond, or along.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 cedere“走”上：access、accession、accede、concede、exceed 都描述朝向、越过或沿着走。"},"items":[{"word":"accessibility","structure":"accessible + -ity","meaning":"the quality of being easy to reach or use","meaningCN":"可及性；无障碍程度（-ity 构成性质名词）","example":"Accessibility is now part of the building code.","exampleCN":"无障碍要求现在已写入建筑规范。"},{"word":"inaccessible","structure":"in- (not) + accessible","meaning":"not able to be reached or understood","meaningCN":"无法到达的；难以理解的（in- 表示否定）","example":"The summit is inaccessible in winter.","exampleCN":"冬季无法到达山顶。"},{"word":"accessibly","structure":"accessible + -ly","meaning":"in an easy-to-reach or easy-to-understand way","meaningCN":"可到达地；易懂地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The data is presented accessibly.","exampleCN":"数据以易懂的方式呈现。"},{"word":"access","structure":"access (noun and verb)","meaning":"the right or act of entering or using","meaningCN":"进入权；通道；访问（名词与动词）","example":"They gained access to the site.","exampleCN":"他们获得了进入该场地的许可。"},{"word":"accessed","structure":"access + -ed (past tense and past participle)","meaning":"reached or entered","meaningCN":"访问过的；进入过的（-ed 构成过去式与过去分词）","example":"The archive was accessed from three terminals.","exampleCN":"这个档案从三台终端被访问过。"},{"word":"accessing","structure":"access + -ing (present participle and gerund)","meaning":"the act of reaching or entering","meaningCN":"访问（动名词）；正在访问（现在分词）","example":"Accessing the site is free for students.","exampleCN":"学生访问这个网站是免费的。"},{"word":"inaccessibility","structure":"in- (not) + accessibility","meaning":"the state of being impossible to reach","meaningCN":"不可达性；难以接近（in- 表否定）","example":"The inaccessibility of the site delayed the dig.","exampleCN":"遗址难以抵达，考古发掘被推迟。"},{"word":"unaccessible","structure":"un- (not) + accessible (variant of inaccessible)","meaning":"not accessible","meaningCN":"不可及的（un- 表否定，与 inaccessible 同义的变体）","example":"The upper shelf is unaccessible without a ladder.","exampleCN":"没有梯子就够不到上层架子。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"accession","structure":"access + -ion","meaning":"joining or taking office; an addition","meaningCN":"加入；就职；增添"},{"word":"accede","structure":"ad- + cedere (go)","meaning":"to agree or take office","meaningCN":"同意；就任"},{"word":"concede","structure":"con- + cedere (go, yield)","meaning":"to admit or give way","meaningCN":"承认；让步"},{"word":"cede","structure":"cedere (go, yield)","meaning":"to give up land or power","meaningCN":"割让；放弃（土地或权力）"}]}},{"word":"accident","ipa_uk":"/ˈæksɪdənt/","ipa_us":"/ˈæksɪdənt/","definition_zh":"事故；意外；偶然","definition_en":"an unexpected event, especially one that causes damage or injury","core_image":"一件东西从上方突然掉落在你身上","scene":"十字路口散落着碎玻璃，两辆车停在路中央。 Two cars crashed at the crossing, glass lay on the road, and a passerby called the emergency line about the accident.","sceneCN":"这里 accident 是「事故」（第 1 个义项：造成伤害的意外事件）；句意：两辆车在十字路口相撞，玻璃散在路面上，路人拨打急救电话报告这起事故。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"事故；意外事件（尤指造成伤害或损失）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"偶然；意外（不可数，表示机缘）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"car accident","zh":"车祸"},{"phrase":"by accident","zh":"偶然地；无意中"},{"phrase":"traffic accident","zh":"交通事故"},{"phrase":"have an accident","zh":"出事故"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"accidents"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"accidental","pos":"adj.","zh":"意外的；偶然的"},{"word":"accidentally","pos":"adv.","zh":"意外地；偶然地"},{"word":"accidence","pos":"n.","zh":"词形变化（语法术语，罕用）"},{"word":"accident-prone","pos":"adj.","zh":"易出事故的；容易闯祸的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"An unintended event that causes harm","titleCN":"事故：非本意且造成伤害","definition":"an unexpected event that happens by chance and causes damage or injury","definitionCN":"偶然发生并造成损坏或伤害的意外事件","example":"Three people were hurt in the car accident.","exampleCN":"三人在车祸中受伤。","why":"Latin accidere meant 'to fall upon'. The word starts with something falling onto a person without warning, which is why an accident is first an event that lands on you.","whyCN":"拉丁语 accidere 意为“落在……之上”。这个词的起点，是某物毫无预警地落到人身上，因此 accident 首先是一种“落到你头上”的事件。"},{"no":"02","title":"An unexpected event","titleCN":"意外事件：没有预料到的事","definition":"an event that happens unexpectedly and is not planned","definitionCN":"出乎意料且非计划中发生的事件","example":"The discovery was a happy accident.","exampleCN":"这项发现是一次幸运的意外。","why":"The 'falling upon' need not hurt. Anything that arrives without being planned is an accident, so the word can cover a lucky meeting as well as a crash.","whyCN":"“落在身上”不一定造成伤害。任何未经计划而到来的事都是 accident，所以这个词既能指车祸，也能指幸运的相遇。"},{"no":"03","title":"By accident: unintentionally","titleCN":"无意中：不是故意的","definition":"in the phrase by accident, without intending to or by chance","definitionCN":"用于 by accident，表示并非有意或出于偶然","example":"I deleted the file by accident.","exampleCN":"我不小心删掉了那个文件。","why":"The phrase marks the absence of intention. What happened fell out of events rather than out of a plan, so no one meant it.","whyCN":"这个短语标记“没有意图”。发生的事是从事件中掉出来的，而不是从计划中产生的，所以没有人是故意的。"},{"no":"04","title":"Mere chance","titleCN":"偶然性：机缘本身","definition":"the force of chance, considered as something that cannot be planned","definitionCN":"偶然的力量，被视为无法计划之物","example":"They met by pure accident, not by design.","exampleCN":"他们纯属偶然相遇，并非刻意安排。","why":"Here accident is not one event but the principle behind events. Whatever is not caused by intention belongs to accident, the opposite of design.","whyCN":"这里的 accident 不是某一件事，而是事件背后的原则。凡不是由意图造成的，都属于偶然，与“设计”相对。"},{"no":"05","title":"An accident of birth","titleCN":"出身的偶然：无法选择的条件","definition":"in the phrase an accident of birth or nature, a condition that depends on chance rather than choice","definitionCN":"用于“an accident of birth/nature”，指取决于偶然而非选择的条件","example":"Her citizenship was an accident of birth.","exampleCN":"她的国籍是出生地带来的偶然结果。","why":"No one chooses where to be born. The word treats that fact as something that fell upon the person, not something they earned or decided.","whyCN":"没有人选择自己出生在哪里。这个词把这一事实当作“落在个人身上”的东西，而不是他挣来或决定的东西。"},{"no":"06","title":"An accident waiting to happen","titleCN":"迟早会出的事：明显隐患","definition":"in the phrase an accident waiting to happen, a situation that is certain to cause harm sooner or later","definitionCN":"用于“an accident waiting to happen”，指迟早必然造成伤害的状况","example":"That loose staircase is an accident waiting to happen.","exampleCN":"那段松动的楼梯迟早会出事。","why":"The phrase turns chance into near-certainty: the falling event has not happened yet, but the conditions are already in place, so the accident is only waiting for its moment.","whyCN":"这个短语把偶然变成近乎必然：坠落事件还没发生，但条件已经齐备，所以事故只是在等它的时机。"},{"no":"07","title":"Hospital: accident and emergency care","titleCN":"医院：急诊科","definition":"the part of a hospital that treats people who arrive suddenly with injuries or urgent illness","definitionCN":"医院中救治突然受伤或急病者的部门","example":"The ambulance took him to accident and emergency.","exampleCN":"救护车把他送到急诊科。","why":"The word names the cause, not the treatment: the department is defined by the unplanned events that arrive there, day and night.","whyCN":"这个词指的是原因，不是治疗：这个科室是按那些不分昼夜突然到来的事件来定义的。"},{"no":"08","title":"Philosophy: a property that is not essential","titleCN":"哲学：非本质的属性","definition":"in logic and philosophy, a feature of a thing that may change without the thing ceasing to be what it is","definitionCN":"在逻辑与哲学中指事物可变化而不失其本性的属性","example":"In Aristotle's account, being tall is an accident of the substance.","exampleCN":"在亚里士多德的论述里，高矮是实体的偶性。","why":"An accident is what merely happens to a thing: the everyday word for an unplanned event becomes the name for any quality that could be otherwise.","whyCN":"偶性就是“碰巧落到某物上”的东西：日常表示未计划事件的词，成了任何“本可以不是这样”的性质的名字。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Accident comes from Latin accidere 'to fall upon'. The image is not a mistake but something landing on a person from outside their plan.","cn":"accident 来自拉丁语 accidere“落在……之上”。它的意象不是“犯错”，而是某物从计划之外落到一个人身上。"},"items":[{"era":"LATE 14C.","en":"First recorded late 14c. meaning 'an occurrence, incident, event; what comes by chance'.","cn":"最早记录于 14 世纪晚期，意为“发生之事、事件；偶然到来之事”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"From Old French accident (12c.), from Latin accidentem (nominative accidens) 'an occurrence; chance; misfortune'.","cn":"来自古法语 accident（12 世纪），再往上为拉丁语 accidentem（主格 accidens）“发生之事；偶然；不幸”。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"Accidens is the present participle of accidere 'happen, fall out, fall upon' = ad- 'to' + cadere 'to fall'.","cn":"accidens 是 accidere“发生、落出、落在……上”的现在分词；accidere = ad-“向”+ cadere“落下”。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Cadere goes back to PIE *kad- 'to fall', the same root behind incident, occasion, cadence, cascade, cadaver and chance.","cn":"cadere 可追溯到原始印欧语 *kad-“落下”，incident、occasion、cadence、cascade、cadaver、chance 都出自这个词根。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The sense drifted from 'any occurrence' toward 'an unfortunate event'. Modern English keeps both: a happy accident and a serious accident.","cn":"词义从“任何发生之事”漂向“不幸事件”。现代英语两者都保留：a happy accident（幸运的意外）和 a serious accident（严重事故）。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group shows the easily confused -cident family; the second shows words for mishaps and chance events.","cn":"第一组展示容易混淆的 -cident 词族；第二组展示表示“事故”和“偶然事件”的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"incident","ipa":"/ˈɪnsɪdənt/","tag":"prefix change","definition":"an event, often a minor or unpleasant one. It shares the Latin root but begins with in- rather than ac-.","definitionCN":"事件，常指较小或不愉快的事件。它共享拉丁词根，但以 in- 开头而不是 ac-。"},{"word":"accidence","ipa":"/ˈæksɪdəns/","tag":"grammar term","definition":"the part of grammar dealing with word endings and inflection; a rare technical word.","definitionCN":"词形变化（语法术语，罕用），指研究词尾与屈折变化的部分。"},{"word":"accidental","ipa":"/ˌæksɪˈdentl/","tag":"derived adjective","definition":"happening by chance; the adjective from accident.","definitionCN":"意外的；偶然的，是 accident 的形容词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"mishap","ipa":"/ˈmɪshæp/","tag":"minor accident","definition":"a small accident or unlucky event, usually without serious damage.","definitionCN":"小事故；不幸的小意外，通常没有严重损失。"},{"word":"crash","ipa":"/kræʃ/","tag":"vehicle accident","definition":"a violent collision involving a vehicle; a specific type of accident.","definitionCN":"撞车；交通工具的猛烈碰撞，是 accident 的具体类型。"},{"word":"misfortune","ipa":"/ˌmɪsˈfɔːtʃuːn/","tag":"bad luck","definition":"bad luck or an unlucky event; broader and less physical than accident.","definitionCN":"不幸；厄运，比 accident 更宽泛，也不那么强调物理伤害。"},{"word":"chance","ipa":"/tʃɑːns/","tag":"fortuity","definition":"the possibility or occurrence of something without plan; the abstract side of accident.","definitionCN":"偶然；机缘，是 accident 的抽象一面。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts and relatives: ad- 'to' + cadere 'fall', with incident, occasion, cadence and chance.","cn":"真实构词与同族词：ad-“向”+ cadere“落下”，以及 incident、occasion、cadence、chance。"},"normal":[{"en":"ad- 'to' + cadere 'fall' = to fall upon. An accident is something that lands on you from outside your plan.","cn":"ad-“向”+ cadere“落下”=落到……上。accident 就是从计划之外落到你身上的事。"},{"en":"Incident, occasion, cadence, cascade and chance all come from the same 'fall' root.","cn":"incident、occasion、cadence、cascade、chance 都出自同一个“落下”词根。"},{"en":"By accident is the fixed phrase for 'not on purpose'.","cn":"by accident 是表示“不是故意”的固定短语。"},{"en":"Accident-prone describes a person who seems to attract accidents.","cn":"accident-prone 描述似乎总招来事故的人。"},{"en":"An accident of birth treats where you were born as something that fell on you rather than something you chose.","cn":"“an accident of birth”把出生地当作“落到你身上”的东西，而不是你选择的东西。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a roof tile falling just as someone walks past: the tile was not aimed, but it lands on the person. That landing is the accident.","cn":"想象一片屋瓦在某人走过时正好落下：瓦片并没有瞄准谁，却落在人身上。这次“落下”就是 accident。"},{"en":"The falling thing can be a car, a chance meeting, a discovery, or a fact of birth.","cn":"落下的东西可以是一辆车、一次偶遇、一项发现，或一个出生事实。"},{"en":"The word does not blame a planner; it points to what arrived without a plan.","cn":"这个词不指向谋划者，而指向“没有计划却到来了”的东西。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The accident happened at the corner of the street.","cn":"事故发生在街道拐角处。"},{"en":"I found the old letter by accident.","cn":"我偶然找到了那封旧信。"},{"en":"Losing his passport was an unfortunate accident.","cn":"丢失护照是一次不幸的意外。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“阿克西登特”——阿克西在路口被突然落下的东西砸到 → accident 事故、意外","word":"accident"},"root":"拉丁语 ad“向”+ cadere“落下”，字面义“落到身上”，核心是“计划之外突然降临之事”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of accident, all one thing falling unplanned: a harmful event, an unexpected occurrence, the phrase for 'not on purpose', chance itself, an accident of birth, a danger waiting for its moment, the hospital unit, and a property that is not essential.","cn":"accident 的八个义项都是同一件“未经计划而落下”的事：造成伤害的事件、意外发生之事、“不是故意”的短语、偶然本身、出身的偶然、只等时机的隐患、医院急诊科，以及非本质的属性。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: something falls on a person from outside their plan.","cn":"核心意象：某物从计划之外落到一个人身上。"},"chain":["FALL","FALL UPON","HAPPEN","UNEXPECTED","MISFORTUNE","WHAT IS NOT ESSENTIAL"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 07","en":"HARM: an unintended injury, and the hospital unit that receives it.","cn":"伤害：非本意的受伤，以及接收它的医院部门。"},{"senses":"02 · 04","en":"WHAT HAPPENS: an unexpected event, and chance itself with no event at all.","cn":"发生之事：没有预料到的事件，以及根本没有事件的“偶然”本身。"},{"senses":"03 · 06","en":"NOT ON PURPOSE: the phrase for doing something unintentionally, and a danger only waiting for its moment.","cn":"并非故意：表示无意而为的短语，以及只等时机到来的隐患。"},{"senses":"05","en":"CIRCUMSTANCE: the conditions one is born into and cannot choose.","cn":"处境：一个人出生时就被放入、无法选择的条件。"},{"senses":"08","en":"THE PHILOSOPHERS' WORD: a quality that could be otherwise without changing what the thing is.","cn":"哲学家的用词：一种可以不同、却不改变事物本性的性质。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Accident forms accidental and accidentally, and the rare grammar noun accidence. Accident-prone is a compound adjective.","cn":"accident 构成 accidental 和 accidentally，以及罕用的语法名词 accidence。accident-prone 是复合形容词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is built on cadere 'to fall': incident, occasion, cadence, cascade and chance all describe falling or happening.","cn":"这一拉丁词族建立在 cadere“落下”上：incident、occasion、cadence、cascade、chance 都描述落下或发生。"},"items":[{"word":"accidental","structure":"accident + -al","meaning":"happening by chance, not planned","meaningCN":"意外的；偶然的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"The damage was accidental, not deliberate.","exampleCN":"损坏是意外造成的，不是故意的。"},{"word":"accidentally","structure":"accidental + -ly","meaning":"by chance; unintentionally","meaningCN":"意外地；偶然地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"She accidentally deleted the message.","exampleCN":"她不小心删掉了那条消息。"},{"word":"accidence","structure":"accident + -ence (grammatical form)","meaning":"the grammar of word endings and inflection","meaningCN":"词形变化（语法术语，-ence 构成名词）","example":"The chapter explains English accidence.","exampleCN":"这一章讲解英语的词形变化。"},{"word":"accident-prone","structure":"accident + prone","meaning":"likely to have accidents","meaningCN":"易出事故的；容易闯祸的","example":"He is accident-prone on wet roads.","exampleCN":"他在湿滑路面上容易出事故。"},{"word":"accidentalness","structure":"accidental + -ness (quality)","meaning":"the quality of happening by chance","meaningCN":"偶然性（-ness 构成抽象名词）","example":"The accidentalness of the meeting changed both lives.","exampleCN":"那次相遇的偶然性改变了两个人的人生。"},{"word":"accidented","structure":"accident + -ed (adjective; geology)","meaning":"having an uneven surface; irregular in relief","meaningCN":"地形起伏不平的（-ed 构成形容词，地质学用语）","example":"The accidented relief makes mapping difficult.","exampleCN":"起伏不平的地形使绘图变得困难。"},{"word":"incident","structure":"in- (on) + cadere (fall) + -ent (same Latin root as accident)","meaning":"a single event, often an unpleasant one","meaningCN":"事件；事变（与 accident 同出 cadere“落下”）","example":"The incident was reported at once.","exampleCN":"这一事件立刻被上报了。"},{"word":"occasion","structure":"ob- (toward) + casus (fall) + -ion (same Latin root as accident)","meaning":"a particular time or event","meaningCN":"场合；时机（同出“落下”词根）","example":"The ceremony marked a solemn occasion.","exampleCN":"这场典礼标志着一个庄重的场合。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"incident","structure":"in- (on) + cadere (fall) + -ent","meaning":"an event that falls upon a situation","meaningCN":"事件；事变（落在情境之上）"},{"word":"occasion","structure":"ob- (toward) + cadere (fall)","meaning":"a particular time or event","meaningCN":"场合；时机（落到眼前的时间点）"},{"word":"cadence","structure":"cadere (fall)","meaning":"rhythm; the fall of the voice","meaningCN":"节奏；语调的降落"},{"word":"cascade","structure":"cadere (fall)","meaning":"a small waterfall; a chain of falling events","meaningCN":"小瀑布；接连落下的事件链"},{"word":"chance","structure":"cadere (fall) via Old French cheance","meaning":"the way things fall out without plan","meaningCN":"偶然；机会（事情未经计划地“落”出来）"}]}}]);
